local E = ns.DB.entries
E["npc:abercrombie"] = {t="npc",n="Abercrombie",z="duskwood",s="Abercrombie appears to be a feeble, eccentric hermit dwelling in a dilapidated shack in western Duskwood near Raven Hill Cemetery. Claiming to be a harmless recluse plagued by the horrors of the woods, he readily enlists sympathetic travelers to gather peculiar reagents and supplies on his behalf.",h="Abercrombie appears to be a feeble, eccentric hermit dwelling in a dilapidated shack in western Duskwood near...",sec={{t="The Recluse of Raven Hill",b="Tucked away in the rotting shadows near Raven Hill Cemetery, Abercrombie cuts a pathetic figure. He presents himself as an old man merely trying to survive the terrors of Duskwood, asking travelers to run modest errands into Darkshire for supplies, herbs, and thread. To those unfamiliar with the history of the region, he seems like just another unfortunate soul left behind as the province fell into decay.",sp=0},{t="The Embalmer's Madness",b="Before grief consumed his mind, Abercrombie was a respected, kindly alchemist living in Raven Hill. When his beloved wife, Eliza, died, sorrow broke his sanity. Turning to forbidden necromantic arts, he cut out his own heart and placed it within Eliza's dead breast to bring her back. The ritual succeeded only in creating a monster: Eliza returned cursed with an insatiable hunger for living flesh, forcing the mad alchemist to keep her buried in the cemetery.",sp=2},{t="A Monstrous Deception",b="Known in dark folklore simply as 'The Embalmer,' Abercrombie nurses a deep, psychotic grudge against the township of Darkshire and its leaders. The seemingly innocuous tasks he assigns to helpful adventurers—fetching ghoul ribs, specialty thread, and caustic brews—are actually the final components required to assemble Stitches, a colossal, flesh-stitched abomination engineered to slaughter the Night Watch and burn the town.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Abercrombie?",a="Abercrombie is a hermit dwelling near Raven Hill Cemetery in Duskwood. Once a skilled alchemist, he lost his mind following the death of his wife and is secretly the necromantic figure known as the Embalmer.",al={"who is the hermit","abercrombie lore","who is abercrombie"},sp=2},{q="Why does Abercrombie want supplies from Darkshire?",a="While Abercrombie claims he needs domestic supplies and thread to survive in the wilderness, he is actually tricking adventurers into gathering the necessary parts to assemble the monstrous abomination Stitches.",al={"why does abercrombie need thread","abercrombie supplies","what is abercrombie building"},sp=1},{q="Who was Eliza?",a="Eliza was Abercrombie's wife. After she died, Abercrombie attempted to resurrect her using dark magic, transplanting his own heart into her corpse. She returned as a ravenous undead monster that he had to keep buried in Raven Hill Cemetery.",al={"eliza abercrombie","abercrombie wife","bride of the embalmer"},sp=1},{q="What happens when you deliver the Note to the Mayor?",a="The note reveals Abercrombie's true identity as the Embalmer and his vengeful hatred for Darkshire. Delivering the letter triggers the march of Stitches down the road to assault the town.",al={"note to the mayor","what does the note say","abercrombie letter"},sp=2},{q="Why does Abercrombie hate Darkshire?",a="Driven utterly mad by grief and dark magic, Abercrombie blames the town and its leadership for the tragic events of Duskwood and seeks their total destruction through his monstrous creation.",al={"why does abercrombie attack darkshire","embalmer motive","abercrombie revenge"},sp=1},{q="Is Abercrombie allied with the Scourge?",a="No. Abercrombie is an independent rogue alchemist and necromancer practicing forbidden arts born of his own grief-fueled madness, unrelated to the Lich King's armies.",al={"is abercrombie scourge","who does abercrombie work for"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes who naively lend a helping hand to the miserable hermit unknowingly provide the materials needed to orchestrate an assault on Darkshire.",["class:Paladin"]="Abercrombie represents the sinister corruption of necromancy festering under the guise of an ordinary, harmless townsman in need of charity.",["class:Warlock"]="Abercrombie's sacrifice of his own heart to reanimate a corpse demonstrates the extreme, self-destructive lengths mortals will go to wield dark magic."},kw={"abercrombie","abomination","darkshire","duskwood","eliza","ghoulish effigy","raven hill","the hermit"},rel={"subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:165","quest:253","quest:160","topic:night-watch"},src={"Abercrombie"}}
E["npc:althea-ebonlocke"] = {t="npc",n="Althea Ebonlocke",z="duskwood",s="Commander Althea Ebonlocke leads the Night Watch, the beleaguered town guard protecting Darkshire from the terrors of Duskwood. A relative of Mayor Ello Ebonlocke, she shoulders the defense of an isolated region abandoned by Stormwind's regular military. She organizes patrols, tasks adventurers with culling local horrors, and coordinates the town's survival against constant monstrous threats.",h="Commander Althea Ebonlocke leads the Night Watch, the beleaguered town guard protecting Darkshire from the...",sec={{t="Commander of the Watch",b="While her father, Mayor Ello Ebonlocke, handles civil governance within the town hall, Commander Althea directs Darkshire's thin line of physical defense. When Stormwind failed to deploy royal troops to guard Duskwood against creeping horrors, the citizenry formed the Night Watch. Under Althea's steady, unyielding command, these volunteers patrol the fog-shrouded roads, keeping skeletal undead, ferocious wolves, and spiders from overrunning the town perimeter.",sp=0},{t="A Town on the Brink",b="Althea is pragmatic and understands the limits of her militia. Outnumbered and continually bleeding recruits, she freely enlists passing mercenaries and travelers to thin the threats at Darkshire's doorstep. She directs campaigns against the ghouls and skeletons at the tranquil and sorrowful graveyards of the forest, while remaining vigilant against darker rumors stirring deep in the woods.",sp=0},{t="Tragedies of the Wood",b="Beyond common forest vermin, Althea coordinates the investigation and destruction of Duskwood's greatest blights. She assists in unraveling the dark fate of Stalvan Mistmantle and seeks answers to the restless wandering of Mor'Ladim, the fallen knight Morgan Ladimore. When Abercrombie unleashes the monstrous abomination Stitches down the main road, it is Althea who rallies the Watch for Darkshire's desperate last stand.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Althea Ebonlocke?",a="Commander Althea Ebonlocke is the leader of the Night Watch, the town militia of Darkshire in Duskwood. She is responsible for organizing the defense of the region against the undead and beasts that lurk in the shadows.",al={"who is althea","commander ebonlocke","who is the night watch commander"}},{q="What is the Night Watch?",a="The Night Watch is a volunteer militia raised by the citizens of Darkshire. Because Stormwind has provided virtually no military support to Duskwood, the local townspeople banded together under Althea's leadership to patrol the roads and fight back the horrors of the woods.",al={"what is night watch","who are the night watch","darkshire militia"}},{q="How is Althea related to Mayor Ello Ebonlocke?",a="Althea is a relative of Lord Ello Ebonlocke, the mayor of Darkshire. While her father governs town affairs from the town hall, Althea commands the militia in the field.",al={"ello ebonlocke relative","is althea ello daughter","althea family"}},{q="Why is Stormwind not helping Althea defend Darkshire?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and Stormwind's resources strained, the House of Nobles has largely neglected the kingdom's outer territories. Darkshire receives virtually no soldiers or relief, forcing Althea to depend on local volunteers and freelance adventurers.",al={"why no stormwind guards","stormwind duskwood support","where are the soldiers"}},{q="What quests does Commander Althea offer?",a="Althea offers the core Night Watch questline, dispatching adventurers to hunt wolves, skeletal fiends, and ghouls across Duskwood. She also assists in investigating the Legend of Stalvan and dealing with the wandering terror Mor'Ladim.",al={"althea quests","night watch questline"}},{q="What does Althea do when Stitches attacks Darkshire?",a="When the stitched abomination created by Abercrombie marches on Darkshire, Althea sounds the alarm and leads the town's remaining Night Watch guards in a direct, bloody stand to stop the monster before it enters the town square.",al={"althea stitches","who fights stitches","darkshire under attack"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Althea represents the grim determination of the Alliance's forgotten frontiers, holding the kingdom together where the crown's armies have withdrawn.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors find in Althea a stern, practical commander who respects martial discipline and values frontline fighters willing to hold the line against overwhelming odds.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins walking the gloomy roads of Duskwood can assist Althea in putting restless souls to peace, lifting some of the spiritual dread weighing on her militia."},kw={"althea","commander","darkshire","duskwood","ebonlocke","militia","mor'ladim","night watch","stitches"},rel={"topic:night-watch","npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:56","topic:mor-ladim","quest:66"},src={"Althea Ebonlocke"}}
E["npc:blind-mary"] = {t="npc",n="Blind Mary",z="duskwood",s="Blind Mary is a tormented banshee haunting an abandoned, ruined farmhouse just southeast of Darkshire in Duskwood. Once a vain and beautiful mortal woman, her violent death and transformation drove her to self-inflicted mutilation in grief over what she had become.",h="Blind Mary is a tormented banshee haunting an abandoned, ruined farmhouse just southeast of Darkshire in...",sec={{t="A Tragic Vanity",b="Before the shadows fell across Duskwood, Mary was known as a striking mortal woman who took immense pride in her beauty, rarely seen without her treasured looking glass. When the undead swept over the region, Mary was slain along with many of her neighbors. Unlike those who found rest in the earth, her spirit lingered on as an ethereal banshee, condemned to wander the mortal realm in a ghastly, translucent form.",sp=0},{t="Blinded by Despair",b="Awakening to undeath, Mary was overwhelmed by sorrow, horror, and fury at her monstrous reflection. Incapable of enduring the sight of her spectral visage, she clawed out her own eyes with her bare hands so she would never gaze upon herself again. In her agony, she discarded her beloved looking glass, leaving her to drift through her abandoned home as a blind, weeping wraith clutching to faint memories of the mortal life she lost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Blind Mary?",a="Blind Mary is a banshee haunting a ruined homestead on the southeastern outskirts of Darkshire. In life, she was a beautiful local woman, but she was slaughtered during Duskwood's descent into darkness and arose as an undead spirit.",al={"who is blind mary","blind mary backstory","blind mary lore","blind mary duskwood"}},{q="Why is she called Blind Mary?",a="Consumed by grief and despair over her horrific banshee form, Mary clawed her own eyes out with her bare hands so she would never have to witness her own reflection again.",al={"why is she blind","how did blind mary lose her eyes","blind mary eyes"}},{q="Where does Blind Mary dwell?",a="She lingers inside a dilapidated farmhouse known as Blind Mary's Haunt, situated just southeast of the town of Darkshire in eastern Duskwood.",al={"blind mary location","where is blind mary","blind mary haunt"}},{q="Is Blind Mary hostile to living travelers?",a="Unlike the aggressive ghouls and skeletons wandering the surrounding woods, Blind Mary does not immediately attack travelers. She remains trapped in mourning and can be spoken to by those who approach her ruin.",al={"is blind mary hostile","does blind mary attack","can you talk to blind mary"}},{q="What happened to Mary's looking glass?",a="After tearing out her eyes in horror at her spectral state, Mary cast away her prized looking glass, leaving it lost somewhere among the haunted reaches of Duskwood.",al={"mary mirror","blind mary looking glass","what happened to her mirror"}},{q="Why do adventurers seek out Blind Mary?",a="Travelers and local artisans visit Mary during tasks around Darkshire, whether seeking to recover long-lost items like her discarded mirror, gathering ghost hair for specialized stitching, or returning forgotten personal keepsakes to soothe her tormented spirit.",al={"blind mary quests","why visit blind mary","blind mary questline"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Artisans of the loom occasionally seek out spectral entities like Mary for ghost hair thread, a delicate and supernatural material woven from ethereal remnants.",["class:Priest"]="Mary represents a tragic example of a soul untethered by horrific trauma, caught halfway between life and damnation through grief and vanity.",["faction:Alliance"]="Blind Mary's tragic fate is an intimate reminder for Darkshire's defenders of how deeply the curse of Duskwood has devastated everyday townsfolk."},kw={"banshee","blind mary","darkshire","duskwood","ghost hair","haunt","looking glass","wraith"},rel={"subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:149","quest:154","quest:174"},src={"Blind Mary"}}
E["npc:calor"] = {t="npc",n="Calor",z="duskwood",s="Calor is a dedicated resident of Darkshire who aids the Night Watch and the Carevin family in defending Duskwood. Operating under the direction of Jonathan Carevin, he actively coordinates efforts to hunt down the vicious worgen stalking the gloomy forests. Adventurers looking to push back the ravenous beasts haunting the woods often find their assignments through him.",h="Calor is a dedicated resident of Darkshire who aids the Night Watch and the Carevin family in defending...",sec={{t="A Loyalist in the Shadows",b="Stationed within the beleaguered settlement of Darkshire, Calor works closely with Jonathan Carevin, one of the town's prominent defenders. Amid the endless gloom and creeping terrors of Duskwood, Calor devotes himself to supporting the Carevin household's mission: eradicating the supernatural horrors encroaching upon the town's perimeter before the remaining townsfolk are slaughtered.",sp=0},{t="The Worgen Menace",b="Calor's primary duty centers on confronting the feral worgen prowling the woods, particularly around blighted areas like the Rotting Orchard. These ferocious wolf-men are far more aggressive and dangerous than common beasts, slaughtering travelers and patrols alike. Calor enlists capable fighters to cull their ranks and investigate their origins, desperate to stem the bloodthirsty tide.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Calor?",a="Calor is a human allied with the Carevin family living in Darkshire. He assists in the town's defense by dispatching adventurers to hunt down dangerous threats in Duskwood.",al={"calor darkshire","who is calor","calor duskwood"}},{q="Where can Calor be found?",a="Calor is stationed in Darkshire, the primary Alliance town nestled in the shadowed forests of Duskwood.",al={"where is calor","calor location","calor coordinates"}},{q="What is Calor's relationship with Jonathan Carevin?",a="Calor is a staunch supporter of the Carevin family. He follows the directives of Jonathan Carevin, helping him wage war against the deadly monsters plaguing the forest.",al={"calor and carevin","who does calor work for","carevin family calor"}},{q="What enemies does Calor have you fight?",a="Calor tasks adventurers with hunting the bloodthirsty worgen packs that infest the woods, particularly directing strikes against them near places such as the Rotting Orchard.",al={"calor quests","what does calor want","worgen quests calor"}},{q="Why is the worgen threat so urgent in Duskwood?",a="The worgen are vicious, ravenous predators that attack anything on sight. Without regular culls coordinated by figures like Calor and the Night Watch, the beasts would quickly overrun Darkshire's thin defense lines.",al={"why kill worgen duskwood","duskwood worgen threat"}},{q="Is Calor a member of the Night Watch?",a="While Calor works in close conjunction with town defenders and aligns with Jonathan Carevin, he primarily operates as a direct agent and supporter of the Carevin family's anti-worgen crusade.",al={"calor night watch","is calor in night watch"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Calor serves as a vital contact for Alliance champions willing to brave the gloomy woods to defend the isolated townsfolk of Darkshire.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters will find steady work with Calor, tracking and culling savage, otherworldly beasts that defy the natural order of the forest."},kw={"calor","carevin","darkshire","duskwood","jonathan carevin","night watch","rotting orchard","worgen"},rel={"npc:jonathan-carevin","quest:173","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","topic:worgen","topic:night-watch","subzone:rotting-orchard","quest:1042"},src={"Calor"}}
E["npc:caretaker-folsom"] = {t="npc",n="Caretaker Folsom",z="duskwood",s="Caretaker Folsom is a somber human servant found along the Canals of Stormwind City near the Park. Once the trusted overseer of the noble Flintridge family's estate, he now handles the bitter remnants of their tragic downfall.",h="Caretaker Folsom is a somber human servant found along the Canals of Stormwind City near the Park.",sec={{t="A House in Ruins",b="Like his father before him, Folsom devoted his life to serving the Flintridge family as their estate caretaker. That quiet life of service came to a bloody end with the brutal murder of the Flintridge household at the hands of their tutor, Stalvan Mistmantle. With the bloodline wiped out, the manor sat abandoned until its remaining funds completely dried up. Left alone to oversee the remnants of the household, Folsom bears the sorrowful duty of liquidating the family's surviving heirlooms and possessions at auction.",sp=0},{t="Ties to a Dark Tale",b="Investigators tracing the bloody history of Stalvan Mistmantle are often directed to Folsom along the Stormwind canal walkways. Though burdened by grief and reluctance, the caretaker holds key pieces of the tragedy, including surviving possessions and documents from the Flintridge household that reveal Stalvan's disturbing descent and eventual disappearance into the shadows of Duskwood.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Caretaker Folsom?",a="He is a human servant in Stormwind City who formerly tended the Flintridge noble estate. Following the tragic murder of the entire Flintridge family, he has been left in charge of their remaining property.",al={"folsom","who is folsom","caretaker folsom lore"}},{q="Where can I find Caretaker Folsom?",a="He stands along the stone walkways of the Canals in Stormwind City, close to the entrance of the Park.",al={"where is caretaker folsom","folsom location","caretaker folsom stormwind"}},{q="What happened to the Flintridge family?",a="The entire family was murdered by their tutor, Stalvan Mistmantle. With no heirs remaining to claim the estate, the property was shuttered and left to languish until its funds ran out.",al={"flintridge murder","what happened to flintridge","who killed the flintridges"},sp=1},{q="Why is Folsom selling off family heirlooms?",a="After the family's demise, their remaining funds eventually dried up entirely. Folsom was tasked with the grim duty of sending what was left of the estate's possessions to auction.",al={"why auction","flintridge auction","folsom auction"}},{q="What is his role in The Legend of Stalvan?",a="Folsom assists adventurers piecing together the tragedy of Stalvan Mistmantle by providing access to the remaining personal effects and clues left behind from the Flintridge manor.",al={"stalvan quest folsom","the legend of stalvan folsom"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance investigators tracking the grim fate of Duskwood's most infamous murderer, Folsom provides an indispensable living link to the final days of the Flintridge household."},kw={"canals","caretaker folsom","flintridge","folsom","mistmantle","park","stalvan","stormwind"},rel={"quest:66","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:park","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Caretaker Folsom"}}
E["npc:chef-grual"] = {t="npc",n="Chef Grual",z="duskwood",s="Chef Grual is the resident cook at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. In a secluded town choked by mist and monsters, Grual does his best to keep the Night Watch and weary travelers fed, even if his choice of ingredients raises eyebrows.",h="Chef Grual is the resident cook at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire.",sec={{t="Cooking Under Siege",b="Running an eatery in Darkshire is a grim task. With supply lines from Westfall and Stormwind constantly harassed by highwaymen, wolves, and undead, fresh provisions are virtually nonexistent. Grual makes do with whatever the wilderness provides. From wolf flank to whatever scavenged meats local adventurers drag through the door, Grual cooks with pragmatism born of necessity.",sp=0},{t="Secret Ingredients",b="Grual is infamous for his specialty dishes, most notably his famous 'Dusky Crab Cakes' and seasoned wolf kabobs. Given that coastal crabs are nowhere near the gloomy inland woods of Duskwood, his crab cakes rely on a rather revolting substitute: the gooey legs of local Pygmy Venomblood and giant webwood spiders. Whether patrons realize they are eating arachnid meat or simply prefer not to ask, Grual keeps the kitchen running without apologies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Chef Grual?",a="Chef Grual is the human culinary provider stationed inside the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. He prepares meals for the town's defenders, travelers, and refugees hiding from the dangers of Duskwood.",al={"chef grual","grual darkshire","darkshire cook"}},{q="Where can I find Chef Grual?",a="He can be found standing in the back room and kitchen area of the Scarlet Raven Tavern in central Darkshire, located along the southern edge of the main road.",al={"grual location","where is chef grual","find chef grual"}},{q="What are Dusky Crab Cakes actually made of?",a="Despite the name, there are no crabs in Duskwood. Chef Grual substitutes gooey spider legs harvested from the monstrous arachnids infesting the surrounding forests, mincing them into patties that mimic seafood.",al={"crab cake ingredients","spider crab cakes","what is in dusky crab cakes"}},{q="What quests does Chef Grual offer?",a="Grual tasks travelers with gathering fresh ingredients from the wild, including wolf flanks for his Seasoned Wolf Kabobs and spider legs for his Dusky Crab Cakes. He also assists in preparing a soothing meal to settle Jitters' nervous stomach.",al={"grual quests","chef grual recipes"}},{q="Why does he feed Jitters?",a="Jitters, a terrified hermit camped in the woods, frequently suffers from stomach distress brought on by unrelenting fear and malnutrition. Grual is approached to whip up something hearty to calm his nerves.",al={"jitters food","jitters growling gut grual"}},{q="Is Grual affiliated with the Night Watch?",a="Grual is a civilian cook rather than a militant guardsman, but his kitchen directly supports the Night Watch and local militia by keeping Darkshire nourished in the face of constant siege.",al={"grual night watch","does grual fight"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Grual serves as a grim lesson in culinary improvisation, proving that in isolated regions, a cook uses whatever local wildlife walks or skitters through the trees.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stationed in Darkshire's Scarlet Raven Tavern, Grual keeps the weary defenders of the Alliance nourished despite the lack of regular supply caravans from Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="Like many remaining residents of Darkshire, Grual exhibits a grim, stubborn resilience, adapting to the horrors of the shadowed woods in his own pragmatic way."},kw={"chef grual","crab cakes","darkshire","duskwood","grual","jitters","scarlet raven tavern","wolf kabobs"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:93","quest:90","npc:jitters","quest:5","quest:240"},src={"Chef Grual"}}
E["npc:clerk-daltry"] = {t="npc",n="Clerk Daltry",z="duskwood",s="Clerk Daltry is the civic record keeper stationed in Darkshire Town Hall in Duskwood. Surrounded by ledgers and registry books, he helps investigate the village's past and track down historical records, even if his archives are somewhat neglected and out of date.",h="Clerk Daltry is the civic record keeper stationed in Darkshire Town Hall in Duskwood.",sec={{t="Town Record Keeper",b="While Darkshire struggles against encroaching beasts, undead horrors, and supernatural gloom, everyday civic duties fall to Clerk Daltry. Working out of the Darkshire Town Hall alongside Lord Ello Ebonlocke and the local council, Daltry maintains the town's historical ledgers, property rolls, and census data. In a region fractured by disaster, his records are among the few surviving links to the days before Grand Hamlet fell into shadow.",sp=0},{t="The Paper Trail",b="Because Darkshire has been cut off from regular Stormwind administration, Daltry's record-keeping is notoriously imperfect. Old documents go missing, ledgers fall behind, and vital town files are frequently misplaced or damaged. Adventurers investigating local cold cases or long-lost residents frequently consult him, only to find that uncovering the truth requires digging through overlooked notes or venturing out into the dangerous woods to recover lost papers.",sp=0},{t="The Legend of Stalvan",b="Daltry plays a central role in untangling the dark mystery of Stalvan Mistmantle. When an ominous family legend leads investigators back to Darkshire, Daltry searches his archives for records of the former schoolteacher. Because his town registry entries on Stalvan are fragmented, Daltry must send seekers across town and into forgotten homesteads across the kingdom to piece together the tragic and bloody truth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Clerk Daltry located?",a="Clerk Daltry is found inside the Darkshire Town Hall, located in the central village of Darkshire in Duskwood. He stands amidst the town officials and council members, managing the municipal records.",al={"clerk daltry location","where is daltry","darkshire clerk location"}},{q="What is Clerk Daltry's job in Darkshire?",a="He serves as Darkshire's civic clerk, tasked with preserving documents, town rolls, and legal registries. He assists adventurers who need archival information regarding former residents, land claims, or historical inquiries.",al={"what does daltry do","daltry role","who is clerk daltry"}},{q="Why are his records incomplete?",a="Duskwood has suffered years of isolation, magical corruption, and violent turmoil. With the town's focus consumed by immediate survival against the Night Watch's enemies, maintaining up-to-date ledgers has often fallen by the wayside, leaving his archives fragmented.",al={"why are daltry's records bad","outdated records duskwood","missing ledgers daltry"}},{q="What questlines does Clerk Daltry start or participate in?",a="Daltry is a crucial figure in 'The Legend of Stalvan' storyline, helping players track down the elusive past of Stalvan Mistmantle. He also assists with investigations such as 'The Carevin Family' and 'The Shadowy Search Continues'.",al={"daltry quests","what quests from daltry","clerk daltry quest chain"}},{q="Is Clerk Daltry related to Surveyor Daltry?",a="It is widely suspected they share family ties given their common surname and service roles, though Clerk Daltry stays strictly focused on his municipal duties in Darkshire.",al={"surveyor daltry relation","daltry family"}},{q="Can Horde players speak with Clerk Daltry?",a="No. Clerk Daltry is an Alliance-affiliated municipal servant. Darkshire and its town hall are guarded by the Night Watch and hostile to all Horde adventurers.",al={"is daltry friendly to horde","can horde talk to daltry"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance investigators uncovering the sinister mysteries of Duskwood, Clerk Daltry is an essential bureaucratic contact for long-lost records and cold case files.",["race:Human"]="Daltry preserves what remains of the historical heritage of Grand Hamlet before the darkness descended upon the woodland realm."},kw={"carevin","clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","ledgers","mistmantle","records","stalvan","town hall"},rel={"subzone:darkshire-town-hall","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:66","quest:265","quest:266","quest:1042","subzone:roland-s-doom"},src={"Clerk Daltry"}}
E["npc:glorin-steelbrow"] = {t="npc",n="Glorin Steelbrow",z="duskwood",s="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarven operative found drinking at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Acting as an associate of Bishop Farthing in Darkshire, he helps adventurers investigate the lost Third Fleet and recover sacred relics and materials scattered across the Wetlands coast. His efforts tie the haunted wilderness of Duskwood directly to the sunken shipwrecks of the north.",h="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarven operative found drinking at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Harbor Connection",b="While Bishop Farthing oversees the spiritual and martial defense of Darkshire against the creeping terrors of Duskwood, he maintains ties far to the north in Menethil Harbor. Stationed inside the bustling Deepwater Tavern, Glorin Steelbrow acts as Farthing's eyes and hands on the coast. He offers aid and direction to travelers sent north in search of sacred metals and forgotten relics, providing a crucial bridge between the troubles of the southern forest and the sunken wreckage of the Wetlands.",sp=0},{t="The Doomed Fleet and Lost Relics",b="Steelbrow is intimately familiar with the tragedy of the Third Fleet, whose ships were battered and dragged beneath the waves along the Wetlands shore. He guides adventurers to scour the haunted wreckage for lost ingots of Lightforge iron and the powerful, cursed artifact known as the Eye of Paleth. Glorin knows that recovering such holy armaments is vital for forging weapons capable of holding back the dark forces threatening the Alliance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Glorin Steelbrow?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarf stationed in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. He works in coordination with Bishop Farthing of Darkshire, assisting adventurers who travel north to salvage sunken cargo and relics off the Wetlands coast.",al={"who is glorin","glorin steelbrow lore","what does glorin do"}},{q="Where can I find Glorin Steelbrow?",a="Glorin is located on the ground floor of the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, situated on the western coast of the Wetlands.",al={"glorin location","where is glorin steelbrow","glorin deepwater tavern"}},{q="Why is a dwarf in Menethil Harbor involved with Duskwood?",a="Bishop Farthing in Darkshire requires powerful holy relics and consecrated metals to fight the darkness encroaching on Duskwood. He sends trusted emissaries to Glorin Steelbrow, who knows the Wetlands coast and can point salvagers toward the sunken remains of the Third Fleet.",al={"why duskwood quest in wetlands","connection to farthing","why send to wetlands"}},{q="What is the Third Fleet that Glorin talks about?",a="The Third Fleet was an Alliance naval expedition that met catastrophe off the coast of the Wetlands. Its shattered hulls now litter the seabed, haunted by drowned sailors and hiding valuable cargo like Lightforge iron and ancient artifacts.",al={"what is the doomed fleet","third fleet wetlands","the doomed fleet quest"}},{q="What is the Eye of Paleth?",a="The Eye of Paleth is an ancient religious relic carried aboard the sunken fleet. Once recovered from the ocean floor with Glorin's guidance, it must undergo cleansing by the priesthood due to the dark corruption lingering around the shipwreck.",al={"eye of paleth","paleth relic","what is eye of paleth"}},{q="What is Lightforge iron used for?",a="Lightforge iron is a rare, sanctified metal used to craft blessed weapons capable of striking down powerful undead and demonic forces. Glorin helps recover lost ingots from the shipwrecks to aid the defenders of Duskwood.",al={"lightforge iron","lost ingots","blessed arm"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Glorin represents dwarven enterprise and solidarity, coordinating from the maritime hub of Menethil Harbor to support allies across Khaz Modan and the southern human kingdoms.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins following Farthing's orders will find Glorin indispensable in recovering Lightforge iron, a sacred metal essential for crafting weapons blessed by the Holy Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="Glorin plays a key role in recovering crucial Alliance military relics and sanctified materials lost during naval disasters in the Wetlands."},kw={"bishop farthing","deepwater tavern","doomed fleet","duskwood","eye of paleth","glorin steelbrow","lightforge iron","menethil harbor","wetlands"},rel={"npc:farthing","quest:270","quest:321","quest:324","quest:292","subzone:deepwater-tavern","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands"},src={"Glorin Steelbrow"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-farley"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Farley",z="duskwood",s="Innkeeper Fredrik Farley manages the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, providing food, lodging, and hearthstones to travelers passing through Elwynn Forest. Well-liked and observant, he often holds misplaced mail and listens to the troubles of adventurers on the road.",h="Innkeeper Fredrik Farley manages the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, providing food, lodging, and hearthstones...",sec={{t="A Goldshire Fixture",b="The Farley family has operated the Lion's Pride Inn since the reign of King Llane Wrynn I. Alongside his wife Verina and their daughter Anna, Fredrik runs the establishment with a welcoming hand and a sharp eye. With large, sturdy hands well-suited to breaking up tavern brawls or expelling rowdy patrons, he keeps order in one of the realm's busiest waystations. Though his days are filled with pouring ale and serving cheese, he carries the private grief of losing his brother Frandis, a guard who perished in Lordaeron during the Scourge's plague.",sp=0},{t="The Courier's Abandoned Chest",b="Because Goldshire sits at the crossroads between Stormwind, Westfall, and Duskwood, Farley overhears plenty of rumors and deals with strange travelers. Notably, he once took in a royal courier who bolted into the night in terror, abandoning his satchel behind. Farley safely stowed the leftover missives in an upstairs chest—including an undelivered letter addressed to the former schoolmaster Stalvan Mistmantle, which eventually serves as a critical clue for investigators tracing the fallen tutor's movements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Innkeeper Farley?",a="Fredrik Farley is the proprietor of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. His family has managed the inn for generations, dating back to the time of King Llane Wrynn I. He runs the business alongside his wife, Verina, offering rest and supplies to travelers traversing Elwynn Forest.",al={"innkeeper farley","fredrik farley","who is the goldshire innkeeper"}},{q="What does Farley know about Stalvan Mistmantle?",a="Farley remembers a terrified courier who fled the Lion's Pride Inn in the dead of night, leaving behind several deliveries. Farley stored the abandoned letters in a chest upstairs, among which is an undelivered letter addressed to Stalvan Mistmantle that investigators can retrieve.",al={"farley stalvan","stalvan letter goldshire","legend of stalvan farley"}},{q="Where is Farley's brother?",a="Fredrik's brother, Frandis Farley, left the south to work as a caravan guard in the northern kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Third War, Frandis was reported killed by the plague of undeath, leaving Fredrik heartbroken.",al={"farley brother","frandis farley lore","what happened to farley's brother"}},{q="What services does Farley provide at the inn?",a="Farley sets home hearthstones for travelers, rents rooms, and sells a wide variety of drinks, juices, and cheeses from across the Alliance, ranging from Alterac Swiss and Dalaran Sharp to local Stormwind Brie.",al={"lion's pride services","farley food and drink","goldshire hearthstone"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For fresh recruits heading out from Northshire Valley, Farley's counter at the Lion's Pride is often the very first place they bind their hearthstone and purchase provisions."},kw={"elwynn forest","frandis","fredrik farley","goldshire","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","stalvan"},rel={"subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:66","topic:llane-wrynn-i","topic:alliance","zone:duskwood"},src={"Innkeeper Farley"}}
E["npc:jitters"] = {t="npc",n="Jitters",z="duskwood",s="Jitters is a trembling, reclusive human hiding out among the ruins of Raven Hill in western Duskwood. Consumed by constant paranoia and fear, he survives alone on Duskwood's perilous western edge, relying on passing adventurers for assistance while watching the encroaching shadows.",h="Jitters is a trembling, reclusive human hiding out among the ruins of Raven Hill in western Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Haunted Hermit",b="Found shivering amid the dilapidated houses of Raven Hill, Jitters lives in constant terror of the predators stalking Duskwood's western trails. He relies on passing adventurers for simple sustenance, desperate for food while keeping a frantic eye on the encroaching shadows. His skittish mannerisms and uncanny reflex for leaping clear of sudden danger earned him his moniker long ago, but his frantic paranoia is born from firsthand encounters with horrific horrors.",sp=0},{t="The Awakening at Roland's Doom",b="Jitters was originally affiliated with the Defias Brotherhood as they moved into Duskwood. While digging at the mine known as Roland's Doom, he uncovered the Scythe of Elune protruding from the rock. The artifact unleashed ferocious, bloodthirsty worgen into the woods. Jitters watched in horror as his comrades were torn to pieces, barely escaping the slaughter with his own skin intact.",sp=1},{t="Flight and the Farmstead",b="Fleeing the mine, Jitters retreated to Darkshire, purchasing a blank tome from Clerk Daltry and feverishly chronicling the nightmare while hiding at the Scarlet Raven Tavern. Panicked, he took refuge in a barn at the Yorgen Farmstead. There, he witnessed black-cloaked Dark Riders butchering Sven Yorgen's family in search of the Scythe. Terrified of being blamed or found, Jitters buried pages of his journal in the soil and fled to Raven Hill, pursued by crippling guilt and ceaseless dread.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Jitters?",a="Jitters is a frightened human surviving alone among the abandoned buildings of Raven Hill in Duskwood. Once involved with the Defias Brotherhood, he is now a desperate vagrant tormented by the disasters he inadvertently set in motion.",al={"who is this guy","jitters lore","jitters background"},sp=1},{q="Why is he called Jitters?",a="His nickname originated from his cautious nature, specifically his instinctive habit of flinching away from strikes and leaping clear of sudden pitfalls. His prolonged isolation and sheer terror in Duskwood have only made his nervousness worse.",al={"why jitters","where did his name come from","jitters name origin"}},{q="How did the worgen get into Duskwood?",a="While exploring the mine at Roland's Doom, Jitters unearthed the Scythe of Elune lodged in the stone. Disturbance of the cursed artifact allowed savage worgen to cross into Duskwood, instantly butchering Jitters' companions and spreading across the forest.",al={"who brought worgen","worgen origin duskwood","roland's doom worgen"},sp=1},{q="What happened to Sven Yorgen's family?",a="Ominous figures known as the Dark Riders attacked the farmstead while hunting for the Scythe of Elune. Jitters was hiding in the barn at the time and witnessed the slaughter of Sven's wife and children, but was too terrified to intervene.",al={"sven farm massacre","who killed sven family","yorgen farmstead murder"},sp=1},{q="Why is Sven Yorgen angry with Jitters?",a="When Sven returned to find his family murdered, he caught sight of Jitters frantically burying a journal near the property before fleeing into the woods. Sven initially suspected Jitters of having a hand in the tragedy or hiding knowledge of the killers.",al={"sven and jitters","why does sven hate jitters"},sp=1},{q="What is Jitters' journal?",a="After escaping Roland's Doom, Jitters bought a blank book from Clerk Daltry in Darkshire and spent nights at the Scarlet Raven Tavern writing down the events surrounding the Scythe of Elune, the worgen, and the Dark Riders. Parts of this journal were later buried at the Yorgen Farmstead.",al={"jitters diary","jitters completed journal","daltry book"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Jitters represents the human face of Duskwood's tragedy—a man whose misguided curiosity shattered the fragile safety of the realm and left the Night Watch fighting a desperate war against beasts and riders.",["class:Rogue"]="Before his terror took hold, Jitters put his quick instincts to work alongside the Defias Brotherhood during their covert infiltration of the southern territories.",["race:NightElf"]="The artifact Jitters disturbed at Roland's Doom bears the name of the moon goddess Elune, hinting at sacred Kaldorei magic that has been twisted into a feral nightmare."},kw={"clerk daltry","dark riders","duskwood","jitters","raven hill","roland's doom","scythe of elune","sven yorgen","worgen"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","subzone:roland-s-doom","subzone:yorgen-farmstead","topic:worgen","topic:dark-riders","topic:elune","quest:5","quest:163"},src={"Jitters"}}
E["npc:jonathan-carevin"] = {t="npc",n="Jonathan Carevin",z="duskwood",s="Jonathan Carevin is a resolute human hunter residing in Darkshire, dedicated to eradicating the darkness plaguing Duskwood. Unlike the defensive Night Watch, he and his family actively hunt down the undead, worgen, and any heretical threats lurking under the darkened canopies.",h="Jonathan Carevin is a resolute human hunter residing in Darkshire, dedicated to eradicating the darkness...",sec={{t="The Carevin Crusade",b="While Darkshire depends upon the Night Watch to patrol the roads and safeguard the township, Jonathan Carevin believes a mere defensive perimeter is insufficient. Alongside his family and allies like Calor, Jonathan takes the offensive. He actively targets the unholy fiends wandering Duskwood, pursuing a personal crusade to purge all demons, undead, and heretics from the region under the grace of the Light.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Worgen",b="Jonathan's vigilance extends beyond shambling skeletons and ghouls. He pays close attention to the savage, wolf-like beasts known as worgen that stalk the forest depths. Knowing the danger they present to an already besieged settlement, Jonathan coordinates investigations into their mysterious presence, seeking to uncover where these ungodly predators originated and putting an end to their nocturnal prowling.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Jonathan Carevin?",a="Jonathan Carevin is a grim hunter living in Darkshire in Duskwood. He leads the Carevin family in an active fight against the foul monsters haunting the forest.",al={"who is carevin","jonathan carevin lore","carevin darkshire"}},{q="How does he differ from the Night Watch?",a="While the Night Watch focuses primarily on guarding Darkshire's perimeter and keeping the roads passable, Jonathan and his supporters actively track and hunt down the undead and other abominations to eradicate them at their source.",al={"is he night watch","carevin vs night watch"}},{q="What threats does he fight?",a="Jonathan actively hunts the undead, ravenous worgen packs, demons, and anyone who would offer shelter or aid to such unholy abominations.",al={"what does carevin hunt","carevin targets"}},{q="Is Jonathan affiliated with the Scarlet Crusade?",a="His harsh rhetoric, fervent devotion to the Light, and strict zero-tolerance approach toward corruption mirror Scarlet beliefs, but officially he operates independently alongside his family in Darkshire.",al={"carevin scarlet crusade","is carevin scarlet"}},{q="Who assists Jonathan in his mission?",a="Beyond his immediate family, Jonathan receives direct assistance from sympathetic combatants such as Calor, who aids him in tracking monstrous incursions across the woods.",al={"carevin allies","who helps carevin"}},{q="What is his connection to the worgen?",a="Jonathan views the worgen as an unnatural menace terrorizing Duskwood's people and tasks travelers with uncovering the source of their sudden emergence in the wilderness.",al={"carevin worgen","why carevin hate worgen"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions trying to stabilize Duskwood, Jonathan Carevin provides targeted strikes against the supernatural threats that Stormwind's neglect has left unchecked.",["class:Paladin"]="Carevin's zeal and invocation of the Light against demonic and undead corruption resonate deeply with a paladin's sacred vows.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters find common ground with Carevin's proactive tracking and methodical culling of Duskwood's nocturnal predators."},kw={"calor","carevin family","darkshire","duskwood","jonathan carevin","night watch","undead","worgen"},rel={"quest:1042","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","npc:calor","quest:173","quest:1043","topic:night-watch","topic:worgen"},src={"Jonathan Carevin"}}
E["npc:lars"] = {t="npc",n="Lars",z="duskwood",s="Lars is a beleaguered human survivor camping out in the wilderness of Duskwood. Along with his companion Sven Yorgen, he struggles to hold his ground on the northern edge of the Hushed Bank against the terrors that stalk the forest.",h="Lars is a beleaguered human survivor camping out in the wilderness of Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Precarious Perch",b="Perched in a modest camp on the northern edge of the Hushed Bank, Lars ekes out a precarious survival far from the questionable safety of Darkshire. Duskwood is treacherous at the best of times, but the surrounding woods crawl with ferocious beasts, relentless undead, and creeping worgen. Lars stays close by Sven Yorgen, striving simply to stay alive in an increasingly hostile wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Threat from the Wilds",b="Survival at the camp requires constant vigilance against the local predators. Lars finds himself sorely pressed by the relentless packs of starving dire wolves that haunt the shadows around their fire. Unable to lower his guard or drive them back alone, he relies on capable travelers to thin the hungry predators before his small camp is completely overrun.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lars?",a="Lars is a human survivor camping out in the wilds of Duskwood. He lives alongside his friend and companion Sven Yorgen on the northern border of the Hushed Bank, doing what he can to survive the forest's horrors.",al={"lars duskwood","who is lars","lars npc"}},{q="Where can Lars be found?",a="Lars is stationed at a small wilderness camp along the northern edge of the Hushed Bank, situated in western Duskwood.",al={"where is lars","lars location","lars camp"}},{q="What problem does Lars face?",a="Lars and Sven are constantly harassed by the ravenous wolves and predators lurking in the woods nearby. Through the task 'Wolves at Our Heels', Lars asks passing adventurers to hunt down the predators before they tear his camp apart.",al={"lars quest","wolves at our heels quest","why does lars need help"}},{q="What is Lars's relationship to Sven Yorgen?",a="Lars and Sven Yorgen are companions surviving together in the wilderness. Sven has his own dark history and vendetta in the region, while Lars helps maintain their rough, isolated outpost.",al={"lars and sven","who is sven to lars"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lars is a beleaguered human civilian surviving outside the town guard's reach, glad to find Alliance champions willing to cut down the wolves circling his campsite."},kw={"camp","duskwood","hushed bank","lars","sven yorgen","wolves","wolves at our heels"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","subzone:hushed-bank","zone:duskwood","quest:226","topic:worgen"},src={"Lars"}}
E["npc:madame-eva"] = {t="npc",n="Madame Eva",z="duskwood",s="Madame Eva is a revered fortune-teller and matriarch living in Darkshire in the shadowed forest of Duskwood. Practicing older, mystic arts of divination and cartomancy, she often serves as the first townsperson to sense unnatural disturbances across the woods. Travelers frequently seek her out to unravel grim mysteries or procure occult charms against the creeping dark.",h="Madame Eva is a revered fortune-teller and matriarch living in Darkshire in the shadowed forest of Duskwood.",sec={{t="The Fortune-Teller of Darkshire",b="Dwelling quietly amidst the gloom of Darkshire, Madame Eva practices cartomancy and ancient folk rituals that many in Stormwind's cathedral would view with suspicion. In a forsaken region plagued by feral beasts, the undead, and darker horrors, her eerie insights are tolerated and sought after by desperate townspeople and visiting adventurers alike.",sp=0},{t="Ties of Blood and Prophecy",b="Beyond her role as an occult reader, Madame Eva is deeply devoted to her family, serving as grandmother to Alyssa Eva and young Lohgan. When her cartomancy reveals dark omens threatening her granddaughter, Eva does not hesitate to enlist the aid of passing wanderers to scour the woods, uncovering long-buried tragedies before history can repeat itself.",sp=0},{t="Weaving Protection Against the Night",b="Eva's knowledge extends beyond card reading to ritual crafting and warding. From weaving supernatural garments using spectral thread to crafting bizarre folk relics like the Totem of Infliction, she understands the strange, twilight logic that governs Duskwood's restless spirits better than almost anyone else in town.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Madame Eva?",a="Madame Eva is an elderly human fortune-teller and diviner residing in Darkshire. She practices cartomancy and ancient folk crafts to glimpse the unseen perils stalking Duskwood.",al={"madame eva","who is eva","darkshire fortune teller"}},{q="What is Madame Eva's role in the mystery of Stalvan?",a="Madame Eva reads the cards and senses an imminent, supernatural danger encircling her granddaughter Alyssa. Her readings guide adventurers to investigate forgotten documents and trails that uncover the grim history of Stalvan Mistmantle.",al={"eva stalvan","legend of stalvan eva","why does eva care about stalvan"}},{q="Is Madame Eva a witch or a mage?",a="Eva is primarily a seer and practitioner of older mystic arts, such as cartomancy, spirit-thread weaving, and folk effigies. Her magic is more akin to traditional fortune-telling and occult lore than the structured arcanum of Dalaran or the Holy Light.",al={"is eva a witch","eva magic type","what magic does eva use"}},{q="Who is related to Madame Eva in Darkshire?",a="She is the grandmother of Alyssa Eva and Lohgan Eva. The town's Night Watch also includes Watcher Eva, who is believed to share ties with her family.",al={"eva family","madame eva grandchildren","alyssa eva grandmother"}},{q="What is Ghost Hair Thread used for?",a="Madame Eva gathers ethereal strands of ghost hair thread from restless spirits to weave specially prepared ritual garments and provide supplies needed by allies across the realm.",al={"ghost hair thread","eva thread quest"}},{q="Why does Madame Eva craft the Totem of Infliction?",a="Madame Eva crafts the Totem of Infliction as a dark, sympathetic effigy. By binding specific creature materials to it, the totem directs curses and harm back onto the fell beasts terrorizing the woods.",al={"totem of infliction","eva totem"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions stepping into the oppressive shadow of Duskwood, Madame Eva is an indispensable guide whose premonitions cut through the woods' deadly confusion.",["class:Priest"]="While the Holy Light brings solace to the living, priests will find Eva's reliance on cartomancy and spirit remnants a curious, earthen counterpoint to traditional church liturgy.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Tailors will appreciate Eva's knowledge of bizarre weaving materials, specifically her ability to work spectral thread plucked directly from the ghosts of the region."},kw={"alyssa eva","cartomancy","darkshire","duskwood","fortune teller","ghost hair thread","madame eva","stalvan"},rel={"quest:66","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:149","quest:101","quest:157","quest:262","quest:148"},src={"Madame Eva"}}
E["npc:sirra-von-indi"] = {t="npc",n="Sirra Von'Indi",z="duskwood",s="Sirra Von'Indi is the resident historian of Darkshire, stationed within the town hall amid stacks of forgotten records. Versed in ancient languages and local history, he assists the township in deciphering mysterious documents and uncovering the dark past of Duskwood.",h="Sirra Von'Indi is the resident historian of Darkshire, stationed within the town hall amid stacks of...",sec={{t="The Town Historian",b="Sirra Von'Indi serves as Darkshire's foremost scholar, keeping watch over the settlement's archives from inside the Darkshire Town Hall. While the town guard focuses on the immediate threats lurking in the woods, Sirra turns his attention to the written word, translating cryptic texts and preserving the fading history of Grand Hamlet before the shadow fell across the region.",sp=0},{t="Deciphering the Hermit's Words",b="When town leadership becomes suspicious of the hermit Abercrombie living out on the lonesome hills of Duskwood, Sirra is called upon to translate the recluse's mysterious notes. His linguistic expertise allows the council to read between the lines of seemingly innocuous requests, unraveling the bizarre inquiries arriving from the haunted woods.",sp=1},{t="Tragedies of the Past",b="Beyond routine translations, Sirra plays a crucial role in shedding light on the sorrowful history of Duskwood. Inquirers seeking to understand the mysterious weathered grave in the town cemetery find Sirra to be one of the few souls who remembers the tragic downfall of the paladin Morgan Ladimore, providing travelers with the context needed to lay restless spirits to peace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sirra Von'Indi?",a="Sirra Von'Indi is a human scholar and the official historian of Darkshire. He spends his days inside the Darkshire Town Hall studying ancient arts, translating obscure languages, and keeping the town's historical records.",al={"who is sirra","sirra von'indi lore","darkshire historian"}},{q="Where can Sirra Von'Indi be found?",a="He can be found inside the Darkshire Town Hall in the settlement of Darkshire, located in central Duskwood. He is typically standing among desks and bookshelves consulting historical texts.",al={"where is sirra","sirra von'indi location","find sirra darkshire"}},{q="What role does he play with Abercrombie's note?",a="When Mayor Ello Ebonlocke suspects the eccentric hermit Abercrombie of hiding his true intentions, Sirra uses his linguistic skills to translate a strange note provided by the hermit, helping the council understand Abercrombie's odd demands.",al={"abercrombie letter translator","translate abercrombie note","sirra note translation"}},{q="What does Sirra know about Morgan Ladimore?",a="Sirra is one of the few residents in Darkshire who knows the full history of Morgan Ladimore, the fallen paladin buried in the Weathered Grave. He helps recount Ladimore's descent into madness and tragedy after the Third War.",al={"sirra weathered grave","morgan ladimore lore sirra","story of the weathered grave"}},{q="Is Sirra related to anyone in Karazhan?",a="Sirra shares his uncommon surname with Lady Catriona Von'Indi, a spectral noblewoman haunting the nearby tower of Karazhan in Deadwind Pass, suggesting his family has longstanding ties to the nobility of the region.",al={"lady catriona von'indi","von'indi family","karazhan connection"}},{q="Why does Sirra make travelers wait while translating?",a="Deciphering obscure dialects and archaic handwriting is meticulous work. Sirra often asks travelers to give him time while he cross-references references and finishes a reliable translation.",al={"why is sirra busy","wait for sirra to finish","sirra translating wait"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Mages visiting Darkshire often appreciate Sirra's academic discipline, as his focus on ancient languages and historical study mirrors the archival research practiced in the Kirin Tor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Sirra represents the surviving civic institution of Darkshire, helping maintain the heritage of the Kingdom of Stormwind in a province otherwise consumed by darkness."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","duskwood","historian","morgan ladimore","sirra","town hall","translation","von'indi","weathered grave"},rel={"subzone:darkshire-town-hall","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:251","quest:401","quest:252","npc:abercrombie","subzone:karazhan"},src={"Sirra Von'Indi"}}
E["npc:stitches"] = {t="npc",n="Stitches",z="duskwood",s="Stitches is a colossal, stitched-together undead abomination that terrorizes Duskwood. Spawning in the western reaches of the zone, the monster relentlessly marches down the main road toward Darkshire, slaughtering unwary travelers and overwhelming Night Watch checkpoints.",h="Stitches is a colossal, stitched-together undead abomination that terrorizes Duskwood.",sec={{t="The Terror of the Main Road",b="Stitches is an undead abomination assembled from harvested corpses and unholy sorcery. Appearing near Abercrombie's shack northeast of Raven Hill Cemetery, the lumbering monstrosity immediately sets out eastward along the road toward Darkshire. Imbued with immense physical strength and relentless malice, Stitches tears through any Night Watch checkpoints stationed along the thoroughfare—including the defense camp across from Vul'Gol Ogre Mound and the outpost outside the Rotting Orchard—bringing outright slaughter to unwary travelers and town defenders alike.",sp=0},{t="The Embalmer's Twisted Revenge",b="Stitches did not appear in Duskwood by mere chance; he was deliberately crafted as an instrument of retribution. Abercrombie, known to passersby only as a harmless hermit, harbored a deep grudge against Lord Ello Ebonlocke, the mayor of Darkshire. By relying on unsuspecting adventurers to collect occult reagents, tools, and materials under innocent guises, Abercrombie finalized his horrific creation. He sent Stitches as a mocking \"gift\" to Darkshire, intent on breaking the town's defenses and punishing Lord Ebonlocke.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who created Stitches?",a="Stitches was created by Abercrombie, a hermit living northeast of Raven Hill Cemetery. Abercrombie disguised himself as a harmless recluse while secretly practicing necromancy and orchestrating the abomination's construction.",al={"stitches creator","who made stitches","abercrombie stitches"},sp=2},{q="Why is Stitches marching toward Darkshire?",a="Abercrombie dispatched Stitches as a lethal 'gift' to Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke to enact revenge on the leadership of Darkshire. The abomination follows the road directly toward the town hall to butcher the Night Watch and slaughter the townsfolk.",al={"why stitches darkshire","stitches attack goal","where is stitches walking"},sp=2},{q="Can the Night Watch stop Stitches on their own?",a="No. Left alone, Stitches easily overwhelms and decimates the Night Watch checkpoints outside Vul'Gol Ogre Mound and the Rotting Orchard before reaching the gates of Darkshire. It requires concerted militia defense and traveling adventurers to bring him down.",al={"guards vs stitches","night watch beat stitches","can darkshire guards kill stitches"}},{q="Where does Stitches spawn?",a="Stitches spawns behind Abercrombie's shack, situated along the road northeast of Raven Hill Cemetery, before beginning his long, deadly march eastward across Duskwood.",al={"where does stitches spawn","stitches location","stitches start point"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Stitches poses a catastrophic threat to Darkshire's beleaguered citizens, turning the Duskwood high road into a deadly gauntlet for fresh Alliance recruits.",["class:Paladin"]="As a grotesque product of necromancy and profane flesh-crafting, Stitches represents everything the Holy Light is called upon to purge."},kw={"abomination","darkshire","ello ebonlocke","night watch","raven hill","stitches"},rel={"npc:abercrombie","npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","topic:night-watch","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:252","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","subzone:rotting-orchard"},src={"Stitches"}}
E["npc:sven-yorgen"] = {t="npc",n="Sven Yorgen",z="duskwood",s="Sven Yorgen is a grieving farmer camped along the Hushed Bank in northern Duskwood, accompanied by his companion Lars. Having survived the brutal slaughter of his family at the Yorgen Farmstead, Sven is consumed by a relentless drive to uncover who brought ruin upon his home and exact vengeance.",h="Sven Yorgen is a grieving farmer camped along the Hushed Bank in northern Duskwood, accompanied by his...",sec={{t="A Life Shattered",b="Sven was born before the First War, old enough to recall the days before the region became shrouded in gloom following Medivh's fall. For years he worked the soil at the Yorgen Farmstead in western Duskwood alongside his wife and children. That quiet existence ended in sudden violence when mysterious Dark Riders raided his homestead while he was away, butchering his family and turning the farm into a graveyard.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance from the Hushed Bank",b="Unable to return to the ruins of his home, Sven established a secluded refuge on the Hushed Bank with his friend Lars. Distrustful of outsiders, he demands proof of loyalty from travelers before sharing his burden. Sven spotted a skulking figure lurking near his devastated farmstead and became convinced this interloper was either directly responsible for the massacre or tied to the sinister horsemen who tore his world apart.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Truth",b="The shadowy figure stalking Sven's property turns out to be Jitters, an errant vagrant whose blundering inadvertently drew the Dark Riders into Duskwood in their search for the Scythe of Elune. Though Jitters did not strike the fatal blows, his actions unchained the nightmare that obliterated the Yorgen family, directing Sven's fury toward the dark forces haunting Raven Hill and the necromancer Morbent Fel.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sven Yorgen?",a="Sven Yorgen is a human farmer residing at a small camp on the northern edge of the Hushed Bank in Duskwood. After his family was massacred at their homestead, he dedicated his life to seeking retribution against those responsible.",al={"sven yorgen","who is sven","sven lore"}},{q="What happened to Sven's family?",a="While Sven was away from home, terrifying black-cloaked figures known as the Dark Riders arrived at the Yorgen Farmstead. Hunting for a powerful artifact, they mercilessly slaughtered Sven's wife and children and left the land tainted by undead.",al={"yorgen farmstead tragedy","sven family dead","what happened to sven's farm"}},{q="Why is Sven hiding in the Hushed Bank?",a="Sven abandoned his ruined farmstead after the massacre. He set up a temporary camp along the riverbank alongside Lars to stay hidden from the undead roaming western Duskwood while planning his revenge.",al={"where is sven","sven's camp","why is sven camped out"}},{q="Who is the shadowy figure Sven saw?",a="Sven does not know. He spotted a skulking figure near the ruins of his homestead and asks trustworthy travelers to help him learn who it was and whether they had a hand in his family's deaths.",al={"shadowy figure sven","who was at yorgen farmstead","shadowy figure duskwood"},sp=1},{q="Why did the Dark Riders attack Sven's farm?",a="The Dark Riders were searching Duskwood for the Scythe of Elune, an ancient artifact of immense power. Their pursuit of this relic led them directly across Sven's lands, leaving death in their wake.",al={"why dark riders attack","what were dark riders looking for","scythe of elune sven"},sp=1},{q="How long has Sven lived in Duskwood?",a="Sven is old enough to remember Duskwood before it fell into darkness, meaning he lived in the area prior to the First War when the region was still known as the bright and peaceful Grand Hamlet.",al={"sven age","how old is sven","sven before dark"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Sven represents the tragic collapse of rural life in the kingdom's frontier territories, where ordinary subjects are left undefended against dark magic and shadowy horrors.",["class:Paladin"]="Sven's heartbreak and thirst for justice offer paladins a direct duty to avenge innocent blood and purge the lingering undead raised across his family's soil."},kw={"dark riders","duskwood","hushed bank","jitters","lars","morbent fel","scythe of elune","sven yorgen","yorgen farmstead"},rel={"subzone:yorgen-farmstead","subzone:hushed-bank","npc:lars","npc:jitters","topic:dark-riders","quest:55","quest:95","quest:262"},src={"Sven Yorgen"}}
E["npc:tavernkeep-smitts"] = {t="npc",n="Tavernkeep Smitts",z="duskwood",s="Tavernkeep Smitts is the barkeep of the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. Operating at the social center of Duskwood, Smitts possesses an encyclopedic knowledge of town gossip and unsolved local tragedies. His long memory and keen eye make him an invaluable contact for anyone investigating the region's dark history.",h="Tavernkeep Smitts is the barkeep of the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire.",sec={{t="Heart of Darkshire",b="Behind the bar of the Scarlet Raven Tavern, Tavernkeep Smitts offers warm hearth fires and drink to the weary travelers, local townspeople, and nervous Night Watch guards braving Duskwood's perils. As one of the longest-standing public faces in town, Smitts hears every rumor that filters through the gloom. While other townsfolk shrink behind locked shutters, Smitts maintains a pragmatic, observant eye on everyone who passes through his door, noting unusual behavior, hurried departures, and strange patrons.",sp=0},{t="The Memory of Stalvan",b="Smitts has spent years quietly tracking the legend of Stalvan Mistmantle. When a visiting family of Stormwind nobles was butchered years ago, Smitts joined Marshal Haggard to examine the scene of the slaughter. Smitts recovered torn, muddy journal pages from the carnage, but investigators were never able to formally connect the handwriting to Stalvan at the time. Smitts held onto those faded scraps for years, convinced that the grim truth would eventually come to light.",sp=1},{t="The Shadowy Patron",b="Smitts's attentiveness extends to contemporary threats as well. When the terrified hermit Jitters took refuge in the Scarlet Raven, Smitts watched him scribbling feverishly into a personal diary before fleeing the tavern in blind panic. When an investigator recovers the abandoned journal, Smitts readily recognizes the book and points the tracker toward Raven Hill, aiding the effort to unravel the cursed events plaguing the woods.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Tavernkeep Smitts?",a="Smitts stands behind the counter on the ground floor of the Scarlet Raven Tavern, the central inn located on the town square in Darkshire.",al={"smitts location","where is tavernkeep smitts","scarlet raven barkeep"}},{q="What does Smitts know about Stalvan Mistmantle?",a="Years ago, Smitts accompanied Marshal Haggard to investigate the slaughter of visiting nobles. Smitts discovered muddy, torn pages at the scene, which he preserved. If presented with new evidence linking Stalvan to the crime, Smitts hands over the muddy journal pages so they can be delivered to Commander Althea Ebonlocke.",al={"smitts stalvan","stalvan legend smitts","muddy pages stalvan"},sp=1},{q="What does Smitts know about Jitters?",a="Jitters spent time staying at the Scarlet Raven Tavern, where Smitts observed him frantically writing in a journal before fleeing in terror. When you bring Jitters's journal back to the tavern, Smitts identifies it and directs you toward Raven Hill Cemetery to track him down.",al={"smitts jitters","jitters journal smitts","inquire at the inn smitts"},sp=1},{q="What drinks does Smitts brew or request?",a="Smitts is involved in procuring components for local concoctions, including sending adventurers into the cursed wilds for Rot Blossoms to brew a potent local mixture known colloquially as Zombie Juice.",al={"zombie juice","smitts rot blossoms","smitts brew"}},{q="Who is Marshal Haggard, and how does Smitts know him?",a="Marshal Haggard is an old veteran of the Stormwind Guard who lives in a secluded cottage in the hills. He and Smitts worked together years ago to investigate the grisly noble murders, forming a bond over the unsolved case.",al={"smitts haggard","haggard connection"}},{q="Does Smitts have any known family in Darkshire?",a="He shares a surname with Mary Smitts, who also lives in Darkshire, suggesting they are family members surviving together in the blighted town.",al={"smitts relatives","mary smitts"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers stepping out of the shadowed woods, Smitts provides not just shelter and drinks, but essential local intelligence regarding the threats haunting Duskwood.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues investigating cold cases and shadowy figures will find Smitts an ideal informant, as he notices what patrons write, when they panic, and what they leave behind."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","haggard","jitters","scarlet raven","smitts","stalvan","tavernkeep","zombie juice"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:66","quest:266","quest:453","quest:158","npc:althea-ebonlocke"},src={"Tavernkeep Smitts"}}
E["npc:viktori-prism-antras"] = {t="npc",n="Viktori Prism'Antras",z="duskwood",s="Viktori Prism'Antras is an eccentric stargazer residing in a small hillside hut overlooking Darkshire. While the town around him succumbs to dread and looming horrors, Viktori focuses intently on building a telescope to view the heavens clearly. To realize his vision, he relies on adventurous travelers to acquire intricate parts based on gnomish schematics.",h="Viktori Prism'Antras is an eccentric stargazer residing in a small hillside hut overlooking Darkshire.",sec={{t="Eyes Upon the Heavens",b="Perched up the slope just beyond the gryphon roost, Viktori Prism'Antras spends his days peering outward from the gloom of Duskwood. Amid undead incursions, ravenous spiders, and creeping shadows, his obsession lies far beyond the suffocating canopy. He dreams of building a magnificent optical telescope capable of bringing the stars into brilliant focus, offering a quiet escape from the dread that engulfs the hamlet.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Schematics and Scattered Parts",b="Constructing such a delicate apparatus is no simple matter in a cursed forest. Viktori works from blueprints provided by his gnomish friend, Cog Glitzspinner. To complete the device, he enlists passersby to track down rare lens-crafting materials and mechanical housings, ranging from finely cut glass to metal lenses scattered across perilous territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Viktori Prism'Antras?",a="Viktori is an eccentric human stargazer residing in Darkshire. Rather than concerning himself with the town's immediate political or supernatural threats, he is singularly obsessed with constructing a powerful telescope to study the stars.",al={"who is viktori","viktori prism'antras lore","viktori duskwood"}},{q="Where can I find Viktori in Darkshire?",a="He lives in a small wooden hut up the hill just past the Darkshire gryphon master, located to the right as you ascend the path.",al={"viktori prism'antras location","where is viktori","find viktori darkshire"}},{q="What is Viktori trying to build?",a="Viktori is attempting to build an astronomical telescope using blueprints drawn up by his gnomish colleague Cog Glitzspinner, which requires several specialized lenses and components to assemble.",al={"viktori telescope","look to the stars device","what does viktori make"}},{q="Why is he studying the stars from Duskwood?",a="Despite the darkness and constant terror permeating Duskwood, Viktori is consumed by celestial curiosity. Focusing on the untainted majesty of the night sky provides him an intellectual refuge from the decaying land around him.",al={"why darkshire telescope","why study stars in duskwood"}},{q="Who designed the plans for Viktori's telescope?",a="The blueprints were engineered by Cog Glitzspinner, an inventive gnome acquaintance of Viktori who provided the schematics necessary to assemble the viewing apparatus.",al={"cog glitzspinner","who made the telescope schematics"}},{q="Does Viktori help defend Darkshire?",a="No. Viktori is a civilian scholar rather than a warrior. He leaves the defense of the town to Commander Althea Ebonlocke and the Night Watch, preferring to dedicate all his energies to his astronomical work.",al={"is viktori a night watchman","does viktori fight"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Tinkers will appreciate Viktori's endeavor, as building his precision viewing instrument relies entirely on sophisticated gnomish schematics.",["race:Gnome"]="Viktori's entire project rests on the ingenuity of the gnome inventor Cog Glitzspinner, showcasing the reach of gnomish engineering even in the most desolate human towns.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting Viktori provides a rare, peaceful pursuit in Darkshire, helping an Alliance townsman seek wonder amidst pervasive tragedy."},kw={"astronomy","cog glitzspinner","darkshire","duskwood","look to the stars","prism'antras","stargazer","telescope","viktori"},rel={"zone:duskwood","subzone:darkshire","quest:174"},src={"Viktori Prism'Antras"}}
E["npc:watcher-dodds"] = {t="npc",n="Watcher Dodds",z="duskwood",s="Watcher Dodds is a human scout of the Night Watch stationed at the central crossroads of Duskwood. Manning a lonely roadside outpost far from Darkshire's town walls, he monitors the encroaching horrors and tasks travelers with culling the local giant spider population.",h="Watcher Dodds is a human scout of the Night Watch stationed at the central crossroads of Duskwood.",sec={{t="On the Crossroads Watch",b="Watcher Dodds serves the Night Watch under Commander Althea Ebonlocke, holding down an exposed post at the intersection connecting Darkshire to Raven Hill and Deadwind Pass. While Darkshire huddles within its palisades, forward sentries like Dodds live on the knife's edge between wolf packs, ravenous ghouls, and oversized arachnids. From his roadside camp, he keeps an eye on approaching threats and enlists wandering mercenaries to thin out the spiders crawling out from the undergrowth before they completely overrun the overgrown thoroughfares.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Watcher Dodds?",a="He is a human member of the Night Watch, the militia formed to defend Duskwood against the undead and beasts plaguing the region. He is stationed at the central crossroads rather than within the safety of Darkshire.",al={"watcher dodds","who is dodds","dodds duskwood"}},{q="Where can I find Watcher Dodds?",a="Dodds maintains a small roadside camp at the main crossroads in central Duskwood, where the roads between Darkshire, Raven Hill, and the southern passes diverge.",al={"watcher dodds location","where is dodds","dodds coords"}},{q="Why does he want spiders killed?",a="Giant venomous spiders infest the surrounding woods and prey upon wanderers and supply couriers using the road. Dodds relies on passing adventurers to cull the webwood brood to prevent the paths from becoming entirely impassable.",al={"eight-legged menaces","dodds spider quest","why kill spiders"}},{q="Who does Watcher Dodds report to?",a="He answers to Commander Althea Ebonlocke, the leader of the Night Watch headquartered at the town hall in Darkshire.",al={"dodds commander","who leads night watch"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers navigating Duskwood, Dodds's campfire marks one of the few safe bastions of friendly support along the dark roads between Darkshire and western lands."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","crossroads","darkshire","duskwood","night watch","spiders","watcher dodds"},rel={"npc:althea-ebonlocke","quest:245","zone:duskwood","subzone:crossroads","subzone:darkshire","quest:163"},src={"Watcher Dodds"}}
E["quest:101"] = {t="quest",n="The Totem of Infliction",z="duskwood",s="Madame Eva of Darkshire offers to craft a protective ward known as the Totem of Infliction for travelers passing through the shadowed woods. By harvesting remains from the ghouls, skeletons, and venomous spiders haunting the region, she binds their innate malice into a charm that retaliates against attackers. The task serves as both a grim test of survival and a superstitious safeguard against the pervasive darkness of Duskwood.",h="Madame Eva of Darkshire offers to craft a protective ward known as the Totem of Infliction for travelers...",sec={{t="A Fortune of Bloodshed",b="Within her candle-lit abode in Darkshire, Madame Eva peers past the veil into the fortunes of those who cross her threshold. Sensing impending danger and violence waiting patiently on the horizon, she offers more than mere divination: practical, sympathetic sorcery. By gathering ten ghoul fangs, ten skeleton fingers, and five vials of spider venom from the haunted thickets, an adventurer supplies the raw materials needed to construct a protective ward against Duskwood's ravenous predators.",sp=0},{t="Sympathetic Magic",b="The Totem of Infliction operates on the principles of sympathetic magic, turning the essence of Duskwood's horrors against themselves. Ghoul fangs steeped in necrotizing hunger, finger bones wrested from restless dead, and potent arachnid venom are woven together by Madame Eva's enchantments. When grasped in times of mortal peril, the totem radiates a magical aura designed to reflect cruelty, inflicting spiritual and physical harm upon anyone foolish enough to strike its bearer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Madame Eva?",a="Madame Eva is a fortune teller and mystic dwelling in the embattled town of Darkshire. She interprets omens and brews protective wards for locals and passing adventurers attempting to survive the supernatural perils of Duskwood.",al={"madame eva","who gives this quest","eva darkshire"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Totem of Infliction?",a="The totem is an enchanted talisman meant to ward off assailants. Held when threatened, its magic retaliates against hostile foes who attempt violent acts against the bearer, turning the dark energies of Duskwood's predators outward.",al={"totem of infliction purpose","what does totem do","totem lore"}},{q="Why does Madame Eva need ghoul fangs, skeleton fingers, and spider venom?",a="The charm relies on sympathetic sorcery. By utilizing the anatomical weapons and remains of the forest's most aggressive monsters—the bites of ghouls, the grasping claws of skeletons, and arachnid venom—Eva binds their innate malice into a protective retaliatory enchantment.",al={"why spider venom","ingredients for totem","why skeleton fingers"}},{q="Where are the components for the totem found?",a="The components are harvested from the undead and beasts infesting Duskwood. Skeletons and ghouls haunt the cemeteries and haunted orchards across the zone, while large venomous spiders nest throughout the shadowed woods.",al={"where find fangs","where to get materials","where are ghouls and spiders"}},{q="What danger does Madame Eva foresee?",a="Eva warns that whispering winds speak of a looming threat waiting in the near future, specifically telling the adventurer that she foresees widespread bloodshed on their path ahead.",al={"eva fortune","what danger coming","future bloodshed"}},{q="Is crafting the totem considered dark magic?",a="While crafting items out of corpse parts and venom edges close to shadow craft, in the desperate environment of Duskwood, folk hedge-magic and sympathetic charms are widely accepted methods of self-defense against the surrounding horrors.",al={"is this necromancy","is eva evil","dark magic totem"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="In a borderland cut off from major military reinforcement, Alliance travelers frequently rely on the folk charms and wards of local mystics like Madame Eva to endure the forest's terrors.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins may look askance at assembling wards from undead bones and spider venom, yet in the dire gloom of Duskwood, even holy warriors must sometimes reckon with pragmatic folk sorcery.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks will readily recognize the principles of retaliatory curses and sympathetic components woven into Eva's protective charm.",["class:Priest"]="While Church of the Holy Light orthodoxy emphasizes faith and devotion, hedge-witches like Madame Eva channel spiritual will through tactile, grim talismans."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","ghoul fangs","madame eva","protective ward","skeleton fingers","spider venom","totem of infliction"},rel={"npc:madame-eva","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Madame Eva",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=101},src={"The Totem of Infliction"}}
E["quest:133"] = {t="quest",n="Ghoulish Effigy",z="duskwood",s="Deep in the gloomy wilderness of Duskwood, the eccentric hermit Abercrombie claims his isolated shack is under siege by the walking dead. To protect his home, he tasks passing adventurers with harvesting ghoul ribs to assemble a bizarre protective scarecrow.",h="Deep in the gloomy wilderness of Duskwood, the eccentric hermit Abercrombie claims his isolated shack is...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Plight",b="Abercrombie lives far beyond the guarded boundaries of Darkshire, isolated amidst the shadowed trees of Duskwood. Out here, wandering ghouls like Flesh Eaters and Bone Chewers roam unchecked. Claiming that ravenous corpses recently battered down his walls, the panicked hermit requests the ribs of these horrors to fashion a deterrent, hoping a grisly effigy will keep the hungry dead at bay.",sp=0},{t="A Bizarre Defense",b="While common sense might suggest running toward the safety of the Night Watch or fortifying his wooden shack, Abercrombie insists on macabre methods. He believes erecting an effigy made from ghoul remains will frighten off other scavenging dead. Though building a scarecrow out of slaughtered undead seems unsettling, travelers in Duskwood often take the eccentric hermit at his word to earn some needed coin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Abercrombie live?",a="Abercrombie resides in a solitary shack in western Duskwood, just northeast of Raven Hill Cemetery and far from the protection of Darkshire.",al={"abercrombie location","where is abercrombies shack","hermit shack duskwood"}},{q="Why does Abercrombie need ghoul ribs?",a="Abercrombie claims packs of ghouls are pounding on his shack's walls. He intends to use the bones to craft a gruesome scarecrow effigy to frighten away scavenging undead.",al={"ghoul ribs purpose","why ghoul ribs","what is the effigy for"}},{q="Which creatures drop the Ghoul Ribs?",a="The ribs can be gathered from any of the local undead wandering Duskwood's roads and cemeteries, specifically Flesh Eaters, Bone Chewers, Brain Eaters, Rotted Ones, and Plague Spreaders.",al={"where to get ribs","ghoul rib drops","which ghouls drop ribs"}},{q="Does building an undead scarecrow actually repel ghouls?",a="Undead rarely show fear, making Abercrombie's plan dubious to seasoned monster hunters. Still, the hermit insists on his strange project, and few question a paying employer in such desperate woods.",al={"do effigies work on ghouls","ghoul scarecrow logic"}},{q="Why doesn't Abercrombie simply relocate to Darkshire?",a="Abercrombie chooses to live in isolation away from the Night Watch and town governance. Despite the obvious perils of Duskwood's wilderness, he prefers managing his shack alone with his own peculiar defenses.",al={"why live in woods","why doesn't abercrombie move","darkshire safety"}},{q="What comes next after gathering the ribs?",a="After receiving the ghoul ribs, Abercrombie finds yet another bizarre dilemma to resolve, sending adventurers further into the wild to deal with local ogres who stole his belongings.",al={"next quest","what after ghoulish effigy"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Night Watch struggles to protect the roads, leaving isolated forest dwellers like Abercrombie to rely on passing Alliance travelers for protection against the rotting Scourge remnant.",["class:Paladin"]="Hunting down Flesh Eaters and Bone Chewers cleanses the blight from Duskwood's soil, even if handing their remains to a hermit feels distinctly unsettling.",["class:Priest"]="Lending aid to a frightened hermit stranded among dark spirits is noble work, though assembling effigies from harvested remains tests one's stomach."},kw={"abercrombie","bone chewers","darkshire","duskwood","effigy","flesh eaters","ghoul rib","hermit"},rel={"npc:abercrombie","zone:duskwood","subzone:beggar-s-haunt","subzone:manor-mistmantle","subzone:darkshire","quest:938"},m={start="Abercrombie",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=133},src={"Ghoulish Effigy (Classic)"}}
E["quest:134"] = {t="quest",n="Ogre Thieves",z="duskwood",s="Abercrombie, the peculiar hermit dwelling in western Duskwood, asks travelers to venture into the ogre stronghold of Vul'Gol Ogre Mound. He claims that ogres ambushed him while he was foraging and made off with a crate filled with his irreplaceable herbs and tools.",h="Abercrombie, the peculiar hermit dwelling in western Duskwood, asks travelers to venture into the ogre...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Lost Goods",b="Isolated out along the damp roads of western Duskwood, the aged hermit Abercrombie claims he was attacked while gathering supplies in the wilderness. According to him, brutes from the southern ogre mound drove him off, forcing him to abandon a sturdy wooden crate packed with precious herbs and delicate instruments.",sp=0},{t="The Vul'Gol Threat",b="The Vul'Gol Ogre Mound in southern Duskwood is a fortified hive of hostile ogres who harass unwary wanderers and clash with Night Watch patrols like Watcher Dodds. The crate sits right near the entrance of their cavernous mound, daring outsiders to step past roaring brutes and spell-weaving magi to haul it back to the hermit.",sp=0},{t="A Slip of the Tongue",b="Upon recovering his missing goods, Abercrombie's eccentric demeanor cracks into manic excitement. He catches himself almost shouting praises to 'the Nec—' before hastily pivoting to thank the adventurer instead, eager to lock himself away and put his retrieved supplies to use in the dark.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Abercrombie?",a="Abercrombie is an eccentric, solitary hermit residing in a worn shack in western Duskwood. Though he acts frail, helpless, and in need of assistance, his frantic behavior and strange requests hint at darker, unsettling motives.",al={"abercrombie lore","who gave me this quest","who is the hermit"}},{q="Where did the ogres take Abercrombie's crate?",a="The crate was brought to the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound in southern Duskwood. It rests exposed on the dirt right outside the mouth of the ogre cave.",al={"where is the crate","crate location","vul'gol crate"}},{q="Why are there ogres in Duskwood?",a="The ogres of the Vul'Gol clan carved out a foothold in the rugged southern hills of Duskwood following the Second War. Aggressive and opportunistic, they regularly raid passersby, ambush solitary wanderers, and hoard stolen plunder around their mound.",al={"duskwood ogres","vul'gol ogres origin","why ogres here"}},{q="What is actually inside the crate?",a="Abercrombie claims the crate contains rare herbs and specialized harvesting tools he abandoned during the attack, and he is overjoyed to have them back.",al={"what did abercrombie lose","contents of crate"},sp=1},{q="What did Abercrombie almost say when receiving the crate?",a="Upon getting his crate back, Abercrombie starts to thank someone else before abruptly catching himself and thanking the adventurer instead, then gleefully looks forward to the nights ahead.",al={"thank the nec","what was abercrombie saying","abercrombie quote"},sp=1},{q="Does this quest connect to other tasks at the ogre mound?",a="Yes. Adventurers heading to the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound often combine this errand with duties from Watcher Dodds regarding the ogre threat, as well as tasks tied to Viktori Prism'Antras.",al={"ogre mound quests","quests near vulgol"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks familiar with forbidden arts will easily recognize Abercrombie's slip of the tongue as an ode to dark spellcraft rather than simple botanical zeal.",["class:Paladin"]="Abercrombie's eager, secretive delight at recovering his crate should put any servant of the Holy Light on guard against aiding the reclusive hermit blindly.",["profession:Herbalism"]="While Abercrombie claims his crate holds mere herbs, an herbalist might wonder what bizarre flora requires such desperate retrieval from an ogre mound."},kw={"abercrombie","crate","duskwood","hermit","ogre","vul'gol","watcher dodds"},rel={"npc:abercrombie","zone:duskwood","npc:watcher-dodds","npc:viktori-prism-antras"},m={start="Abercrombie",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=134},src={"Ogre Thieves (Classic)"}}
E["quest:146"] = {t="quest",n="Messenger to Darkshire",z="duskwood",s="Messenger to Darkshire concludes the desperate diplomatic correspondence between Lakeshire and Darkshire. Magistrate Solomon's plea for military reinforcement is firmly rejected by Lord Ello Ebonlocke, exposing the bitter truth that both towns have been abandoned to their fates by Stormwind.",h="Messenger to Darkshire concludes the desperate diplomatic correspondence between Lakeshire and Darkshire.",sec={{t="A Desperate Request Denied",b="Facing an onslaught of Blackrock orcs and gnolls, Magistrate Solomon of Redridge hoped his old peer in Duskwood could spare troops. But Lord Ello Ebonlocke's reaction is bordering on outrage. Darkshire is barely holding back the living dead, ravenous beasts, and cursed magic pressing in from every corner of the woods. Ebonlocke bluntly states that the Night Watch exists only because Stormwind abandoned Duskwood first. Stripping Darkshire of its defenders would ensure the settlement falls before the patrol even crosses the forest's edge.",sp=0},{t="A Pattern of Abandonment",b="When Solomon reads Ebonlocke's reply, the harsh reality of the kingdom sets in. The Stormwind Army pulled out of Westfall, left Darkshire to fend for itself, and has now ignored Lakeshire's calls for aid. Solomon is forced to confront what local leaders across the kingdom have begun whispering: this is not mere bureaucratic oversight or incompetence, but suspected treachery lurking at the heart of Stormwind itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why won't Lord Ebonlocke send the Night Watch to help Lakeshire?",a="Darkshire is besieged on all sides by undead, beasts, and foul sorcery. The Night Watch is an irregular local militia created precisely because Stormwind withdrew its garrisons. If Ebonlocke sent his guards to Redridge, Darkshire would be overrun before the troops even made it past the forest's edge.",al={"why ebonlocke refuse","why no night watch for lakeshire","darkshire refuses help"}},{q="What does Magistrate Solomon realize upon reading the response?",a="Solomon realizes that Lakeshire's plight is part of a kingdom-wide crisis. With the army having retreated from Westfall and the guard completely gone from Darkshire, Solomon suspects active treachery within Stormwind's leadership rather than simple neglect.",al={"solomon reaction","what does solomon realize"}},{q="Who formed the Night Watch?",a="The Night Watch was assembled by the beleaguered citizens and leaders of Duskwood, led by Lord Ello Ebonlocke, after Stormwind's official forces abandoned the territory to darkness and rot.",al={"night watch origins","who made night watch"}},{q="Where does Solomon go from here to get help?",a="With Darkshire refusing aid and Westfall overrun by the Defias Brotherhood, Lakeshire stands entirely alone. Solomon is forced to look closer at the palace court in Stormwind to find out why the crown refuses to protect its outlying territories.",al={"what does solomon do next","who else can help lakeshire"}},{q="Did Stormwind officially pull out of Duskwood and Westfall?",a="Yes. As dark magic corrupted Duskwood and unrest erupted in Westfall, regular Stormwind forces withdrew, leaving the frontier towns to raise local militias like the Night Watch and the People's Militia to survive.",al={"why did stormwind leave","stormwind abandoned towns"}},{q="What is the relation between Solomon and Ebonlocke?",a="They are long-standing peers and fellow magistrates governing frontier towns of the kingdom. Solomon counted on this personal relationship when asking for troops, but the sheer severity of Duskwood's perils made compliance impossible.",al={"are solomon and ebonlocke friends","solomon and ello relationship"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This dispatch exposes the deep cracks fracturing the southern kingdom, as peripheral Alliance settlements find themselves discarded and defenseless.",["race:Human"]="For human travelers, the correspondence is a sobering illustration of how isolated the towns of the realm have become while the royal court looks the other way."},kw={"darkshire","ebonlocke","lakeshire","messenger","night watch","solomon","stormwind"},rel={"quest:145","npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","npc:magistrate-solomon","topic:night-watch","subzone:darkshire","subzone:lakeshire","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-army"},m={start="Lord Ello Ebonlocke",["end"]="Magistrate Solomon",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=146},src={"Messenger to Darkshire (2)"}}
E["quest:148"] = {t="quest",n="Supplies from Darkshire",z="duskwood",s="Supplies from Darkshire is an Alliance quest in Duskwood where the hermit Abercrombie asks passing travelers to run an errand to Darkshire on his behalf. Claiming to be too frail to make the dangerous trek through the haunted forest, he seeks a rare material known as Ghost Hair Thread from Madame Eva.",h="Supplies from Darkshire is an Alliance quest in Duskwood where the hermit Abercrombie asks passing travelers...",sec={{t="A Feeble Request",b="Isolated in a shack north of Raven Hill Cemetery in western Duskwood, the hermit Abercrombie cuts a pitiful figure. When approached by travelers, he laments his old age and frail body, claiming he cannot survive the journey through the woods to purchase goods from Darkshire. His requested errand appears simple: travel back to the township's town square and speak with Madame Eva to procure a spool of Ghost Hair Thread.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Material",b="Reaching Madame Eva reveals that Abercrombie's request is far from standard sewing supplies. Madame Eva, the local diviner and spinner of strange artifacts, does not keep Ghost Hair Thread readily in stock. Fulfilling the hermit's errand requires securing raw hair from the vengeful phantoms that haunt Duskwood's cursed cemeteries, marking this simple delivery run as the start of a far more sinister arrangement.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Supplies from Darkshire?",a="The quest is given by Abercrombie, a hermit living in a lonely shack north of Raven Hill Cemetery in western Duskwood.",al={"quest giver supplies from darkshire","who starts supplies from darkshire","abercrombie errand"}},{q="Who do I speak with in Darkshire to get the supplies?",a="You must speak with Madame Eva, who resides in a house overlooking the central square in Darkshire.",al={"where to turn in supplies from darkshire","supplies from darkshire turn in","madame eva location"}},{q="What specific item is Abercrombie looking for?",a="Abercrombie asks for Ghost Hair Thread, an unusual and macabre material woven by Madame Eva.",al={"what does abercrombie want","what are the supplies","abercrombie item"}},{q="Does Madame Eva have the Ghost Hair Thread ready?",a="No, Madame Eva has none in stock when you arrive. She agrees to spin it for you, but only if you gather the spectral materials she needs from nearby spirits.",al={"does eva have thread","supplies from darkshire completion"}},{q="What quest precedes Supplies from Darkshire?",a="The prerequisite quest is The Hermit, which directs adventurers out from Darkshire to seek out Abercrombie at his lonely dwelling.",al={"prerequisite supplies from darkshire","supplies from darkshire prequest"}},{q="What quest follows Supplies from Darkshire?",a="Completing this conversation with Madame Eva immediately leads into the quest Ghost Hair Thread, tasking you with hunting restless spirits for their hair.",al={"next quest after supplies from darkshire","supplies from darkshire followup"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers seeking to assist the beleaguered settlement of Darkshire often find themselves running courier tasks for isolated hermits living along the hazardous backroads.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Woven items usually rely on linen or silk, making Madame Eva's craft of spinning ethereal hair into thread a macabre curiosity for any tailor."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","duskwood","ghost hair thread","madame eva","supplies from darkshire","the hermit"},rel={"npc:abercrombie","npc:madame-eva","quest:149","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Abercrombie",["end"]="Madame Eva",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=148},src={"Supplies from Darkshire (Classic)"}}
E["quest:149"] = {t="quest",n="Ghost Hair Thread",z="duskwood",s="Ghost Hair Thread is an errand undertaken for the fortune-teller Madame Eva in Darkshire. In order to gather spectral thread for an enchanted garment, travelers are sent south to seek out Blind Mary, a tormented spirit who dwells in an abandoned farmhouse. By presenting her with an ethereal comb, one can gather the necessary strands from her ghostly tresses.",h="Ghost Hair Thread is an errand undertaken for the fortune-teller Madame Eva in Darkshire.",sec={{t="A Fortuneteller's Request",b="Madame Eva of Darkshire requires specialized, otherworldly materials to weave a garment of protective magic. Standard threads of linen and wool will not suffice for the rituals of Duskwood; instead, she requires ethereal strands harvested directly from a spirit. To secure this macabre component without violence, Eva provides a delicate Spectral Comb capable of passing through the veil of death to gather loose spectral hair.",sp=0},{t="The Sorrow of Blind Mary",b="South of Darkshire, tucked away in the shadowy hills, lies an abandoned farmstead haunted by the wailing apparition known as Blind Mary. Consumed by self-loathing, the spirit constantly laments her hideous appearance and screams at intruders to avert their eyes, having torn out her own eyes in anguish before or upon her death. The gift of the Spectral Comb offers her a fleeting moment of comfort, coaxing her to groom her ghostly hair despite her unending torment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Blind Mary?",a="Blind Mary is a sorrowful ghost haunting a derelict farmhouse in the hills south of Darkshire. Driven mad by despair and perceived ugliness, she tore out her own eyes so she would never have to see herself again. Despite her lack of sight, she remains acutely and agonizingly aware of anyone looking at her.",al={"blind mary lore","who is mary duskwood","spectral comb woman"}},{q="Why does Madame Eva need ghost hair?",a="Madame Eva requires strands of ghost hair to spin spectral thread. In the haunted environment of Duskwood, mundane craft supplies are often inadequate, and she relies on occult components to complete her rituals and protective enchantments.",al={"why ghost hair","what is ghost hair thread for","madame eva hair thread"}},{q="Where can Blind Mary's house be found?",a="Her ruined homestead sits in the hills directly south of Darkshire, past the town cemetery and surrounded by the prowling horrors and undead that plague the darkened woods.",al={"where is blind mary","blind mary location","farmhouse south of darkshire"}},{q="How does the Spectral Comb work on a spirit?",a="Crafted or enchanted for the unseen world, the Spectral Comb can interact with intangible apparitions. It glides through spiritual matter just as a physical comb passes through living hair, collecting dropped strands that retain an ethereal form.",al={"how does spectral comb work","spectral comb lore","comb ghost hair"}},{q="Is Blind Mary hostile to travelers?",a="No. Despite her terrifying screams and weeping, Blind Mary is not hostile toward living visitors. Her anguish is turned entirely inward, though the surrounding woods and nearby structures harbor many aggressive creatures and undead.",al={"will blind mary attack","is blind mary dangerous"}},{q="What happens after giving Mary the comb?",a="Once Mary uses the comb, she returns it tangled with her spectral hair. Adventurers must bring the comb back to Madame Eva in Darkshire so she can spin the strands into ghost hair thread.",al={"what next ghost hair","return the comb quest","after ghost hair thread"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Spinning thread from the incorporeal remains of a ghost is a rare occult technique far removed from standard spinning wheels and looms.",["class:Priest"]="Witnessing a spirit who gouged out her own eyes out of spiritual torment illustrates the profound tragedy and lingering shadows that afflict Duskwood's restless dead.",["faction:Alliance"]="The tragic specters haunting the farms around Darkshire serve as a reminder of how quickly prosperous Grand Hamlet fell to darkness and isolation."},kw={"blind mary","darkshire","duskwood","farmhouse","ghost","ghost hair thread","madame eva","spectral comb"},rel={"npc:blind-mary","npc:madame-eva","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Madame Eva",["end"]="Blind Mary",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=149},src={"Ghost Hair Thread (Classic)"}}
E["quest:154"] = {t="quest",n="Return the Comb",z="duskwood",s="Return the Comb is an Alliance errand in Duskwood that concludes the haunting transaction with the spirit Blind Mary. After being presented with a comb to harvest strands of her spectral hair, the tortured ghost is overcome with despair over her lost beauty and casts the implement away. Returning the hair-laden comb to Madame Eva allows the mystic to spin the ethereal thread needed for an enchanted ceremonial shroud.",h="Return the Comb is an Alliance errand in Duskwood that concludes the haunting transaction with the spirit...",sec={{t="A Bitter Reflection",b="Blind Mary lingers in a decrepit shack south of Darkshire, eternally mourning her tragic death and changed state. When approached with Madame Eva's comb, the reminder of mundane grooming only deepens her sorrow. Realizing she is now nothing more than an apparition—a monster stripped of mortal grace whom no one will ever love again—she recoils in horror, thrusting the comb and the ghostly hair tangled in its teeth back into the traveler's hands.",sp=0},{t="Weaving the Supernatural",b="Madame Eva awaits the return of the comb in Darkshire, well aware of the macabre nature of the task. With the ghostly hair secured, the fortune teller possesses the rare spiritual medium necessary to spin a spool of Ghost Hair Thread. Eva utilizes these ethereal fibers to craft warding garments and fabrics capable of channeling subtle enchantments, paying travelers for any stray hairs left over from the delicate spinning process.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Blind Mary react with horror to the comb?",a="The comb reminds Blind Mary of her mortal life and beauty. Seeing herself reduced to a withered, spectral form causes an outburst of grief, driving her to reject the comb and lament that she has become a monster whom no one will ever cherish again.",al={"why is mary upset","why did blind mary scream","mary comb reaction"}},{q="What does Madame Eva do with the hair on the comb?",a="Madame Eva weaves the strands collected in the comb into Ghost Hair Thread, a mystical crafting component with supernatural properties used to stitch enchanted garments.",al={"why ghost hair","what does eva do with ghost hair","madame eva thread"}},{q="Where is Blind Mary located?",a="Blind Mary haunts an abandoned, dilapidated shack located just south of Darkshire, near Tranquil Gardens Cemetery in Duskwood.",al={"where is blind mary","blind mary location"}},{q="Who is Madame Eva?",a="Madame Eva is a mysterious human mystic and diviner residing in Darkshire. She provides fortune readings, cryptic guidance, and crafts magical trinkets and reagents for those navigating the perils of Duskwood.",al={"who is madame eva","eva darkshire"}},{q="What follows after returning the comb to Madame Eva?",a="Once Madame Eva takes the comb and prepares the spool of Ghost Hair Thread, she asks you to deliver the completed thread to Abercrombie, the hermit dwelling near Raven Hill Cemetery.",al={"what comes next","next quest after return the comb"},sp=1},{q="Why does Madame Eva give you coins upon completion?",a="Eva notes that the comb yielded more than enough ghostly hair to weave the spool of thread required, and she compensates you with a few coins to buy out the surplus strands for her own use.",al={"why do i get coins","extra strands money"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="The spinning of Ghost Hair Thread highlights the eerie crafts of Duskwood, demonstrating that spectral material can be harvested and carded into durable supernatural textiles.",["class:Priest"]="Witnessing Blind Mary's agonizing self-loathing offers a bleak study in the torment of unsettled spirits who remain bound to the mortal world through grief rather than malice.",["faction:Alliance"]="Navigating the gloomy roads between Darkshire and Mary's desolate home exposes travelers to the pervasive decay gripping the heart of Duskwood."},kw={"blind mary","darkshire","duskwood","ghost hair","ghost hair thread","madame eva","return the comb"},rel={"quest:149","npc:blind-mary","npc:madame-eva","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Blind Mary",["end"]="Madame Eva",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=154},src={"Return the Comb (Classic)"}}
E["quest:156"] = {t="quest",n="Gather Rot Blossoms",z="duskwood",s="Tavernkeep Smitts of Darkshire requires rot blossoms to concoct a batch of his infamous 'zombie juice'. These macabre flora sprout directly from the decaying skulls of skeletal horrors and fiends prowling Duskwood's restless graveyards.",h="Tavernkeep Smitts of Darkshire requires rot blossoms to concoct a batch of his infamous 'zombie juice'.",sec={{t="A Bizarre Ingredient",b="While most barkeeps pride themselves on aged ales and fine wines, Tavernkeep Smitts of the Scarlet Raven Tavern occasionally brews more unsettling fare. His recipe for 'zombie juice' demands rot blossoms—foul, necrotic vegetation that takes root within the empty skulls of animated skeletons. Smitts himself is sensible enough never to get close to the undead, leaving the gruesome harvest to passing mercenaries.",sp=0},{t="Graveyard Pest Control",b="Gathering these blooms requires cutting down the skeletal horrors and fiends wandering the overgrown plots of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery or the vast expanse of Raven Hill Cemetery. Duskwood's local militia, the Night Watch, is perpetually stretched thin fighting back the creeping terrors of the woods. Smitts ensures that any adventurer braving the tombstones is duly commended to Commander Althea Ebonlocke for culling the restless dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a rot blossom?",a="A rot blossom is a foul plant that sprouts in conditions steeped in dark magic and decay. In Duskwood, they grow directly inside the cranial cavities of animated skeletal horrors and fiends.",al={"rot blossom","what is rot blossom","where do rot blossoms come from"}},{q="Why does Tavernkeep Smitts need rot blossoms?",a="Smitts uses the blossoms as a key component to brew a concoction known as 'zombie juice', a potent drink requested by certain patrons in the region.",al={"why smitts want blossoms","zombie juice ingredients","smitts drink"}},{q="Where can the skeletons bearing these blossoms be found?",a="Skeletal horrors and skeletal fiends congregate throughout the burial grounds of Duskwood, particularly within Tranquil Gardens Cemetery near Darkshire and across the vast Raven Hill Cemetery to the west.",al={"where are skeletal horrors","rot blossom location","tranquil gardens skeletons"}},{q="Does this task help the defense of Darkshire?",a="Yes. Darkshire relies on the Night Watch for survival against constant undead attacks. Smitts notes that hunting skeletons for the blossoms assists Commander Althea Ebonlocke by thinning the ranks of monsters threatening the town.",al={"night watch help","althea ebonlocke skeleton killing"}},{q="What comes next after delivering the blossoms?",a="Once Smitts receives the blossoms and brews the zombie juice, he asks you to deliver the finished draught to Abercrombie, an eccentric hermit dwelling near Raven Hill Cemetery.",al={"next quest after rot blossoms","juice delivery follow up"},sp=1},{q="Is zombie juice a normal beverage served in Darkshire?",a="No. The Scarlet Raven Tavern typically serves standard regional fare. Zombie juice is a bizarre, specialized brew prepared only when Smitts receives an eccentric order requiring necrotic ingredients.",al={"is zombie juice normal","scarlet raven drinks"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Unlike standard herbs that flourish in rich soil and sunlight, rot blossoms are dark botanical anomalies rooted entirely in necromantic decay and animated bone.",["faction:Alliance"]="Hunting the undead in Duskwood's cemeteries offers much-needed relief to the beleaguered Night Watch of Darkshire, who fight a daily battle to keep the town from falling."},kw={"darkshire","night watch","raven hill cemetery","rot blossom","skeletal fiend","skeletal horror","tavernkeep smitts","tranquil gardens cemetery","zombie juice"},rel={"quest:158","npc:tavernkeep-smitts","subzone:tranquil-gardens-cemetery","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","npc:althea-ebonlocke","topic:night-watch","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Tavernkeep Smitts",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=156},src={"Gather Rot Blossoms (Classic)"}}
E["quest:157"] = {t="quest",n="Deliver the Thread",z="duskwood",s="Deliver the Thread is an Alliance errand in Duskwood that ferries a spool of Ghost Hair Thread from Madame Eva in Darkshire across the haunted forest to Abercrombie. The eccentric hermit living near Raven Hill Cemetery claims he needs the enchanted thread to ward his ramshackle hut against restless spirits. However, Madame Eva's dark remarks about the thread hint that there may be far more sinister uses for it.",h="Deliver the Thread is an Alliance errand in Duskwood that ferries a spool of Ghost Hair Thread from Madame...",sec={{t="A Crossing in the Dark",b="Once Madame Eva finishes spinning spectral hair gathered from the ghost Blind Mary, she entrusts the Ghost Hair Thread to any traveler willing to carry it west. The journey requires crossing the shadowed expanse of Duskwood, slipping past lurking spiders and roaming undead to reach Abercrombie's dilapidated shack just north of the vast cemetery grounds.",sp=0},{t="Threads of Life and Death",b="Abercrombie insists he needs the woven spectral strand to line his windows and doorframe to keep out the wailing dead of Raven Hill. Yet Madame Eva lets slip that ghost hair thread has a thousand uses: binding malevolent spirits, but also sewing semblance of life into dead and inanimate matter. The hermit greets the spool with immense delight, eager to set his hidden craft in motion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is ghost hair thread?",a="It is an enchanted spool spun by Madame Eva in Darkshire using hair gathered from the ghost Blind Mary. According to Eva, it possesses powerful occult properties, capable of binding spirits or sewing life into inanimate objects.",al={"ghost hair","what is the thread","ghost thread"}},{q="Who is Abercrombie?",a="Abercrombie is a reclusive old man dwelling in a lonely shack just north of Raven Hill Cemetery. He presents himself as a harmless, frail recluse who is perpetually terrified of the undead prowling near his home.",al={"hermit","who is abercrombie","shack guy"}},{q="Why does Abercrombie claim he needs the thread?",a="Abercrombie tells visitors that he intends to string the ghost hair along his windows and doorways. He claims its spiritual properties will act as a ward to keep out the unwanted ghouls and spirits wandering Duskwood.",al={"why thread","abercrombie excuse","warding spirits"}},{q="Where is Abercrombie located?",a="He lives in an isolated wooden shack situated north of the main grounds of Raven Hill Cemetery, just off the western road running through Duskwood.",al={"abercrombie location","where is the shack","hermit shack"}},{q="What happens after giving the thread to Abercrombie?",a="Once Abercrombie receives the thread, he rewards the courier and immediately begins complaining of other pressing needs, sending travelers on further errands for odd alchemical ingredients like Zombie Juice.",al={"next quest","what comes after","after deliver thread"}},{q="Does Madame Eva know what Abercrombie is up to?",a="Eva does not directly accuse Abercrombie of foul play, but her cryptic parting words note that ghost hair can be used to sew life into inanimate objects. She seems well aware of the thread's necromantic potential, even if she fulfills the order without protest.",al={"does eva know","madame eva complicit","eva warning"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Spinning spectral hair into viable spools is no ordinary weaving; it blends needlecraft with hedge necromancy, crafting material capable of stitching matter beyond the physical realm.",["class:Priest"]="Warding one's home against the restless dead usually calls for holy rites of the Light; relying on woven remnants of the dead themselves suggests Abercrombie treads a far darker path.",["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire's fragile safety depends on vigilance, and sending aid across the monster-infested western woods to an isolated hermit strains the Night Watch's stretched frontier."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","deliver the thread","duskwood","ghost hair thread","madame eva","raven hill","raven hill cemetery","zombie juice"},rel={"quest:149","npc:abercrombie","npc:madame-eva","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","zone:duskwood","quest:163","topic:light"},m={start="Madame Eva",["end"]="Abercrombie",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=157},src={"Deliver the Thread (Classic)"}}
E["quest:158"] = {t="quest",n="Zombie Juice",z="duskwood",s="Zombie Juice is an errand run on behalf of Abercrombie, the peculiar hermit dwelling in the haunted wilds of Duskwood. Claiming to suffer from the oppressive midnight chill, he dispatches travelers to Darkshire's tavern to secure an unusually potent concoction.",h="Zombie Juice is an errand run on behalf of Abercrombie, the peculiar hermit dwelling in the haunted wilds of...",sec={{t="A Chilly Request",b="Dwelling alone among the horrors of the shadowed woods, the hermit Abercrombie frequently sends sympathetic travelers on strange errands. Claiming that the creeping dusk drains his warmth and vitality, he asks that an adventurer make the trek east to Darkshire. His target is Tavernkeep Smitts of the Scarlet Raven Tavern, from whom he seeks a bottle of a potent, ominously named brew known as Zombie Juice to put fire back in his veins.",sp=0},{t="At the Scarlet Raven",b="Darkshire's tavern sees plenty of weary guards and frightened townsfolk, but requests for Zombie Juice are rare even for Tavernkeep Smitts. The drink carries a reputation for being dangerously strong. While Smitts recognizes the vintage, Abercrombie's thirst for such a morbid concoction raises quiet eyebrows in a region already besieged by the restless dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Zombie Juice?",a="It is an exceptionally strong, morbidly named liquor sold by Tavernkeep Smitts at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. It is rarely requested by ordinary patrons.",al={"zombie juice drink","what is the liquor","zombie juice lore"}},{q="Who sends you to fetch Zombie Juice?",a="The hermit Abercrombie, who lives isolated in a shack in western Duskwood, asks travelers to fetch it to help warm his cold bones.",al={"who gives quest zombie juice","abercrombie quest drink","hermit drink request"}},{q="Where do you turn in the quest?",a="You speak with Tavernkeep Smitts inside the Scarlet Raven Tavern, the central inn of Darkshire in eastern Duskwood.",al={"where is smitts","turn in zombie juice","smitts location"}},{q="Why does Abercrombie want it?",a="Abercrombie claims the gloomy, shadowed nights of Duskwood leave him shivering and that he needs the fiery drink to warm his blood.",al={"why does abercrombie need juice","abercrombie cold","why does he drink zombie juice"}},{q="Is Tavernkeep Smitts surprised by the order?",a="Yes. Smitts notes that Zombie Juice is extraordinarily potent stuff and mentions that he does not usually receive requests for it from his regular clientele.",al={"smitts reaction","does smitts have zombie juice","smitts dialogue"}},{q="Does this quest involve fighting any monsters?",a="No. The errand itself simply requires traveling along the road from Abercrombie's secluded hut to Darkshire and speaking with Tavernkeep Smitts, though the roads of Duskwood are always fraught with wandering beasts and undead.",al={"zombie juice combat","is zombie juice dangerous","zombie juice mobs"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers working to support the embattled outpost of Darkshire often find themselves serving as couriers for the eccentric recluses sheltering along Duskwood's perilous roads."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","duskwood","liquor","scarlet raven tavern","tavernkeep smitts","zombie juice"},rel={"npc:abercrombie","npc:tavernkeep-smitts","subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Abercrombie",["end"]="Tavernkeep Smitts",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=158},src={"Zombie Juice (Classic)"}}
E["quest:159"] = {t="quest",n="Juice Delivery",z="duskwood",s="Juice Delivery is an errand running between Darkshire and the western edge of Duskwood. Tavernkeep Smitts entrusts you with a potent concoction known as Zombie Juice to deliver to the reclusive hermit, Abercrombie. While ostensibly meant to keep the shivering old man warm, the brew's uncanny potency raises eyebrows.",h="Juice Delivery is an errand running between Darkshire and the western edge of Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Dubious Concoction",b="Tavernkeep Smitts of Darkshire brews a legendary draught known colloquially as Zombie Juice. When the order is finally filled, Smitts hands over the bottle with a stern warning to handle it gingerly, remarking that the concoction is stout enough to raise the dead. For a tired adventurer running errands across a haunted forest, delivering high-proof moonshine to an eccentric loner feels like routine charity.",sp=0},{t="The Hermit's Slip",b="Carrying the volatile brew west past the howling worgen and restless dead leads straight to Abercrombie's shack on the edge of the woods. Upon receiving the bottle, the frail recluse claims he requires the liquor merely to warm his aching bones through Duskwood's freezing, fog-choked nights. Yet upon taking possession of it, he nearly thanks the traveler for their 'foolishness' before quickly correcting himself to praise their 'kindness'—a momentary lapse that hints there is far more brewing in the hermit's mind than a simple evening drink.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Zombie Juice?",a="Zombie Juice is an extremely potent brew crafted by Tavernkeep Smitts at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. While treated as a strong alcoholic drink, Smitts notes that the brew is potent enough to wake the dead, making it far more volatile than ordinary spirits.",al={"zombie juice lore","what is smitts juice","abercrombie drink"}},{q="Who orders the Zombie Juice?",a="The delivery is requested by Abercrombie, an eccentric old hermit living in a lonely shack out near the western boundary of Duskwood.",al={"who wants the juice","who is juice delivery for"}},{q="Why does Abercrombie want the drink?",a="Abercrombie claims he needs the drink to keep him warm during the bitterly cold, damp nights in Duskwood. However, his slip of the tongue when receiving the bottle hints he has far more sinister designs for the concoction.",al={"why does abercrombie need juice","abercrombie cold"}},{q="Who brews the Zombie Juice?",a="Tavernkeep Smitts, the barkeep running the Scarlet Raven Tavern in the heart of Darkshire, brews the drink personally once provided with the necessary pungent ingredients.",al={"who makes zombie juice","smitts barkeep"}},{q="Where is Abercrombie's shack?",a="Abercrombie's shack sits isolated in western Duskwood, northwest of the cemetery hills and just east of the mountain pass leading toward Westfall.",al={"abercrombie location","where is abercrombie shack"}},{q="What does Abercrombie do next after receiving the juice?",a="Once he secures the Zombie Juice, Abercrombie continues imposing on gullible travelers, sending them into Raven Hill Cemetery to gather ghoul ribs for a ghoulish effigy he claims will keep the undead away.",al={"next quest after juice delivery","what happens next"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire's citizens rely on brave Alliance couriers to traverse the peril-filled roads of Duskwood, though trusting every hermit in the woods can lead to unforeseen trouble.",["profession:Cooking"]="Tavernkeep Smitts' recipe for Zombie Juice leans heavily on pungent, unconventional ingredients, testing the limits of what passes for a tavern beverage."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","duskwood","juice delivery","scarlet raven","tavernkeep smitts","zombie juice"},rel={"quest:158","npc:abercrombie","npc:tavernkeep-smitts","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Tavernkeep Smitts",["end"]="Abercrombie",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=159},src={"Juice Delivery (Classic)"}}
E["quest:160"] = {t="quest",n="Note to the Mayor",z="duskwood",s="Note to the Mayor is an Alliance errand in Duskwood that links the eccentric hermit Abercrombie to the leadership of Darkshire. After aiding the reclusive old man, adventurers are asked to hand-deliver a personal message to Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke. However, the missive immediately stirs suspicion rather than warmth.",h="Note to the Mayor is an Alliance errand in Duskwood that links the eccentric hermit Abercrombie to the...",sec={{t="A Friendly Message?",b="After helping Abercrombie recover his stolen chest from the ogres of the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound, the hermit sends you back down the mist-shrouded roads toward town. Cackling with delight, Abercrombie claims that he and Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke are old friends. He insists that upon discovering what the adventurer has accomplished, the mayor will be just as thrilled as he is.",sp=0},{t="Puzzled Leadership",b="Upon arriving at the town hall in Darkshire, the reality contradicts Abercrombie's claims. Lord Ello Ebonlocke has no recollection of anyone named Abercrombie. Unfolding the parchment only deepens the mystery: far from a heartfelt greeting between old companions, the text is inscribed in an ancient, unreadable script that leaves Darkshire's mayor thoroughly baffled.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends the Note to the Mayor?",a="Abercrombie, an eccentric hermit dwelling in a solitary shack on the western edge of Duskwood, hands you the letter after you recover his stolen possessions from the local ogres.",al={"who gives note to the mayor","who starts note to the mayor","abercrombie letter sender"}},{q="Are Abercrombie and Mayor Ebonlocke actually friends?",a="No. While Abercrombie claims they are old acquaintances, Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke has never heard of him and expresses utter bewilderment at receiving the message.",al={"do they know each other","is abercrombie friends with the mayor","abercrombie ello ebonlocke relationship"}},{q="What is written in the note?",a="The note is written in an ancient, obscure language that neither the courier nor Mayor Ebonlocke can decipher, prompting the mayor to seek outside translation.",al={"what does abercrombie note say","can ello read the note","what language is the letter"}},{q="Where is Lord Ello Ebonlocke located?",a="Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke is located inside the Darkshire Town Hall, on the east side of town along the main road in Duskwood.",al={"where is the mayor","ello ebonlocke location","where do i turn in note to the mayor"}},{q="What happens after Mayor Ebonlocke receives the letter?",a="Because Lord Ebonlocke cannot read the mysterious script, he asks you to seek out someone who can interpret the text, leading to the quest Translate Abercrombie's Note.",al={"what is next after note to the mayor","what follows note to the mayor"}},{q="Why was Abercrombie laughing when he gave you the letter?",a="Abercrombie's gleeful laughter hints that his intentions are far darker than a simple reunion with an old acquaintance, foreshadowing sinister trouble for Darkshire.",al={"why does abercrombie laugh","is abercrombie evil","abercrombie laugh note"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire's survival depends on unraveling strange disturbances before they breach the Night Watch's perimeter, making this suspicious letter an immediate security concern for Alliance agents.",["race:Human"]="Human couriers serving the Night Watch and the House of Ebonlocke quickly realize that the odd old hermit on the outskirts of Duskwood has deceived them."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","duskwood","ello ebonlocke","letter","mayor","note to the mayor"},rel={"npc:abercrombie","npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","quest:251","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Abercrombie",["end"]="Lord Ello Ebonlocke",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=160},src={"Note to the Mayor (Classic)"}}
E["quest:163"] = {t="quest",n="Raven Hill",z="duskwood",s="Reports of shifting shadows and flickering window light in the abandoned settlement of Raven Hill have set the Night Watch on edge. Dispatched by Elaine Carevin in Darkshire, travelers are sent west across the haunted woods to confront whatever sinister presence has taken shelter among the ruins.",h="Reports of shifting shadows and flickering window light in the abandoned settlement of Raven Hill have set...",sec={{t="Eyes in the West",b="To the rangers of the Night Watch, the far western edge of Duskwood has long been surrendered to the dead and the wilderness. Yet complete abandonment would be preferable to unexpected activity. Calor, a watcher patrolling the gloomy roads, noticed movement among the silent houses of Raven Hill two nights in a row, punctuated by the unsettling flicker of a lantern in a window. In a land plagued by ghouls, skeletons, and beasts, any unexplained signs of life demand immediate investigation.",sp=0},{t="A Rattled Hermit",b="Those expecting to clash with an emergent demon or undead warlord inside Raven Hill find a far more pathetic reality. Huddled in terror amid the dilapidated ruins is Jitters, a thoroughly unhinged vagabond trembling at every rustle in the dark. While he frantically protests that there is no threat besides 'harmless Jitters,' his manic rambling suggests that he knows far more about the nightmare consuming Duskwood than he dares to say.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to investigate Raven Hill?",a="Elaine Carevin, a resident in Darkshire who assists the Night Watch, asks travelers who care about Duskwood's safety to check out the disturbing sightings reported from the west.",al={"who gives raven hill quest","quest giver raven hill","elaine carevin quest"}},{q="What did Calor actually see in Raven Hill?",a="Calor reported seeing moving shadows in the abandoned settlement two nights in a row, as well as a lantern or candle burning in one of the building windows the night before that.",al={"what did calor see","calor sighting raven hill","shadows in raven hill"}},{q="What monster is haunting the ruins?",a="That is exactly what you are sent to discover. Calor has only glimpsed moving shadows and a light in a window; whatever lurks in the derelict buildings of Raven Hill must be found in person.",al={"who is haunting raven hill","what is in raven hill","is raven hill monster real"},sp=1},{q="Who is Jitters?",a="Jitters is a jumpy, paranoid vagrant living on the edge of terror in western Duskwood. While he claims to be completely harmless, his extreme guilt and frantic ramblings hint that he is tangled up in the region's darker mysteries.",al={"jitters lore","who is jitters duskwood","why is jitters hiding"},sp=1},{q="Where is Raven Hill located?",a="Raven Hill lies in the far western section of Duskwood, situated just south of the massive, undead-infested cemetery that shares its name.",al={"raven hill location","where to find raven hill","raven hill map"}},{q="Why is the Night Watch so concerned about moving shadows?",a="Darkshire is stretched thin against skeletal uprisings, feral worgen, and lurking spiders. Any sign of organized movement or strange inhabitants in the abandoned west could signal an impending assault on the remaining living settlements.",al={"why care about raven hill","night watch raven hill"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Night Watch of Duskwood receives little to no aid from Stormwind's garrison, forcing them to rely on traveling Alliance heroes to investigate ominous threats in the ruined corners of the territory.",["class:Paladin"]="Trained to hunt the restless undead that plague the neighboring cemetery, a paladin investigating reports of sinister haunting may find the whimpering, flesh-and-blood Jitters to be an unexpected discovery."},kw={"calor","darkshire","duskwood","elaine carevin","jitters","night watch","raven hill"},rel={"zone:duskwood","npc:jitters","npc:calor","topic:light"},m={start="Elaine Carevin",["end"]="Jitters",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=163},src={"Raven Hill (quest)"}}
E["quest:164"] = {t="quest",n="Deliveries to Sven",z="duskwood",s="Deliveries to Sven is an Alliance task given by Elaine Carevin in Darkshire, requesting that vital provisions be carried out to a lonely camp on the northwest frontier of Duskwood. There, Sven Yorgen and his few remaining followers wage a desperate, solitary struggle against the horrors of the blighted woods. The errand connects town folk struggling in the gloom with an isolated band on the edge of the wilderness.",h="Deliveries to Sven is an Alliance task given by Elaine Carevin in Darkshire, requesting that vital provisions...",sec={{t="A Lifeline to the Wilderness",b="While Darkshire barely holds its own walls against wolves, spiders, and the restless dead, some refuse to cower behind palisades. Sven Yorgen and a meager handful of companions established a solitary encampment along the northwestern perimeter of Duskwood. So pressed are they by constant danger that they cannot spare a single man to make the perilous trek back to town for provisions. Elaine Carevin steps in to coordinate aid, relying on brave travelers to ensure these frontier fighters do not starve.",sp=0},{t="The Carevin Connection",b="The Carevin family holds high regard for Sven, viewing his fierce stand as true devotion to the Light. Elaine's willingness to organize and dispatch supplies highlights the quiet networks of survival that keep Duskwood from completely collapsing into shadow. When Sven receives the crate, he recognizes the enduring support of the Carevins, though his thoughts remain consumed by the grim battle at hand.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sven Yorgen?",a="Sven Yorgen is a frontiersman who keeps an armed camp on the northwestern edge of Duskwood. Viewed by figures like Elaine Carevin as an upright fighter doing the work of the Light, Sven and his small band struggle against the myriad terrors that plague the surrounding forests.",al={"who is sven","sven lore","sven yorgen info"}},{q="Why does Sven need supplies brought to him?",a="Sven's band is critically small and constantly on guard against surrounding threats. They cannot spare even a single person to make the dangerous journey to Darkshire and back, leaving them entirely reliant on sympathetic townsfolk and passing couriers for sustenance.",al={"why can't sven get supplies","sven supplies","why delivery"}},{q="Who provides the supplies?",a="Elaine Carevin provides the supplies from Darkshire. Her family maintains a close relationship with Sven and holds his dedication in high esteem, regularly arranging aid to support his encampment.",al={"who sends supplies","elaine carevin","carevin family"}},{q="Where is Sven's camp located?",a="Sven's camp lies tucked against the northwestern mountains of Duskwood, situated far past the road and north of the blighted farmland, directly on the borderland wilderness.",al={"where is sven","sven location","sven camp"}},{q="Is this delivery mandatory before helping Sven further?",a="No. While Elaine Carevin offers this task to direct travelers toward Sven, adventurous travelers who discover Sven's camp independently can aid him directly without carrying Elaine's crate.",al={"is deliveries to sven required","do i need deliveries to sven","deliveries prerequisite"}},{q="What does Sven do after receiving the delivery?",a="Sven expresses sincere gratitude for the Carevin family's support, but his mind immediately shifts toward the dire threats menacing his camp and family history, seeking capable fighters to aid his vengeance.",al={"what happens next","after deliveries to sven","sven next quest"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Outlying sentinels like Sven represent the Alliance's frayed reach in Duskwood, where survival hinges on voluntary couriers rather than regular garrison supply lines.",["class:Paladin"]="Elaine speaks of Sven as a man doing the true work of the Light, making this supply run an act of solidarity with a brother under siege.",["race:Human"]="The Carevins and Sven's followers demonstrate the stubborn grit of Stormwind's rural folk, refusing to abandon Duskwood despite its unrelenting gloom."},kw={"carevin","darkshire","duskwood","elaine carevin","light","supplies for sven","sven yorgen"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","quest:95","zone:duskwood","quest:1042","topic:light"},m={start="Elaine Carevin",["end"]="Sven Yorgen",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=164},src={"Deliveries to Sven"}}
E["quest:165"] = {t="quest",n="The Hermit",z="duskwood",s="Concerned by the prolonged absence of an elderly recluse, Elaine Carevin in Darkshire asks travelers to check on him. The lonely old man, Abercrombie, lives in a rickety shack perched right on the edge of Raven Hill Cemetery.",h="Concerned by the prolonged absence of an elderly recluse, Elaine Carevin in Darkshire asks travelers to check...",sec={{t="A Neighborly Check-In",b="In a beleaguered settlement like Darkshire, it is easy to lose track of eccentric loners until their absence becomes alarming. Elaine Carevin recalls an old man who once regularly trekked into town for provisions before abruptly vanishing from sight. Given the relentless dangers haunting the roads of Duskwood, she directs wandering adventurers to inspect his shack overlooking the haunted expanse of Raven Hill Cemetery to make sure he hasn't met a grim fate.",sp=0},{t="The Recluse of Raven Hill",b="Reaching the lonely hut reveals that its resident, an old man named Abercrombie, is still among the living. He chuckles softly at the mention of the Carevins, claiming that his long absence is merely the consequence of advancing age and the treacherous monsters prowling the woods. Relieved to find an able traveler at his door, Abercrombie wastes no time in asking whether they might run a few helpful errands for him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this errand?",a="Elaine Carevin, a resident of Darkshire in Duskwood, starts the task out of concern for an old hermit who used to purchase supplies in town.",al={"who gives the hermit","where to start the hermit","elaine carevin quest"}},{q="Where is the hermit located?",a="Abercrombie lives inside a dilapidated wooden shack situated at the northern edge of Raven Hill Cemetery in western Duskwood.",al={"where is abercrombie","hermit location duskwood","shack near raven hill"}},{q="Why was Elaine Carevin worried about him?",a="Abercrombie used to visit Darkshire regularly to buy supplies, but stopped appearing entirely. With wild beasts and undead roaming the roadways, she feared he might have perished.",al={"why check on abercrombie","why is elaine worried","what happened to the old man"}},{q="Is Abercrombie actually in danger when you find him?",a="No. When you arrive at his shack, Abercrombie is alive, well, and quietly amused by the town's concern, explaining that the dangerous roads and his old age simply made travel too burdensome.",al={"is abercrombie ok","is the hermit dying","did the hermit get attacked"}},{q="Why does someone choose to live right next to Raven Hill Cemetery?",a="Abercrombie claims to prefer the seclusion, though living in the shadow of one of the most necromantically corrupted graveyards in the Eastern Kingdoms strikes many travelers as unsettling.",al={"why live by raven hill","abercrombie cemetery shack","why is the hermit near graves"}},{q="What does Abercrombie ask for once you reach him?",a="Abercrombie is eager to take advantage of having an able-bodied adventurer at his doorstep, immediately requesting assistance with various errands and tasks around the woods.",al={"what does abercrombie want","hermit followup quest","what comes after the hermit"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Night Watch struggles to protect the roads between Darkshire and Raven Hill, leaving remote recluses like Abercrombie entirely cut off from the safety of town.",["race:Human"]="The Carevin family represents the enduring neighborly ties of Duskwood, watching out for eccentric community elders even as their region falls into shadow."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","duskwood","elaine carevin","raven hill cemetery","shack","the hermit"},rel={"npc:abercrombie","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","zone:duskwood","quest:163"},m={start="Elaine Carevin",["end"]="Abercrombie",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=165},src={"The Hermit (Classic)"}}
E["quest:173"] = {t="quest",n="Worgen in the Woods",z="duskwood",s="Calor, a disillusioned former guardsman stationed in Darkshire, tasks adventurers with culling the sinister Nightbane Shadow Weavers prowling Duskwood. By taking the hunt to Brightwood Grove and the Rotting Orchard, outsiders can prove their mettle to Master Jonathan Carevin's monster hunters.",h="Calor, a disillusioned former guardsman stationed in Darkshire, tasks adventurers with culling the sinister...",sec={{t="A Private Vigil",b="The Night Watch struggles constantly against the undead, spiders, and outlaws pressing against Darkshire's borders. For some, like Calor, the official guard proved too slow and complacent to cleanse the land. Leaving the Watch behind, Calor threw in his lot with Master Jonathan Carevin, dedicating his blade to the total eradication of heresy and corruption. But Carevin does not accept just anyone into his circle; those seeking to aid their cause must first prove they can survive against the woods' most ferocious horrors.",sp=0},{t="The Nightbane Lurkers",b="The proving ground lies in Brightwood Grove and the blighted Rotting Orchard, where feral lupine beasts known as worgen hold dominion. Among them, the Nightbane Shadow Weavers harness dark magics to blind and ensnare their victims before tearing them apart. Calor sends aspiring hunters to cut down these spell-weaving beasts, both to test an outsider's resolve and to thin out a threat whose origins remain deeply unsettling to Darkshire's defenders.",sp=0},{t="Monsters from Nowhere",b="While wolf-men have become an inescapable nightmare in Duskwood, their presence defies explanation. Calor notes that the worgen seemed to appear out of thin air, with no natural lineage in the region. Unlike the ravenous feral wolves or the walking corpses risen from local barrows, these bipedal predators wield bizarre and alien sorceries. Slaying the Shadow Weavers demonstrates martial skill, but it only skims the surface of an unnatural infestation taking root across the forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Calor?",a="Calor is a hunter and former member of Darkshire's Night Watch. Having grown frustrated with the town militia's cautious bureaucracy, he joined Master Jonathan Carevin to actively hunt down the foul creatures threatening Duskwood.",al={"calor","calor darkshire","who gives worgen in the woods"}},{q="Why does Calor want Nightbane Shadow Weavers killed?",a="Calor uses the Nightbane Shadow Weavers as a trial of skill and courage. Anyone wishing to aid Master Carevin's mission must demonstrate that they can hunt dangerous spell-weaving worgen rather than just talking about defending the town.",al={"why kill shadow weavers","worgen in the woods goal"}},{q="Where are the Nightbane Shadow Weavers found?",a="They prowl two primary areas west and southwest of Darkshire: the twisted trees of Brightwood Grove and the abandoned, overgrown grounds of the Rotting Orchard.",al={"where are nightbane shadow weavers","shadow weaver location"}},{q="Where did the worgen in Duskwood come from?",a="Their sudden appearance is a mystery to the people of Duskwood. As Calor observes, the beasts seemed to materialize out of nowhere, bringing dark shadow magic and ravenous fury to a forest already on the brink of collapse.",al={"worgen origin duskwood","why are worgen in duskwood","where do worgen come from"}},{q="Who is Master Carevin?",a="Master Jonathan Carevin is an independent monster hunter based in Darkshire. He and his followers operate outside the Night Watch, focusing aggressively on exterminating evil, undead, and bizarre monstrosities across the region.",al={"carevin","master carevin","who is master carevin"}},{q="Why did Calor leave the Night Watch?",a="Calor became disillusioned with what he saw as the Night Watch's passivity and complacency. Rather than manning perimeter fences while the dark closed in, he preferred Carevin's proactive approach to hunting evil.",al={"why did calor leave the watch","calor night watch"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire feels entirely abandoned by Stormwind's high seat, leaving townspeople and vigilantes like Calor to recruit any roaming Alliance adventurer capable of holding back the monsters.",["race:Human"]="For humans from Elwynn or Westfall, witnessing the tragic ruin of Duskwood's farms like the Rotting Orchard serves as a grim warning of what unchecked dark magic can do to a kingdom's breadbaskets.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunting the Nightbane tests tracking and beast lore to the extreme, as worgen are neither natural wildlife nor simple human outlaws, but bipedal horrors wielding shadow spells."},kw={"brightwood grove","calor","carevin","darkshire","duskwood","nightbane","rotting orchard","shadow weaver","worgen"},rel={"npc:calor","zone:duskwood","subzone:brightwood-grove","subzone:rotting-orchard","subzone:darkshire","topic:worgen"},m={start="Calor",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=173},src={"Worgen in the Woods (Classic)"}}
E["quest:174"] = {t="quest",n="Look To The Stars",z="duskwood",s="Look To The Stars begins Viktori Prism'Antras's endeavor to gaze past the eerie canopy of Duskwood. Believing that a scientific answer beyond arcane superstition explains the forest's dark curse, Viktori recruits you to gather components for a telescope designed by his gnomish associate.",h="Look To The Stars begins Viktori Prism'Antras's endeavor to gaze past the eerie canopy of Duskwood.",sec={{t="Searching the Skies",b="Amid the gloom and fear shrouding Darkshire, Viktori Prism'Antras takes a distinctly unconventional view of Duskwood's misfortune. Rather than attributing the land's corruption purely to black magic, curses, or restless dead, Viktori suspects that greater truths await high above the canopy. With the aid of blueprints drawn up by his gnomish partner, Cog, he sets out to build an optical device capable of peering into the heavens.",sp=0},{t="A Matter of Engineering",b="To commence assembly on the stargazing apparatus, Viktori needs a sturdy frame. Following Cog's specifications, he asks travelers to procure a machined bronze tube. This first step relies directly on the ingenuity of mortal mechanics rather than spellcraft, highlighting Viktori's stubborn insistence that practical craft and observation might shed light where mysticism has failed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Viktori Prism'Antras?",a="Viktori Prism'Antras is a scholarly resident of Darkshire. Unlike many locals paralyzed by fear or consumed by superstition, he seeks rational explanations for the corruption overtaking Duskwood by studying the stars.",al={"viktori","who gives look to the stars","viktori prismantras"}},{q="Why does Viktori want to build a telescope?",a="Viktori believes there is a tangible truth beyond magic that explains Duskwood's strange transformation. He hopes peering through a telescope into the skies will reveal insights that local legends and spellcasters have overlooked.",al={"why look at stars","why bronze tube duskwood","telescope quest darkshire"}},{q="Who is Cog?",a="Cog is a gnomish engineer and friend of Viktori. He drew up the mechanical blueprints required to construct the stargazing device.",al={"cog gnome","who designed telescope"}},{q="Where does one obtain a bronze tube?",a="A bronze tube is typically crafted by engineers with moderate experience. Travelers who are not engineers themselves often acquire one through trade, auction houses, or from traveling engineering peddlers who happen to carry spare stock.",al={"how to get bronze tube","bronze tube location","where find bronze tube"}},{q="Is this part of a longer questline?",a="Yes. This task is the opening step of a multi-part effort to assemble and calibrate Viktori's stargazing apparatus in Darkshire.",al={"look to the stars chain","how many look to the stars quests"}},{q="Why is Viktori looking for natural explanations in Duskwood?",a="While the forest crawls with the undead and dark enchantments, Viktori believes fundamental cosmic or natural laws might still govern the transformation, driving him to seek answers in celestial study.",al={"why scientific explanation duskwood","magic vs science duskwood"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The entire undertaking hinges on gnomish design and skilled metalwork, offering tinkerers a direct role in aiding Viktori's astronomical pursuits.",["race:Gnome"]="Viktori relies on the ingenuity of his gnomish associate, Cog, demonstrating how gnomish craft brings order and reason even to the darkest corners of the kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="While Night Watch patrols fend off horrors along the roads of Darkshire, Viktori's project represents the town's small, stubborn hope to understand what poisoned their home."},kw={"bronze tube","cog","darkshire","duskwood","look to the stars","telescope","viktori prism'antras"},rel={"npc:viktori-prism-antras","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Viktori Prism'Antras",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=174},src={"Look To The Stars (Classic)"}}
E["quest:175"] = {t="quest",n="Look To The Stars",z="duskwood",s="Following the blueprints provided by the tinker Cog, Viktori Prism'Antras seeks a reflective surface to assemble his observatory telescope in Darkshire. He directs travelers to southern Duskwood to locate Mary, a local woman remembered for carrying a looking glass.",h="Following the blueprints provided by the tinker Cog, Viktori Prism'Antras seeks a reflective surface to...",sec={{t="A Reflective Surface",b="Having secured a bronze tube for his telescope, Viktori Prism'Antras turns to the next requirement outlined in Cog's blueprints: a reliable mirror to direct and reflect light through the device. Rather than forging fine silvered glass from scratch amidst the shortages plaguing Darkshire, Viktori recalls Mary, a local resident known across the region for always carrying a looking glass.",sp=0},{t="Searching the South",b="Mary's former residence lies deep in southern Duskwood, just north of the haunted Tranquil Gardens Cemetery. Seeking her out takes adventurers past the safe patrol borders of the Night Watch and into blighted groves teeming with ravenous wolves, feral spiders, and wandering undead.",sp=0},{t="A Tragic Resident",b="Reaching Mary's humble southern shack reveals the bleak reality of Duskwood's fall. The woman Viktori remembered is no longer a living resident, but Blind Mary—a wandering spirit lingering near her old dwelling and the nearby cemetery, tethered to the memories and possessions of her former life.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Viktori Prism'Antras building?",a="Viktori is constructing an astronomical telescope at the tower in Darkshire, working off designs drawn up by a tinker named Cog.",al={"viktori telescope","look to the stars project","what is viktori making"}},{q="Why does Viktori need a looking glass?",a="Cog's optical blueprints require a mirror to reflect and focus light through the telescope housing. Viktori remembers Mary carrying a looking glass and hopes to acquire it for the assembly.",al={"why need mirror","reflective surface telescope"}},{q="Where can Mary be found?",a="Mary resides in a ruined home in southeastern Duskwood, situated just north of the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.",al={"where is mary","mary location duskwood","find blind mary"}},{q="Who is Mary?",a="Mary was a resident of southern Duskwood before the land fell into cursed darkness, well known around Darkshire for always carrying a looking glass. What became of her is something you must discover at her old home near Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.",al={"who is blind mary","blind mary backstory"},sp=1},{q="Does Mary still have her looking glass?",a="When approached, Mary acknowledges that she once owned a looking glass, though she no longer has it and can only point you toward where it went.",al={"does mary have mirror","blind mary looking glass"},sp=1},{q="What dangers surround Mary's cottage?",a="The southeastern woods and the adjacent Tranquil Gardens Cemetery crawl with hostile undead, feral duskbats, venom web spiders, and rabid wolves that prey upon travelers venturing south of Darkshire.",al={"hazards near mary","tranquil gardens cemetery threats"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Viktori build his telescope offers a rare glimmer of curiosity and progress in a town otherwise consumed by terror and rot.",["profession:Engineering"]="Telescope assembly relies on precise optical specifications, borrowing from gnomish blueprints to mirror and magnify faint starlight."},kw={"blind mary","darkshire","duskwood","look to the stars","looking glass","mary","telescope","tranquil gardens","viktori prism'antras"},rel={"npc:viktori-prism-antras","npc:blind-mary","zone:duskwood","subzone:tranquil-gardens-cemetery","topic:light","quest:174"},m={start="Viktori Prism'Antras",["end"]="Blind Mary",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=175},src={"Look To The Stars (2)"}}
E["quest:177"] = {t="quest",n="Look To The Stars",z="duskwood",s="This quest sends adventurers to recover Blind Mary's discarded looking glass for the astronomer Viktori Prism'Antras. The fragile mirror fell into the hands of an Insane Ghoul that wanders the desolate Tranquil Gardens Cemetery in southern Duskwood.",h="This quest sends adventurers to recover Blind Mary's discarded looking glass for the astronomer Viktori...",sec={{t="A Relic of Better Days",b="Before the creeping gloom overran Grand Hamlet and turned her into a weeping spirit, Blind Mary treasured an ornate looking glass. Following the horrific incident that claimed her sight and sanity, she cast the keepsake into the dirt behind her family barn. The reflective mirror is exactly what Viktori Prism'Antras needs to build his grand telescope in Darkshire, but it was snatched away into the shadows long before the astronomer dreamed of studying the heavens.",sp=0},{t="The Graveyard Scavenger",b="The mirror was scavenged by an Insane Ghoul that prowled behind the ruined farmsteads. Driven south by restless hunger, the wretched undead creature carried the looking glass into the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery, haunting an abandoned chapel amid the overgrown tombstones. Reclaiming the delicate lens means navigating the flesh-eating horrors that infest the southern woods to pry Mary's lost treasure from rotting claws.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Viktori need Mary's looking glass?",a="Viktori Prism'Antras is assembling a powerful telescope atop the town hall in Darkshire. He requires high-quality reflective lenses and mirrors to channel the dim starlight, and Mary's prized heirloom fits the precise optical requirements for his invention.",al={"viktori mirror","why looking glass","what is the mirror for"}},{q="Who is the Insane Ghoul that stole the mirror?",a="The Insane Ghoul is a scavening undead fiend that gathered trinkets from the abandoned homesteads near Mary's house. It fled south and took refuge in the ruined chapel inside the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.",al={"where is the insane ghoul","who has the looking glass","ghoul in chapel"}},{q="Why did Blind Mary throw her looking glass away?",a="Mary prized her looking glass until 'the incident' that took her sight, tore her mind, and bound her as a restless shade. After that calamity, she could no longer bear to look upon it or hold it, discarding it in despair behind her barn.",al={"why did mary throw it away","blind mary mirror","mary looking glass incident"}},{q="Where is the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery?",a="The Tranquil Gardens Cemetery lies in the southeastern reaches of Duskwood, south of the main road. Once a peaceful burial ground for Grand Hamlet, it is now infested with aggressive ghouls, skeletons, and carrion beasts.",al={"tranquil gardens location","where is cemetery"}},{q="Who is Cog?",a="Cog is a gnome tinkerer residing in Darkshire. Viktori relies on Cog's engineering expertise to evaluate and assist in constructing the delicate mechanisms of his star-viewing machine.",al={"who is cog","viktori cog"}},{q="What happens after returning the mirror to Viktori?",a="With the reflective device in hand, Viktori is thrilled with the progress of the apparatus. He then moves forward with the final stage of assembling his telescope, asking for one last crucial component to finish the lens system.",al={"look to the stars next quest","what comes next"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate Viktori's improvised optical mechanics, turning ordinary polished hand mirrors into reflective components for an astronomical instrument.",["class:Priest"]="Priests walking the tainted soil of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery witness the horrific indignity suffered by Duskwood's dead, where fallen villagers are reduced to insane scavengers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering lost town relics from the hands of ravenous undead highlights the bitter fate of Duskwood's people, abandoned on the dangerous fringes of the Kingdom of Stormwind."},kw={"blind mary","cog","darkshire","insane ghoul","look to the stars","mary's looking glass","telescope","tranquil gardens cemetery","viktori prism'antras"},rel={"quest:174","npc:viktori-prism-antras","npc:blind-mary","subzone:tranquil-gardens-cemetery","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:1599"},m={start="Blind Mary",["end"]="Viktori Prism'Antras",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=177},src={"Look To The Stars (3)"}}
E["quest:181"] = {t="quest",n="Look To The Stars",z="duskwood",s="This quest marks the final chapter in Viktori Prism'Antras's endeavor to assemble a stargazing device in Darkshire. With the telescope structure otherwise built, Viktori sends travelers to the dangerous Vul'Gol Ogre Mound to retrieve a lens large enough for his contraption: a monocle worn by the ogre Zzarc'Vul.",h="This quest marks the final chapter in Viktori Prism'Antras's endeavor to assemble a stargazing device in...",sec={{t="The Final Piece",b="Throughout the construction of his stargazing telescope, Viktori Prism'Antras has relied on plans drafted by the gnome engineer Cog Glitzspinner. While brass tubes and sturdy mountings could be scavenged or assembled from local supplies, the apparatus required an exceptionally massive focusing lens. Standard magnifying glasses and optical components from Stormwind traders simply lacked the diameter called for by Cog's ambitious design, leading Viktori to look toward an unlikely and perilous alternative.",sp=0},{t="The Ogre's Eyepiece",b="In the shadow of the southern hills lies the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound, an encampment swarming with hostile brute-kin. Among them dwells Zzarc'Vul, a singular ogre known for wearing a glass monocle large enough to serve as the observatory lens. Striking deep into the mound and taking the eyepiece from Zzarc'Vul fulfills Cog's schematics, allowing Viktori to finish his telescope and peer into the heavens above the shadowed canopy of Duskwood.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Viktori Prism'Antras?",a="Viktori Prism'Antras is an astronomer and scholar living in a hut up the hill in Darkshire. Despite the gloom shrouding Duskwood, he remains dedicated to completing his observatory telescope to study the stars.",al={"who is viktori","viktori prism'antras"}},{q="Where can I find Zzarc'Vul?",a="Zzarc'Vul resides in the southern reaches of Duskwood within the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound. He prowls around the mound's camp and cave network, requiring searchers to navigate through heavily guarded ogre territory to find him.",al={"zzarc'vul location","where is the ogre","ogre monocle location"}},{q="Why does an ogre possess a monocle?",a="While ogres are not widely celebrated for their academic pursuits or fine optics, Zzarc'Vul carries an oversized monocle. Its unusual proportions make it the only lens in the region massive enough to fit Cog's telescope plans.",al={"why ogre monocle","ogre's monocle lore"}},{q="What happens once the device is completed?",a="Securing the monocle allows Viktori to fit the final optic into place. With the telescope fully assembled, Viktori can resume his astronomical studies unobstructed by the bleak forest ground below.",al={"telescope finished","quest conclusion"}},{q="Who designed the telescope?",a="The blueprints for the device were provided by an engineer named Cog, whose complex design called for specialized parts, metal framing, and a lens far larger than standard dwarven or gnomish spectacles.",al={"cog blueprints","who built telescope"}},{q="Is Vul'Gol Ogre Mound safe to enter alone?",a="No. The Vul'Gol Ogre Mound is densely populated by hostile ogres that often patrol in packs or guard narrow paths. Venturing deep into the mound to locate Zzarc'Vul poses significant danger to solitary travelers.",al={"vul'gol difficulty","ogre mound safe"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire clings to fragile survival against horrors and beasts, making Viktori's pursuit of celestial knowledge an enduring, if eccentric, beacon of civilian perseverance.",["race:Gnome"]="The contraption relies on schematics drawn up by gnomish craftsmanship, demanding ingenious field improvisations like converting brute eyewear into precision optics.",["profession:Engineering"]="Mages and tinkers alike appreciate the audacity of substituting a massive ogre monocle to satisfy the focal requirements of an astronomical lens."},kw={"cog","darkshire","look to the stars","monocle","telescope","viktori prism'antras","vul'gol ogre mound","zzarc'vul"},rel={"npc:viktori-prism-antras","subzone:vul-gol-ogre-mound","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:174"},m={start="Viktori Prism'Antras",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=181},src={"Look To The Stars (4)"}}
E["quest:221"] = {t="quest",n="Worgen in the Woods",z="duskwood",s="As the Nightbane pack encroaches further upon Darkshire, Calor tasks adventurers with striking down the pack's primary rank-and-file stalkers. These ferocious Dark Runners have overrun the nearby Rotting Orchard, threatening to completely surround the besieged town.",h="As the Nightbane pack encroaches further upon Darkshire, Calor tasks adventurers with striking down the...",sec={{t="A Tightening Perimeter",b="While scouts first encountered lone worgen weaving shadowy magic on the fringes of the forest, Calor's rangings revealed a far more urgent tactical threat. Larger, swifter beasts known as Nightbane Dark Runners have massed in the Rotting Orchard just southwest of Darkshire. Rather than merely lurking beneath the canopy, these predators form the bulk of the pack's numbers, establishing a staging ground within striking distance of the village gates.",sp=0},{t="An Inexhaustible Tide",b="Culling the Dark Runners temporarily blunts the pack's offensive, but it offers little peace of mind to the Night Watch. Calor notes with growing dread that every beast felled seems instantly replaced by another prowling the mists. The supernatural resilience and sheer replenishment rate of the Nightbane leave the town's defenders bewildered, forcing them to look to veteran monster hunters like Master Jonathan Carevin to uncover whatever foul catalyst summoned these alien horrors to Duskwood.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are Nightbane Dark Runners?",a="Nightbane Dark Runners are larger, physically imposing worgen that constitute the primary front-line forces of the pack haunting Duskwood. Unlike the mystical Shadow Weavers, Dark Runners rely on raw speed, claws, and sheer predatory ferocity.",al={"dark runners","what are dark runners","nightbane dark runner"}},{q="Where is the Rotting Orchard located?",a="The Rotting Orchard lies just southwest of Darkshire. Once productive farmland, it has devolved into a corrupted, blighted clearing that the Nightbane pack seized as a forward foothold near the town.",al={"rotting orchard location","where is rotting orchard"}},{q="Who is Calor?",a="Calor is a ranger and member of the Night Watch stationed in Darkshire. He scouts the outskirts of the settlement, tracking the aggressive movements of the worgen packs that threaten the town's survival.",al={"who is calor","calor duskwood","calor questgiver"}},{q="Why do the worgen numbers seem endless to the defenders?",a="The defenders do not yet understand the supernatural nature of the worgen presence. They believe an evil power is actively summoning or drawing the beasts into Duskwood, causing fresh waves to appear as quickly as the existing ones are slain.",al={"why so many worgen","inexhaustible worgen","where do worgen come from"}},{q="Who is Master Carevin?",a="Master Jonathan Carevin is a seasoned hunter and marksman stationed in Darkshire. The Night Watch places immense trust in his expertise to track down the root cause behind the monstrous infestations plaguing the region.",al={"master carevin","jonathan carevin","who is carevin"}},{q="How does this task fit into the defense of Darkshire?",a="Darkshire is an isolated settlement with dwindling supplies and no aid from Stormwind. Clearing the Rotting Orchard prevents the Nightbane pack from staging direct, overwhelming ambushes on the town's southwest perimeter.",al={"why kill dark runners","darkshire defense"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Duskwood has received virtually no reinforcement from the Stormwind crown, forcing local volunteer militias like the Night Watch to rely entirely on traveling Alliance heroes to thin out encroaching predator packs.",["class:Hunter"]="The rapid encroachment of unnatural bipedal wolves at the Rotting Orchard offers hunters a grim lesson in dealing with otherworldly beasts whose instincts defy the natural ecology of Azeroth."},kw={"calor","carevin","dark runner","darkshire","duskwood","night watch","nightbane","rotting orchard","worgen"},rel={"npc:calor","subzone:rotting-orchard","subzone:darkshire","topic:worgen","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Calor",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=221},src={"Worgen in the Woods (Classic, 2)"}}
E["quest:222"] = {t="quest",n="Worgen in the Woods",z="duskwood",s="As the Nightbane pack tightens its grip on Duskwood, Calor directs adventurers to strike against their deadliest ranks. Taking the fight directly to their southern dens and mines, defenders push back the feral threat encroaching on Darkshire.",h="As the Nightbane pack tightens its grip on Duskwood, Calor directs adventurers to strike against their...",sec={{t="A Feral Foothold",b="The worgen infestation haunting Duskwood is far from mindless chaos. Having carved out territory in the dark expanse south of Darkshire, the beasts known as the Nightbane have begun establishing fortified camps. Calor watches their bonfires flicker in the distance with growing dread, noting that the creatures have occupied deep caves and abandoned mining shafts. Among them, the Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones represent the most vicious breeds, displaying ferocious savagery and a tenacity that threatens to overwhelm the town's perimeter.",sp=0},{t="Calor's Endorsement",b="Calor serves as the watchful frontline recruiter for Darkshire's defense, though he harbors few illusions about the terrifying nature of the lupine invaders. Breaking the back of the Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones tests the mettle of any hero. Those who succeed in culling these hardened packs earn more than mere coin; they earn Calor's respect and a personal recommendation to Master Carevin, the reclusive figure coordinating the broader offensive against the worgen scourge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones located?",a="These dangerous breeds of the Nightbane pack congregate around caves and the mine in the southern reaches of Duskwood, often gathered around visible bonfires.",al={"where are tainted ones","where are vile fangs","worgen locations duskwood"}},{q="Who is Calor?",a="Calor is a dedicated resident of Darkshire who monitors the worgen threat in the woods and enlists capable adventurers to stem the creatures' advance.",al={"calor darkshire","who gives worgen in the woods 3"}},{q="Who is Master Carevin?",a="Master Carevin is a seasoned hunter in Darkshire who coordinates efforts to eradicate the worgen threat from the surrounding region.",al={"master carevin","carevin duskwood"}},{q="Why do the worgen have bonfires?",a="Despite their monstrous, wolf-like appearance, the Nightbane worgen exhibit an unsettling intelligence, gathering in organized camps, using fire, and holding fortified positions like mines.",al={"why do worgen make fires","nightbane bonfires"}},{q="What happens after completing this hunt?",a="Impressing Calor earns you a letter of recommendation, sending you directly to Master Carevin to aid him in the next phase of the hunt.",al={"next quest after worgen in the woods 3","worgen in the woods follow up"}},{q="Why is Darkshire so concerned about these specific worgen?",a="The Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones are among the most lethal and aggressive members of the pack. Leaving them unchecked near the southern mines risks letting the beasts overrun the surrounding roads entirely.",al={"why nightbane vile fang","vile fang danger"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire stands isolated in the gloomy south of the kingdom; clearing the southern caves helps protect the fragile supply lines and remaining homesteads of Duskwood.",["class:Hunter"]="The cunning shown by the Nightbane pack makes them unnatural prey, demanding vigilance from trackers venturing near their darkened dens."},kw={"calor","carevin","darkshire","duskwood","nightbane","tainted one","vile fang","worgen"},rel={"npc:calor","topic:worgen","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","topic:light"},m={start="Calor",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=222},src={"Worgen in the Woods (Classic, 3)"}}
E["quest:223"] = {t="quest",n="Worgen in the Woods",z="duskwood",s="This errand delivers Calor's letter of recommendation to Jonathan Carevin in Darkshire, concluding your pursuit of the savage worgen haunting Duskwood. Impressed by your prowess against the beastly invaders, Calor points you directly to a man fighting deeper threats among the shadows.",h="This errand delivers Calor's letter of recommendation to Jonathan Carevin in Darkshire, concluding your...",sec={{t="A Rare Recommendation",b="Having culled the Nightbane pack stalking Roland's Doom and the shadowed glades, you earn the hard-won respect of Calor. Stationed on the darkened frontiers of the woods, Calor is rarely eager to hand out compliments, let alone formal introductions. Handing over a faded scrap of parchment, he directs you to deliver his word directly to Jonathan Carevin in Darkshire, remarking that if they had more fighters of your caliber, their small cohort might finally eclipse the town's beleaguered Night Watch.",sp=0},{t="Carevin's Vigil",b="Jonathan Carevin operates within Darkshire under tremendous strain, wary of outsiders and perpetually pressed for time. The town faces onslaughts not only from slavering worgen, but also from unresting undead, shadowy demonic forces, and traitorous cultists aiding the corruption from within. Receiving Calor's glowing endorsement breaks Carevin's cold demeanor, confirming you as a trustworthy blade dedicated to preserving the Light against the suffocating terrors of Duskwood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="Calor sends you on this errand. Having observed your success against the voracious worgen packs throughout Duskwood, he provides you with a faded note of recommendation to carry to his associate, Jonathan Carevin.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","calor"}},{q="Who is Jonathan Carevin?",a="Jonathan Carevin is a grim, highly focused resident of Darkshire who coordinates efforts against the supernatural evils menacing the town. While wary of strangers, he works alongside trusted figures like Calor to root out undead, demons, and the sympathizers aiding them.",al={"carevin","who is carevin","master carevin"}},{q="Why is Calor so dismissive of the Night Watch?",a="Calor hints that the town's official Night Watch is struggling and stretched too thin to handle the variety of horrors invading Duskwood. He believes a few capable, dedicated fighters working outside the formal bureaucracy can achieve far more against the encroaching shadows.",al={"calor night watch","outnumber the night watch","why compete with night watch"}},{q="What threats does Carevin warn about upon delivery?",a="Upon reading the recommendation, Carevin warns that Darkshire faces threats on all fronts: ravenous worgen, wandering undead, invading demons, and insidious cultists or sympathizers providing them aid. He cautions you to remain ever-vigilant and trust only proven allies.",al={"carevin enemies","what does carevin say","what are we fighting"}},{q="Does this quest require any combat?",a="No. This final step is entirely a delivery mission. After enduring the dangerous hunts against the Nightbane worgen across Duskwood in the earlier parts of the chain, this task merely requires bringing Calor's note safely to Carevin in Darkshire.",al={"any fighting","do i kill anything","delivery only"}},{q="Where can I find Jonathan Carevin?",a="Jonathan Carevin can be found inside the town of Darkshire in Duskwood, attending to urgent matters regarding the town's precarious defense.",al={"carevin location","where is carevin","where to turn in"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="With the Kingdom of Stormwind failing to spare soldiers for Duskwood's borderlands, independent Alliance adventurers and vigilantes like Carevin represent the town's only line of defense.",["class:Paladin"]="Carevin greets proven allies with invocations of the Holy Light, seeking holy champions willing to stand firm against Duskwood's rampant unholy evils.",["class:Priest"]="Carevin's parting blessing of 'Glory under the Light' echoes the desperate faith held by Darkshire's remaining defenders in the face of unending dark corruption."},kw={"calor","calor's note","darkshire","duskwood","jonathan carevin","night watch","worgen in the woods"},rel={"npc:calor","npc:jonathan-carevin","topic:night-watch","zone:duskwood","quest:56","topic:light"},m={start="Calor",["end"]="Jonathan Carevin",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=223},src={"Worgen in the Woods (Classic, 4)"}}
E["quest:226"] = {t="quest",n="Wolves at Our Heels",z="duskwood",s="Wolves at Our Heels is an Alliance quest offered by Lars at Sven's Camp in western Duskwood. Tasked with hunting the rabid and starving dire wolves stalking the surrounding woods, travelers help clear immediate wilderness threats so Sven and Lars can focus on their vendetta against the necromancer Morbent Fel.",h="Wolves at Our Heels is an Alliance quest offered by Lars at Sven's Camp in western Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Precarious Camp",b="Tucked away along the western hills of Duskwood near the Westfall border, Sven Yorgen and his companion Lars maintain an isolated outpost. Living away from Darkshire leaves them entirely reliant on their own foraging and hunting to survive. However, carrying fresh game through these dark woods makes Lars an irresistible target for the ravenous predators stalking the shadowed riverbanks and underbrush.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Woods",b="The local packs of starving and rabid dire wolves roam primarily to the north and east of the camp toward the river. By culling these frenzied beasts, travelers lift an immediate siege on Lars's hunting efforts. Thinning out the wolves frees both men from constantly fighting for their daily bread, allowing them to turn their full attention toward the necromancer Morbent Fel, who lurks further east.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lars?",a="Lars is a rugged survivalist aiding Sven Yorgen at a small camp nestled in the hills of western Duskwood. He handles the camp's daily hunting and foraging while Sven obsesses over vengeance against the dark forces threatening the region.",al={"lars","who gives wolves at our heels","quest giver lars"}},{q="Where are the wolves prowling?",a="The dire wolves roam the forests directly north and east of Sven's Camp, especially along the banks of the river that divides Duskwood from the zones to the north.",al={"wolf location","where are rabid dire wolves","where are starving dire wolves"}},{q="Why are the dire wolves so aggressive?",a="Duskwood's wilderness has deteriorated under an encroaching shadow. Game is scarce, driving the dire wolves into near starvation, and disease or dark corruption has left many of them rabid and recklessly violent toward anyone carrying fresh meat.",al={"why are wolves attacking","rabid wolves duskwood"}},{q="Who is Morbent Fel?",a="Morbent Fel is a powerful necromancer practicing dark arts from the cemetery and mounds to the east. Sven and Lars hold a bitter grudge against him and are preparing to take him down once their basic survival needs are met.",al={"morbent fel","the necromancer","who is the necromancer to the east"}},{q="What are the Flash Bundles Lars gives as a reward?",a="Flash Bundles are crafted incendiary devices made by the townsfolk of Darkshire. Sympathetic residents donated them to Sven's camp to aid his struggle against the undead and beasts infesting the woods.",al={"flash bundles","lars reward","what is flash bundle"}},{q="Why don't Sven and Lars live in Darkshire?",a="Sven's family suffered a tragedy that turned him into an embittered, driven vigilante. Rather than sheltering behind the Night Watch in Darkshire, Sven and Lars stationed themselves in the wild to stalk the evils plaguing the woods firsthand.",al={"why live in a camp","svens camp location","why not in town"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Taming or culling Duskwood's warped wildlife demands acute awareness; these dire wolves are far more desperate and vicious than ordinary forest beasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Lars stabilizes Sven's remote camp, securing an allied staging ground against the undead forces plaguing western Duskwood."},kw={"dire wolf","duskwood","flash bundles","lars","morbent fel","rabid dire wolf","starving dire wolf","sven","sven's camp"},rel={"npc:lars","quest:230","quest:55","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Lars",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=226},src={"Wolves at Our Heels (Classic)"}}
E["quest:230"] = {t="quest",n="Sven's Camp",z="duskwood",s="Sven's Camp is an Alliance quest in Duskwood that uncovers a crucial clue regarding the tragedy at the Yorgen homestead. By unearthing a buried, untitled journal from a mound of loose dirt on the abandoned farm, adventurers piece together who witnessed the slaughter of Sven Yorgen's family.",h="Sven's Camp is an Alliance quest in Duskwood that uncovers a crucial clue regarding the tragedy at the Yorgen...",sec={{t="A Clue in the Dirt",b="Sven Yorgen was driven from his home by dark riders, returning only to find his family murdered and his farm in ruins. Consumed by grief and vengeance, he sent allies to search the wreckage of the homestead. Hidden beneath a mound of freshly turned earth, a small, dirt-stained book lay buried, abandoned in the chaos.",sp=0},{t="A Silent Witness",b="When brought to Sven at his camp in the western hills, the book reveals a chilling detail. It proves that a shadowy figure had watched the horrific massacre of his family take place. Rather than granting Sven peace, the journal turns his grief toward finding this unknown onlooker and demanding answers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the book found in the mound of dirt?",a="It is an untitled, dirt-stained journal buried at the Yorgen farm. Its entries prove that an unidentified onlooker watched the massacre of Sven Yorgen's family.",al={"what book is this","book from svens farm","what did i dig up"}},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Delivering the book to Sven Yorgen leads directly into the quest 'The Shadowy Figure', setting off a search for the mysterious witness.",al={"what comes next","next quest after svens camp","who is the shadowy figure"}},{q="Where is Sven Yorgen located?",a="Sven has taken refuge in an encampment in the northwestern hills of Duskwood, brooding over the fate of his family and plotting his retribution.",al={"where is sven","sven yorgen location","where do i turn this in"}},{q="Why was the book buried at the farm?",a="The book was hidden in a mound of loose dirt amidst the ruined homestead, either hastily discarded or concealed by the observer who lingered at the scene of the attack.",al={"why buried","who hid the book","mound of loose dirt"}},{q="Who killed Sven's family?",a="Mysterious, dark riders rampaged through the farm, slaughtering Sven's kin and turning the once-peaceful homestead into an undead-infested ruin.",al={"who attacked the farm","who killed svens family","svens family killers"}},{q="What faction can complete this quest?",a="This quest is exclusive to Alliance players, as Sven Yorgen only seeks aid from the defenders of Duskwood and the Alliance.",al={"is this alliance only","can horde do svens camp"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating the Yorgen massacre is part of the Alliance's broader struggle to comprehend the dark forces encroaching upon Duskwood."},kw={"dark riders","duskwood","mound of loose dirt","shadowy figure","sven yorgen","yorgen farm"},rel={"quest:95","quest:262","npc:sven-yorgen","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Mound of loose dirt",["end"]="Sven Yorgen",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=230},src={"Sven's Camp"}}
E["quest:240"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Jitters",z="duskwood",s="Return to Jitters concludes Chef Grual's culinary errand in Duskwood. Having prepared his infamous 'crab' cakes using the gooey legs of the local venom web spiders, Grual sends you back to the starving, terrified hermit at Raven Hill. Delivering the meal finally satisfies Jitters' desperate hunger.",h="Return to Jitters concludes Chef Grual's culinary errand in Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Dubious Delicacy",b="Duskwood is short on conventional livestock and sea life, leaving Chef Grual at the Scarlet Raven Tavern to improvise with whatever the blighted forest provides. His renowned 'Dusky Crab Cakes' contain no actual crab meat at all, relying instead on gooey legs harvested from the venom web spiders creeping through the wood. Grual considers this resourceful cooking; anyone with a delicate stomach might view it with horror.",sp=0},{t="Soothing Jitters' Nerves",b="Jitters spends his days huddled at Raven Hill, utterly consumed by fright and paralyzed by whatever horrors drove him out of the woods. Weak with terror and unable to muster the courage to hunt or forage for himself, his empty stomach only amplifies his distress. Receiving the warm cakes brings a rare moment of relief to the trembling vagrant, who is far too hungry to question what kind of 'crab' Chef Grual used.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is in the Dusky Crab Cakes?",a="There are no crabs in Duskwood. Chef Grual makes his specialty cakes using the gooey legs of local venom web spiders, seasoning them to mimic traditional seafood cakes.",al={"crab cakes ingredients","what are dusky crab cakes made of","are they real crab"}},{q="Does Jitters know the cakes are made of spider goo?",a="Chef Grual keeps his culinary secret to himself, and Jitters is far too starved and terrified to ask about the recipe. He eagerly eats them without suspecting their true origin.",al={"does jitters know","does jitters know about the spiders"}},{q="Why couldn't Jitters get his own food?",a="Jitters is completely overwhelmed by fear following his encounters in the wild woods of Duskwood. Paralyzed by panic, he refuses to venture far from his hiding place at Raven Hill and relies on sympathetic travelers to bring him sustenance.",al={"why is jitters starving","why doesn't jitters hunt"}},{q="Who is Chef Grual?",a="Chef Grual is the cook at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. Faced with a town isolated by shadows and beasts, he uses whatever unconventional ingredients scavengers bring him to keep the local tavern fed.",al={"chef grual role","cook in darkshire"}},{q="Where does this quest chain begin?",a="The errand begins with Jitters at Raven Hill asking for help with his rumbling stomach in 'Jitters' Growling Gut', which leads to hunting venom web spiders for Chef Grual before returning here with the finished meal.",al={"how to start jitters food quest","jitters quest chain start"}},{q="Does Jitters recover after eating?",a="The meal satisfies his physical hunger and earns you his heartfelt gratitude, but food does not cure his deep-seated psychological terror. He remains anxious and haunted by the dark secrets of the forest.",al={"is jitters cured","does food help jitters"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Chef Grual's ability to turn gooey venom web spider legs into palatable cakes is a testament to the gritty resourcefulness demanded of cooks on the frontier.",["faction:Alliance"]="The meager, unconventional diet in Darkshire reflects how cut off the town is from Stormwind's broader supply lines, leaving locals to rely on whatever creeps in the shadows."},kw={"chef grual","darkshire","duskwood","dusky crab cakes","growling gut","jitters","scarlet raven tavern"},rel={"quest:93","quest:5","npc:jitters","npc:chef-grual","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Chef Grual",["end"]="Jitters",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=240},src={"Return to Jitters"}}
E["quest:245"] = {t="quest",n="Eight-Legged Menaces",z="duskwood",s="Eight-Legged Menaces is a militia contract issued by Watcher Dodds on Duskwood's western border. Overrun by aggressive venom web spiders, the understaffed Night Watch relies on wandering adventurers to cull the brood before more guards are caught in their webs.",h="Eight-Legged Menaces is a militia contract issued by Watcher Dodds on Duskwood's western border.",sec={{t="A Border Under Siege",b="Along the western road linking Westfall to Duskwood, the dense canopy gives way to tangled thickets choked with webbing. As darkness tightened its grip on Grand Hamlet and turned it into the haunted grove known today, the local arachnids mutated into monstrous predators. Pygmy venom web spiders now infest the brush in swarms, threatening travelers and encroaching upon the fragile defensive lines maintained by the Night Watch.",sp=0},{t="The Burden on the Night Watch",b="Stationed far from the safety of Darkshire, Watcher Dodds finds himself desperately short on troops. Commander Althea Ebonlocke cannot spare reinforcements to secure remote outposts when undead and worgen press against the township itself. Left isolated, Dodds has already watched comrades fall victim to the spiders, discovering men hanging upside down in the canopy as paralytic venom slowly liquefied them for feeding.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest?",a="Watcher Dodds, a member of the Night Watch posted on Duskwood's western boundary near Westfall, offers this task to travelers capable of clearing out the spiders.",al={"quest giver","who gives eight-legged menaces","watcher dodds"}},{q="Why can't the Night Watch handle the spiders themselves?",a="Commander Althea Ebonlocke must concentrate her meager garrison near Darkshire to repel relentless undead assaults. Dodds lacks the manpower to assault the infested border nests without abandoning his post.",al={"why need help","why call adventurers","darkshire militia shortage"}},{q="Where are these spiders located?",a="The pygmy venom web spiders nest heavily in the western woods of Duskwood, lurking in the brush just off the main road coming in from Westfall.",al={"spider location","where are pygmy venom webs","spider woods"}},{q="What makes these spiders so dangerous to the watch?",a="Aside from their sheer numbers, they possess a potent venom that paralyzes and dissolves flesh, leaving ensnared Night Watchmen helpless and strung up in the boughs as easy prey.",al={"spider poison","spider venom","spider victims"}},{q="Are these the only spiders in Duskwood?",a="No. The pygmy venom webs are merely the smaller broodlings. Deeper into the woods dwell much larger, deadlier specimens that pose an even graver danger to travelers.",al={"other duskwood spiders","spider species","venom web spiders"}},{q="Why has the insect and spider population grown so aggressively?",a="The pervasive magical corruption that blankets Duskwood has twisted the indigenous wildlife, accelerating their aggression, size, and lethality across the blighted forest.",al={"why so many spiders","duskwood corruption nature","spider origin"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Night Watch stands entirely alone without aid from the House of Nobles, making any support Alliance travelers provide vital for keeping the roads open.",["class:Hunter"]="The venom web spiders of Duskwood are vicious beasts requiring careful footwork and anti-venom preparation to hunt effectively."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","eight-legged menaces","night watch","pygmy venom web spider","spiders","watcher dodds"},rel={"npc:watcher-dodds","topic:night-watch","quest:56","zone:duskwood","subzone:darkshire"},m={start="Watcher Dodds",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=245},src={"Eight-Legged Menaces"}}
E["quest:251"] = {t="quest",n="Translate Abercrombie's Note",z="duskwood",s="Translate Abercrombie's Note is an Alliance quest in Darkshire that tasks an adventurer with carrying an indecipherable letter to the town's resident scholar. Lord Ello Ebonlocke cannot make sense of the hermit's missive, relying instead on Sirra Von'Indi's knowledge of obscure scripts. It marks the moment Darkshire's leadership realizes Abercrombie's odd errands hide something far more deliberate.",h="Translate Abercrombie's Note is an Alliance quest in Darkshire that tasks an adventurer with carrying an...",sec={{t="An Indecipherable Message",b="When Abercrombie dispatches a sealed letter to Mayor Ello Ebonlocke, the town leader expects an eccentric plea or bitter ramblings from the cemetery hermit. Instead, the parchment is inscribed in strange, cryptic writing that defies standard Common script. Lacking the scholarly training to decipher ancient or esoteric languages, Mayor Ebonlocke refuses to dismiss the letter out of hand, knowing that even mad hermits can pose a hazard in Duskwood.",sp=0},{t="The Scholar of Darkshire",b="To crack the cipher, Ebonlocke directs travelers across the square to Sirra Von'Indi. Sirra is Darkshire's scholar of esoteric lore, well-versed in ancient arts and forgotten tongues. Though Sirra scoffs at Abercrombie's sanity—quipping that anyone dwelling beside a haunted graveyard must have rotted brains—he takes the parchment seriously enough to begin the painstaking process of transcription.",sp=0},{t="A Glimpse into the Hermit's Mind",b="Handing the letter over sets into motion a grim revelation for the town. While Abercrombie previously appeared to be a frail, reclusive old man begging for supplies and protection from ghouls, his encoded letter to the mayor signals a far darker intelligence and an impending reckoning that Darkshire is ill-prepared to confront.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why can't Mayor Ebonlocke read the note himself?",a="The letter delivered from Abercrombie is written in an unusual script or ancient cipher. Mayor Ello Ebonlocke is an administrator and noble rather than a linguist, so he sends it to Sirra Von'Indi, Darkshire's resident expert in ancient arts and arcane tongues.",al={"why can't ello read note","ebonlocke letter translate","why need translator"}},{q="Who is Sirra Von'Indi?",a="Sirra Von'Indi is a learned resident residing in Darkshire. Known for his expertise in obscure languages, history, and ancient arts, he serves as the town's go-to scholar whenever mysterious texts or relics emerge from the darkened woods.",al={"sirra von indi who","who is the translator","darkshire scholar"}},{q="Where does Abercrombie live?",a="Abercrombie lives in a ramshackle shack located just northeast of Raven Hill Cemetery in western Duskwood, surrounded by restless undead and predatory beasts.",al={"where is abercrombie","hermit location","abercrombie duskwood"}},{q="What is Sirra's reaction to Abercrombie's note?",a="Sirra openly doubts Abercrombie's sanity, remarking that anyone willing to live beside a graveyard must have a rotted brain. Nevertheless, he agrees to examine the letter and begins translating its esoteric script.",al={"what does sirra think of abercrombie","sirra von indi dialogue"}},{q="What happens after giving the note to Sirra?",a="Sirra Von'Indi asks the adventurer to wait while he works through the transcription. Once finished, the translated contents reveal Abercrombie's true intentions and escalate the threat against Darkshire.",al={"next quest after translate note","what comes after translate abercrombie note"},sp=1},{q="Why did Abercrombie write to Mayor Ebonlocke?",a="Abercrombie sent the note under the guise of correspondence with town leadership, but disguised his words in a hidden script to veil his sinister plots until he was ready to strike.",al={"why did abercrombie send letter","hermit note purpose"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Mages familiar with obscure dialects and arcane transcriptions will appreciate Sirra Von'Indi's role as Darkshire's local expert on esoteric scripts.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions aiding Duskwood, this errand highlights how vulnerable and isolated Darkshire's civic leadership feels amidst the surrounding darkness."},kw={"abercrombie","cipher","darkshire","duskwood","ello ebonlocke","hermit","sirra von'indi","translation"},rel={"npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","npc:sirra-von-indi","quest:401","npc:abercrombie","quest:165","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Lord Ello Ebonlocke",["end"]="Sirra Von'Indi",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=251},src={"Translate Abercrombie's Note"}}
E["quest:252"] = {t="quest",n="Translation to Ello",z="duskwood",s="Translation to Ello is a pivotal quest in the Abercrombie storyline in Duskwood. Having asked Sirra Von'Indi to decipher the hermit's cryptic writings, the adventurer is tasked with delivering the translated parchment directly to Lord Ello Ebonlocke in Darkshire.",h="Translation to Ello is a pivotal quest in the Abercrombie storyline in Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Belated Realization",b="For days, the elderly hermit Abercrombie had travelers running errands across Duskwood under the pretense of frail survival. He requested thread, preserved reagents, and personal belongings. Only when Sirra Von'Indi finally deciphers his private parchment does the truth come out: the kindly old man is an unhinged embalmer, and the components gathered were used to construct a terrifying weapon of revenge aimed straight at Darkshire.",sp=1},{t="The Road to Darkshire",b="Presenting the translated letter to Lord Ello Ebonlocke drains all color from the mayor's face. Whatever noble motives guided an adventurer's assistance, delivering those final supplies allowed Abercrombie to finish his monstrous creation, Stitches. Handing over the letter sets the behemoth marching directly eastward along the road from Raven Hill Cemetery, slaughtering any Night Watch patrols standing in its path.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written in the translated letter?",a="The letter details Abercrombie's bitter vengeance against Darkshire and Lord Ello Ebonlocke. It reveals that the reagents and materials gathered by unsuspecting travelers were used to assemble and animate Stitches, a massive undead abomination unleashed to destroy the town.",al={"what does the letter say","abercrombie letter text","what was translated"},sp=2},{q="Who is Sirra Von'Indi?",a="Sirra Von'Indi is a scholar residing in Darkshire. His linguistic and analytical expertise allows him to decipher the cryptic notes and letters left behind by Abercrombie when others cannot read his script.",al={"who is sirra","sirra von indi lore"}},{q="Why does Lord Ello blame the player?",a="Lord Ello Ebonlocke reacts with horror because every task completed for the seemingly helpless hermit—fetching thread, ghoul ribs, and embalming supplies—directly facilitated the creation of Stitches. Although done out of charity, those errands effectively handed the mad embalmer the pieces he needed to construct his weapon.",al={"why is ello mad","did i cause stitches","ello reaction"},sp=2},{q="What happens immediately after completing this quest?",a="Handing the translated letter to Lord Ello Ebonlocke sets Stitches in motion. The massive abomination begins his slow, relentless march along the main path from Raven Hill Cemetery straight toward Darkshire, cutting down Night Watch guards as he approaches.",al={"what triggers stitches","does stitches spawn","stitches event"},sp=2},{q="Where does Stitches go after this?",a="Stitches follows the Duskwood thoroughfare eastward from the outskirts of Raven Hill Cemetery toward Darkshire. Along the road, he engages and overwhelms Night Watch defenders before reaching the town gates unless brought down by adventurers.",al={"stitches path","where is stitches marching"},sp=2},{q="What quest comes next?",a="Following the delivery of the letter, Lord Ello sends adventurers to investigate Abercrombie's remaining machinations in the quest 'Bride of the Embalmer', seeking to root out the rest of the necromancer's plots.",al={"next quest","after translation to ello"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, this moment is a painful lesson in Duskwood's treachery: misplaced trust in the woods can endanger an entire settlement of innocent citizens."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","ello ebonlocke","raven hill","sirra von'indi","translation to ello"},rel={"npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","npc:abercrombie","npc:sirra-von-indi","quest:253","quest:401","subzone:darkshire","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery"},m={start="Sirra Von'Indi",["end"]="Lord Ello Ebonlocke",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=252},src={"Translation to Ello"}}
E["quest:253"] = {t="quest",n="Bride of the Embalmer",z="duskwood",s="\"Bride of the Embalmer\" is a perilous task assigned by Lord Ello Ebonlocke in Darkshire. Having pieced together the disturbing truth behind the legendary Embalmer, town leadership sends you into the haunted cemeteries of Duskwood to find his resurrected wife's resting place. By tearing the alchemist's living heart from Eliza's cursed remains, you aim to strip him of his unholy power.",h="\"Bride of the Embalmer\" is a perilous task assigned by Lord Ello Ebonlocke in Darkshire.",sec={{t="A Bedtime Story Come Alive",b="For years, parents in Duskwood told their frightened children the tale of the Embalmer. According to the folktale, he was once a kindly alchemist whose mind shattered following the tragic demise of his beloved wife, Eliza. Desperate to cheat mortality, he turned to foul sorceries and took the ultimate sacrifice: carving out his own beating heart and placing it into his wife's chest. Lord Ello Ebonlocke long dismissed this as mere village folklore, but recent revelations have proven that the Embalmer walks among them, his foul handiwork festering beneath the graveyard dirt.",sp=0},{t="The Resurrected Bride",b="The ritual succeeded in restoring Eliza to animation, but dark necromancy always demands a harrowing toll. Revived by the stolen spark of life, Eliza transformed into a ravenous abomination cursed with an insatiable hunger for living human flesh. Horrified and unwilling to destroy his creation, the Embalmer was forced to conceal his bride away in a lonely grave, visiting her in secret while plotting further depravities. To disarm the necromancer, Lord Ebonlocke directs brave souls to exhume Eliza, strike down the flesh-craving horror, and reclaim the still-pulsing organ that sustains his dark art.",sp=1},{t="Darkshire's Aegis",b="When you tear the beating heart from Eliza's decomposing breast and carry it back to Darkshire, Lord Ebonlocke breathes a sigh of relief. Far from simply destroying it, the town mayor intends to turn the alchemist's dark craft against him. He believes the eldritch magic lingering within the heart will serve as a defensive talisman and aegis over Darkshire, shielding the beleaguered town from whatever wrath the weakened Embalmer might still summon in vengeance.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is the Embalmer?",a="The Embalmer was originally an alchemist in Duskwood who went mad after his wife Eliza died. Turning to necromantic arts, he cut out his own living heart and placed it inside Eliza's corpse to resurrect her, transforming himself into an elusive monster.",al={"embalmer lore","who is the embalmer","embalmer backstory"}},{q="Why was Eliza buried if she was brought back to life?",a="Although the alchemist successfully revived Eliza using his own heart, the dark magic cursed her with an insatiable hunger for living human flesh. Unable to keep her safely in society or quench her feral appetite, he was forced to keep her buried in a cemetery.",al={"why is eliza buried","eliza grave","why keep eliza in a grave"}},{q="Why does Lord Ebonlocke want the Embalmer's Heart?",a="The heart contains the source of the Embalmer's supernatural power. Lord Ebonlocke believes that seizing the beating organ will shatter the necromancer's strength and allow Darkshire to use its foul sorcery as a protective ward against his evil.",al={"why get the heart","embalmer heart purpose"}},{q="Where does this quest chain begin?",a="The quest follows directly from 'Translation to Ello', wherein old letters and research are delivered to Lord Ello Ebonlocke, proving that the Embalmer of local nursery tales is an active and dangerous reality.",al={"quest prerequisite","how to get bride of the embalmer","embalmer prequest"}},{q="Does retrieving the heart defeat the Embalmer permanently?",a="No. Stripping Eliza of the Embalmer's heart breaks the magical conduit of his power, but the Embalmer himself remains at large in Duskwood, plotting retribution against Darkshire for desecrating his beloved's resting place.",al={"is the embalmer dead","does this kill the embalmer"},sp=1},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Lord Ello Ebonlocke, the mayor and leader of Darkshire, gives the quest from the Darkshire Town Hall after learning the chilling truth behind the town's folklore.",al={"quest giver","who starts bride of the embalmer"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Paladins view Eliza's foul reanimation as an affront to the Light and natural law, gladly purging the flesh-eating horror and severing the necromancer's blasphemous lifeline.",["class:Priest"]="Priests recognize the tragedy behind a grieving widower fallen to dark arts, but know Eliza's flesh-hungry mockery of life must be laid to rest with holy finality.",["faction:Alliance"]="With the Night Watch stretched thin fighting the feral terrors of Duskwood, an Alliance champion must step in to defend Darkshire from this ancient, creeping madness."},kw={"alchemist","bride of the embalmer","darkshire","duskwood","eliza","ello ebonlocke","embalmer's heart","grave","the embalmer"},rel={"npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","quest:252","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:938"},m={start="Lord Ello Ebonlocke",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=253},src={"Bride of the Embalmer"}}
E["quest:254"] = {t="quest",n="Digging Through the Dirt",z="duskwood",s="Digging Through the Dirt marks the grim culmination of the hunt for the Embalmer's missing heart in Duskwood. Deep in the ravenous quiet of Raven Hill Cemetery, a disturbed mound of earth conceals a buried horror that refuses to stay dead.",h="Digging Through the Dirt marks the grim culmination of the hunt for the Embalmer's missing heart in Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Grave Disturbed",b="Amid the countless weathered headstones of Raven Hill Cemetery sits a patch of recently turned, semi-loose soil marked with the name Eliza. While many graves in Duskwood lie desecrated by scavengers or feral ghouls, this earth was placed with deliberate intent. Digging past the topsoil reveals the splintered timber of a buried coffin, sealing away whatever remnant Abercrombie sought to hide away from the light of day.",sp=0},{t="The Scratching Within",b="Beneath the splintered wood lies no resting corpse. Pressing against the lid, one can feel frantic vibrations—the frantic scraping of long, clawed fingers and the hollow clatter of rotting jaws. Abercrombie's morbid experiment, Eliza, stirs violently within her pine prison, clutching the Embalmer's missing heart and waiting for unwary hands to pry open the grave.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is buried in Eliza's grave?",a="Buried beneath the dirt is a coffin containing Eliza, an undead monstrosity created by Abercrombie the Embalmer. She has been sealed underground clutching Abercrombie's missing heart.",al={"what is in the grave","who is eliza","eliza grave contents"},sp=1},{q="Where is this grave located?",a="Eliza's grave is located within Raven Hill Cemetery in western Duskwood, amid the sea of haunted crypts and roving undead.",al={"where is elizas grave","eliza grave location","grave dirt location"}},{q="Why do you have to dig into the coffin?",a="You must dig into the grave to confront Eliza and recover the Embalmer's heart, completing the investigation surrounding Abercrombie's twisted machinations.",al={"why dig the grave","purpose of digging","why open the coffin"},sp=1},{q="What happens when the coffin is opened?",a="Opening the coffin unleashes Eliza from her shallow prison, forcing you to destroy the clawing, ravenous ghoul to retrieve the heart locked away inside with her.",al={"what happens next","coffin opened","opening elizas coffin"},sp=1},{q="Who put Eliza in the ground?",a="Abercrombie the Embalmer placed her there, concealing his gruesome creation within the sprawling burial grounds of Raven Hill alongside his prized heart.",al={"who buried eliza","who put her there"},sp=1},{q="Is Eliza an ordinary ghoul?",a="Eliza is the Embalmer's own late wife, revived by his dark magic with his heart placed in her breast, far tougher and more deliberate than the mindless ghouls wandering Duskwood's roads.",al={"what kind of monster is eliza","is eliza a ghoul"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Disturbing fresh graves goes against every funeral rite of the Holy Light, but releasing and destroying the unnatural fiend trapped inside is a necessary act of cleansing.",["class:Priest"]="The sounds of scratching claws and gnashing teeth beneath consecrated soil are an affront to the peaceful repose promised by the Light to the deceased of Duskwood.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Night Watch struggles constantly against the terror spilling out of Raven Hill; rooting out the buried horrors hidden by the Embalmer is vital for Darkshire's safety."},kw={"abercrombie","bride of the embalmer","coffin","digging through the dirt","duskwood","eliza","eliza's grave dirt","embalmer's heart","raven hill cemetery"},rel={"quest:253","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Eliza's Grave Dirt",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=254},src={"Digging Through the Dirt"}}
E["quest:262"] = {t="quest",n="The Shadowy Figure",z="duskwood",s="Haunted by the massacre of his family, the hermit Sven Yorgen tasks you with discovering the identity of a mysterious stranger seen lurking near his farm on that fateful night. Armed only with an enigmatic book recovered from the ruins, you must consult the residents of Darkshire to trace the stranger's footsteps.",h="Haunted by the massacre of his family, the hermit Sven Yorgen tasks you with discovering the identity of a...",sec={{t="Echoes of a Slaughter",b="Sven Yorgen lives in hiding along the desolate hills of Duskwood, broken by the horrific butchery of his family and workers. While he originally placed blame on the mysterious black riders terrorizing the woods, his memory remains tormented by another detail: a quiet, shadowy figure who was lurking nearby on the night of the massacre. Desperate for answers, Sven entrusts you with the only physical clue recovered from the wreckage—a strange book left behind at the ransacked farm.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Divination in Town",b="With no direct leads to pursue in the perilous wilderness, the trail points back east toward Darkshire. Sven hopes that someone among the superstitious locals might recognize the curious volume. Darkshire harbors its share of oddities and mediums, most notably Madame Eva, whose occult senses and divinations allow her to peer beyond ordinary mundane sight to read the spiritual impressions clinging to mysterious relics.",sp=0},{t="Foreign Threads",b="Presenting the book to Madame Eva reveals faint but unmistakable psychic impressions. While Sven's own burning desire for vengeance has recently marked the pages, the underlying aura belongs to someone else entirely. Eva divines that the original owner was not a resident of Darkshire or Duskwood at all, confirming that an outsider walked the farm before the bloodshed began.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sven Yorgen?",a="Sven Yorgen is a devastated farmer driven into exile in the western hills of Duskwood. After dark riders attacked his homestead and slaughtered his entire family, he fled into the wilderness, consumed by grief, fear, and a desperate hunger for revenge against those responsible.",al={"who is sven","sven backstory","sven yorgen"}},{q="What is the book found at Sven's farm?",a="The book is a physical artifact recovered from the dirt and rubble of Sven's destroyed homestead. It belonged to an elusive onlooker who was seen lurking in the shadows during the attack on his family.",al={"what book is this","book from svens farm","mysterious book"}},{q="Why take the book to Madame Eva?",a="Madame Eva is Darkshire's resident seer and fortune teller. Ordinary townsfolk cannot glean much from an unmarked volume, but Eva uses her clairvoyant powers to read residual psychic impressions left by whoever previously owned or carried the object.",al={"why madame eva","who reads the book","darkshire mystic"}},{q="What does Madame Eva learn from the book?",a="Madame Eva senses the powerful emotional imprint of revenge left by Sven's recent handling of it. Beneath that, however, she detects faint traces indicating that the original owner was an outsider not native to Darkshire.",al={"what does eva say","book owner identity","divination result"},sp=1},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Learning that the owner was an outsider prompts Madame Eva to send you searching through other records and local spots in Darkshire, seeking anyone who might recall an unfamiliar traveler matching the figure's description.",al={"what next","next quest after book","who is the shadowy figure"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire's lack of support from Stormwind forces its traumatized frontiersmen and local seers to rely entirely on wandering Alliance champions to investigate deadly atrocities in Duskwood.",["class:Priest"]="Investigating Madame Eva's divination highlights the thin veil between spiritual clairvoyance, shadow magic, and unseen psychic impressions lingering on everyday objects."},kw={"book","darkshire","duskwood","madame eva","shadowy figure","sven yorgen","sven's camp"},rel={"quest:230","quest:265","npc:sven-yorgen","npc:madame-eva","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Sven Yorgen",["end"]="Madame Eva",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=262},src={"The Shadowy Figure"}}
E["quest:265"] = {t="quest",n="The Shadowy Search Continues",z="duskwood",s="Following Madame Eva's divination, this investigation leads from her parlor to Clerk Daltry in Darkshire. It centers on tracing the origins of the journal recovered from the ruins of Sven Yorgen's ransacked farmstead.",h="Following Madame Eva's divination, this investigation leads from her parlor to Clerk Daltry in Darkshire.",sec={{t="Tracing the Binding",b="After examining the burnt journal salvaged from the tragedy at Sven's farm, Madame Eva discerned that while its author was an outsider, the physical volume itself came from within Darkshire. Clerk Daltry frequently sells blank ledgers and tomes to traveling scholars, spellcasters, and record-keepers. By following the trail of local commerce, investigators seek a mundane paper trail to identify an otherwise elusive and sinister trespasser lurking in the gloomy groves of Duskwood.",sp=0},{t="A Jittery Buyer",b="Upon inspecting the tome, Clerk Daltry recalls the transaction clearly despite the volume of records that pass through Darkshire's town hall. Roughly a month prior, a nervous, furtive traveler bought the blank book without ever giving a name. The customer's jittery demeanor and constant glances over his shoulder left a distinct impression on the clerk, confirming that the shadowy figure Sven glimpsed had walked openly among Darkshire's citizens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where did the mysterious book come from?",a="The blank book was purchased directly in Darkshire from Clerk Daltry roughly a month ago, though the grim writings inside were authored by the stranger who bought it.",al={"origin of book","who sold the book","book source"}},{q="Why does Madame Eva send you to Clerk Daltry?",a="Madame Eva recognizes the book's physical binding and materials as having been purchased locally in town. Clerk Daltry handles the sale of blank ledgers and journals to locals and traveling scholars.",al={"why daltry","eva daltry connection","who made the book"}},{q="What does Clerk Daltry remember about the buyer?",a="Daltry recalls selling the tome to a shady, nervous man who refused to give his name and constantly looked over his shoulder as though being watched or pursued.",al={"who bought book","buyer description","shadowy figure appearance"}},{q="How does this connect to Sven's farm?",a="The book was salvaged from Sven Yorgen's destroyed farm in southern Duskwood, left behind during the murderous raid that wiped out his family and workers.",al={"sven connection","why are we looking","sven yorgen"}},{q="Where does the investigation lead next?",a="Since the nervous stranger spent time in town, the search continues at Darkshire's tavern, the Scarlet Raven Inn, to see if anyone witnessed where he stayed or who he spoke with.",al={"what next","after daltry","next clue"},sp=1},{q="Is Clerk Daltry in danger?",a="Daltry was merely an unwitting merchant who sold a blank volume to a passing traveler, unaware that the buyer would soon witness the slaughter at Sven's farm.",al={"clerk daltry danger","daltry safe"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Unraveling who supplied and aided the necromancers in Duskwood is vital for safeguarding Darkshire and bringing justice to slaughtered frontier homesteaders.",["class:Rogue"]="Tracking a nervous target through town by following purchase records and merchant impressions is classic investigative tradecraft."},kw={"book","clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","journal","madame eva","shadowy figure","sven yorgen"},rel={"npc:clerk-daltry","npc:madame-eva","quest:262","quest:266","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Madame Eva",["end"]="Clerk Daltry",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=265},src={"The Shadowy Search Continues"}}
E["quest:266"] = {t="quest",n="Inquire at the Inn",z="duskwood",s="Inquire at the Inn is an Alliance quest in Darkshire that continues the investigation into the mysterious stranger connected to Sven Yorgen's ruined farm. Directed by Clerk Daltry, adventurers take a recovered journal to the Scarlet Raven Tavern to question Tavernkeep Smitts about who stayed there.",h="Inquire at the Inn is an Alliance quest in Darkshire that continues the investigation into the mysterious...",sec={{t="A Lead at the Scarlet Raven",b="After Clerk Daltry finishes examining the tattered book recovered from Sven Yorgen's farm, he suggests that any stranger visiting Darkshire would almost certainly have passed through the local tavern. The Scarlet Raven Inn stands across town as Darkshire's only gathering hall and lodging house, making it the most sensible place to track down transient visitors.",sp=0},{t="The Paranoid Guest",b="Presenting the book to Tavernkeep Smitts confirms Daltry's hunch. Smitts immediately recognizes the tome, recalling a patron who took a room for several days and spent his evenings scribbling obsessively at the bar. According to the innkeeper, the guest fled Darkshire in a state of terror, convinced he was being relentlessly hunted by an unseen pursuer. His path led west down the gloom of the road toward Raven Hill.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to the inn?",a="Clerk Daltry, the town record-keeper situated in Darkshire's town hall, hands back the journal and suggests checking the local inn for anyone who might recognize its owner.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","where does inquire at the inn start"}},{q="What is the book you are carrying?",a="It is the worn journal retrieved from Sven Yorgen's ruined farmstead in southern Duskwood, believed to belong to the shadowy figure seen prowling around the area.",al={"what is the book","book from svens farm","journal"}},{q="Who runs the Scarlet Raven Inn?",a="Tavernkeep Smitts manages the Scarlet Raven Tavern, pouring drinks and renting rooms to whatever travelers still dare to venture into Duskwood.",al={"who is the tavernkeeper","innkeeper darkshire","who is smitts"}},{q="What does Tavernkeep Smitts reveal about the guest?",a="Smitts recalls that the journal's owner rented a room for a few days and spent his nights drinking and writing. The traveler then fled west in a panic, muttering about being hunted by something terrifying.",al={"what did smitts say","what happened to the shadowy figure","what does the innkeeper know"}},{q="Where did the shadowy figure flee?",a="He hurried westward out of Darkshire seeking a hiding place, pointing searchers toward the abandoned settlement and sprawling cemetery grounds of Raven Hill.",al={"where did he go","where is the shadowy figure","where to next"}},{q="What quest follows Inquire at the Inn?",a="Tavernkeep Smitts directs you to follow the stranger's trail westward in the quest 'Finding the Shadowy Figure'.",al={"next quest","what comes after inquire at the inn","following quest"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating threats inside Darkshire helps protect one of the Alliance's most vulnerable and isolated frontier settlements in the southern Eastern Kingdoms.",["class:Rogue"]="Tracking a paranoid fugitive from tavern hearsay to desolate ruins plays directly into an operative's investigative tradecraft."},kw={"clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","inquire at the inn","raven hill","scarlet raven","shadowy figure","sven yorgen","tavernkeep smitts"},rel={"npc:tavernkeep-smitts","npc:clerk-daltry","quest:265","quest:453","quest:262","quest:163","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Clerk Daltry",["end"]="Tavernkeep Smitts",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=266},src={"Inquire at the Inn"}}
E["quest:268"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Sven",z="duskwood",s="This quest marks the moment Sven Yorgen finally learns the truth behind the brutal massacre of his family and workers at the Yorgen Farmstead. After tracking down the runaway Jitters, you return to Sven's isolated camp on the edge of Westfall carrying the vagrant's completed journal. The grim revelations inside pivot Sven's grief toward cold vengeance against the mysterious Dark Riders and the necromancer Morbent Fel.",h="This quest marks the moment Sven Yorgen finally learns the truth behind the brutal massacre of his family and...",sec={{t="A Coward's Confession",b="When Sven Yorgen's farm was attacked, Jitters fled into the woods in terror, leaving behind only an incomplete diary amidst the slaughter. Terrified of Sven's wrath and haunted by what he witnessed, Jitters hid deep within Duskwood. When confronted, he hands over his completed journal willingly, desperately hoping that providing the full story of the attack will spare him from having to face the vengeful farmer in person.",sp=0},{t="Unmasking the Dark Riders",b="Reading Jitters' finished account finally connects the horrifying pieces for Sven. The slaughter at his farm was not a random undead surge or feral beast attack; it was carried out by the enigmatic Dark Riders searching for an artifact. Furthermore, Sven recalls witnessing these very same hooded figures meeting secretly with the necromancer Morbent Fel near the Forlorn Rowe. Jitters' journal transforms Sven's blind sorrow into a targeted hunt for retribution against the dark wizard.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Jitters so terrified of Sven Yorgen?",a="Jitters was staying at Sven's farmstead when the Dark Riders descended upon it. Instead of standing to fight alongside the family or sounding an alarm, Jitters ran for his life and abandoned everyone to their deaths. He knows Sven holds him partly responsible and fears Sven would kill him on sight.",al={"why is jitters scared","jitters afraid of sven","what did jitters do"}},{q="What is in Jitters' completed journal?",a="The journal details the true circumstances of the slaughter at the Yorgen Farmstead, recounting how the sinister Dark Riders attacked the farm in search of the Scythe of Elune and butchered Sven's loved ones while Jitters hid and escaped.",al={"what does the journal say","jitters completed journal lore"},sp=1},{q="Who are the Dark Riders mentioned by Sven?",a="The Dark Riders are mysterious, hooded cloaked figures roaming Duskwood. Ruthless and deadly, they entered the forest searching relentlessly for powerful magical relics, leaving death and ruin wherever they tread.",al={"who are dark riders","riders in duskwood","black riders"}},{q="How is Morbent Fel connected to the attack on Sven's farm?",a="Upon reading the journal, Sven recalls seeing the Dark Riders speaking directly with Morbent Fel at the Forlorn Rowe. Fel is a powerful necromancer wielding dark magic in the region, making him the prime suspect for collaborating with the riders who murdered Sven's family.",al={"morbent fel connection","why morbent fel","who is morbent fel"},sp=1},{q="Where can Sven Yorgen be found?",a="Sven has abandoned his ruined farmstead and now resides at a small, tense encampment tucked against the northwestern hills of Duskwood, near the border crossing into Westfall.",al={"where is sven","sven yorgen location","sven camp"}},{q="What happens after giving Sven the journal?",a="Armed with the knowledge from Jitters' journal, Sven focuses his wrath on the necromancer Morbent Fel. However, before he trusts you to strike at Fel directly, he tests your combat capabilities to ensure you are ready for the horrors ahead.",al={"next quest after return to sven","sven questline next"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The tragic demise of the Yorgen Farmstead is a stark reminder of Stormwind's complete failure to protect Duskwood's frontier settlements from the encroaching shadows.",["class:Paladin"]="Helping Sven unmask the dark forces behind his family's murder and guiding his pursuit toward the necromancer Morbent Fel aligns directly with the holy calling to purge the undead and deliver justice."},kw={"dark riders","duskwood","forlorn rowe","jitters","jitters' completed journal","morbent fel","sven yorgen","yorgen farmstead"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","npc:jitters","quest:453","topic:dark-riders","quest:55","subzone:forlorn-rowe","zone:duskwood","quest:262"},m={start="Jitters",["end"]="Sven Yorgen",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=268},src={"Return to Sven"}}
E["quest:270"] = {t="quest",n="The Doomed Fleet",z="duskwood",s="The Doomed Fleet is a journey northward dispatched by Bishop Farthing in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. Seeking a way to defeat the powerful necromancer Morbent Fel, heroes are sent across Khaz Modan to the drowned wreckage off the coast of the Wetlands.",h="The Doomed Fleet is a journey northward dispatched by Bishop Farthing in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light.",sec={{t="A Weapon of Holy Truth",b="Conventional steel has proven ineffective against the dark wards shielding Morbent Fel at his retreat on the Forlorn Rowe. To pierce such necromantic defenses, Bishop Farthing instructs adventurers that they must forge a weapon bound to the Holy Light. The key component is Lightforge Iron, a rare and consecrated metal whose strikes carry holy truth, cutting through sorcerous protections that turn aside ordinary blades.",sp=0},{t="The Wreck of the Third Fleet",b="Unfortunately, Lightforge Iron is not kept in ready supply in besieged Duskwood. Farthing recalls that years ago, the Third Fleet of the island nation of Kul Tiras met catastrophe along the treacherous shores of the Wetlands north of Ironforge. Aboard one of those sunken galleons was a shipment of the precious ore. Adventurers must travel all the way to Menethil Harbor to consult Glorin Steelbrow, a dwarven contact who knows the marshes and their shipwrecks best.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do I have to travel all the way to the Wetlands?",a="Morbent Fel's dark enchantments protect him from ordinary attacks. Bishop Farthing knows that only a weapon forged from sacred Lightforge Iron can strip those wards away, and the only known shipment lies among the wrecked ships of Kul Tiras's Third Fleet off Menethil Harbor.",al={"why go to wetlands","why menethil harbor","wetlands trip"}},{q="Who is Morbent Fel?",a="Morbent Fel is a sinister necromancer residing on the Forlorn Rowe in Duskwood. His sorcery has fueled much of the undead uprising plaguing the region, making his defeat essential for Darkshire's survival.",al={"morbent fel identity","who is the necromancer","duskwood necromancer"}},{q="Who is Glorin Steelbrow?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarf stationed at Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. He serves as an ally to the Church of the Holy Light and possesses deep knowledge of the coastline, shipwrecks, and salvage operations in the marsh.",al={"who is steelbrow","steelbrow role"}},{q="What is Lightforge Iron?",a="Lightforge Iron is a specially consecrated metal prized by the priesthood. Arms hammered from it strike with holy power, capable of dispelling or piercing dark shields and necromantic curses that defy ordinary iron.",al={"what does lightforge iron do","lightforge metal","blessed iron"}},{q="What happened to the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras?",a="Years ago, the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras was wrecked and sunk along the jagged, swampy coast of the Wetlands. Their hulls remain submerged off the shore, holding lost cargo and defended by drowned sailors and aquatic predators.",al={"third fleet fate","kul tiras ships wetlands","how did ships sink"}},{q="Does this quest involve any fighting right away?",a="This particular leg is entirely a courier quest. It requires a lengthy journey out of Duskwood, through the Kingdom of Stormwind and Khaz Modan, down to Menethil Harbor to make contact with Glorin Steelbrow.",al={"is there combat","just travel quest"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Seeking holy metal to smite an unholy necromancer exemplifies the Paladin calling to purge darkness using weapons sanctified by the Light.",["class:Priest"]="Acting under the guidance of Bishop Farthing connects priests directly to the Church's ancient knowledge of blessed relics and consecrated ores.",["faction:Alliance"]="This quest highlights the logistical span of the Alliance, linking the isolated human towns of the south to dwarven harbors and ancient maritime routes.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Smiths will appreciate the rare lore of Lightforge Iron, a metal imbued with faith that requires master craftsmanship to shape."},kw={"bishop farthing","doomed fleet","glorin steelbrow","kul tiras","lightforge iron","menethil harbor","morbent fel","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"quest:269","quest:321","quest:55","npc:glorin-steelbrow","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","zone:duskwood","topic:kul-tiras"},m={start="Bishop Farthing",["end"]="Glorin Steelbrow",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=270},src={"The Doomed Fleet"}}
E["quest:323"] = {t="quest",n="Proving Your Worth",z="duskwood",s="Proving Your Worth is a crucial step in Sven Yorgen's campaign for revenge in western Duskwood. Before allowing an adventurer to confront the necromancer Morbent Fel directly, the grieving hermit demands proof that they can overcome the undead legions infesting Raven Hill Cemetery.",h="Proving Your Worth is a crucial step in Sven Yorgen's campaign for revenge in western Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Bitter Hermit's Test",b="Sven Yorgen hides in a secluded camp north of the howling woods, consumed by grief and fury over the slaughter of his family. He has pieced together that the shadowy Dark Riders who razed his homestead were allied with a sinister necromancer named Morbent Fel. Though Sven hungers for retribution, he is not reckless enough to throw an untried recruit directly into Fel's grasp. He demands a display of sheer combat mastery against the skeletal forces occupying Raven Hill Cemetery.",sp=0},{t="The Raven Hill Crypts",b="To satisfy Sven, adventurers must push deep into the necropolis of Raven Hill, south of Forlorn Rowe. The mausoleum and the surrounding grounds crawl with restless corpses bound by Fel's foul magic: sword-wielding Skeletal Raiders patrol the tombstones, while Skeletal Warders and Healers tend the darker chambers beneath the earth. Clearing this vanguard is a bloody chore, especially with horrors like the vengeful phantom Mor'Ladim prowling the cemetery paths.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Necromancer",b="Surviving the bone-strewn catacombs convinces Sven that his ally possesses more than just empty courage. However, defeating Fel's lesser minions is only the prelude. Morbent Fel wields dark protective enchantments that render him nearly untouchable by mundane arms, forcing Sven to seek greater wisdom and ancient relics before the final confrontation can begin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Sven make me fight skeletons before facing Morbent Fel?",a="Sven knows Morbent Fel is a lethal necromancer allied with the mysterious Dark Riders. He refuses to send an ally to a meaningless death until they demonstrate the stamina and tactical skill needed to cut through an entire vanguard of undead minions.",al={"why proving your worth","why sven makes me kill skeletons","sven test"}},{q="Where are the Skeletal Warders and Healers found?",a="While Skeletal Raiders wander the open cemetery grounds south of Forlorn Rowe, Skeletal Healers and Warders are primarily found concentrated inside and immediately around the large mausoleum and crypt tunnels west of the cemetery's center.",al={"where are warders","where are skeletal healers","find skeletal warders"}},{q="Who is Mor'Ladim and why should I watch out for him here?",a="Mor'Ladim is a powerful, tragic undead knight who roams the paths of Raven Hill Cemetery. He is far stronger than the ordinary skeletons around the crypts and will quickly cut down unwary adventurers.",al={"morladim danger","who is mor'ladim","wandering elite raven hill"}},{q="How is Morbent Fel connected to the Dark Riders?",a="Sven discovered that Morbent Fel allied with the cloaked Dark Riders who butchered his wife and children. While the riders vanished back into the shadows, Fel remains anchored in Duskwood, continuing his foul necromancy.",al={"morbent fel dark riders connection","why dark riders and fel","sven family killers"}},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Once you prove your combat prowess, Sven acknowledges your strength but explains that Morbent Fel cannot be killed by brute force alone. He directs you to seek counsel from Bishop Farthing in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light to find a way to strip the necromancer of his unholy protections.",al={"next quest after proving your worth","what to do after skeletons"},sp=1},{q="Where is Sven Yorgen's camp located?",a="Sven maintains a hidden campsite in the hills along the far northwestern edge of Duskwood, tucked away safely north of Raven Hill and west of the road leading to Westfall.",al={"where is sven","sven camp location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Western Duskwood has fallen into anarchy without regular Stormwind patrols, leaving devastated frontiersmen like Sven to rely entirely on traveling champions to push back the undead scourge.",["class:Paladin"]="Cleansing Raven Hill Cemetery of Morbent Fel's restless dead is holy work, answering the unburied cries of Duskwood's deceased with the Light's justice.",["class:Priest"]="The desecration of Raven Hill's tombs by dark rituals cries out for spiritual cleansing, putting an end to the warders and healers who pervert life and death."},kw={"dark riders","duskwood","forlorn rowe","morbent fel","proving your worth","raven hill cemetery","skeletal healer","skeletal raider","skeletal warder","sven yorgen"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","quest:268","quest:269","quest:55","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","subzone:forlorn-rowe","topic:mor-ladim","topic:dark-riders"},m={start="Sven Yorgen",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=323},src={"Proving Your Worth (Classic)"}}
E["quest:401"] = {t="quest",n="Wait for Sirra to Finish",z="duskwood",s="This brief pause marks the moment Sirra Von'Indi deciphers the cryptic note delivered from the reclusive hermit Abercrombie. As she puts quill to paper in Darkshire's Town Hall, an ominous dread settles over the room, hinting that the hermit's words are far darker than expected.",h="This brief pause marks the moment Sirra Von'Indi deciphers the cryptic note delivered from the reclusive...",sec={{t="A Moment of Translation",b="After receiving the mysterious note penned by the hermit Abercrombie, Sirra Von'Indi requires only a short spell to decipher its text. As a resident scholar aiding the Night Watch and town leadership, she undertakes the task without realizing immediately what horrors the message conceals.",sp=0},{t="An Ominous Chill",b="The moment Sirra completes the transcription, the atmosphere shifts palpably. A sudden heaviness hangs over the room, likened to a thick black curtain dropping over the region. The deciphered note portends great danger for Darkshire, revealing that Abercrombie's seemingly harmless errands were part of a sinister, vengeful design.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sirra Von'Indi?",a="Sirra Von'Indi is an educated scholar residing in Darkshire's Town Hall. She assists Mayor Ello Ebonlocke and the local authorities by translating ancient scripts, strange documents, and ciphered messages brought in from the gloomy wilds of Duskwood.",al={"sirra von'indi","who is sirra","sirra duskwood"}},{q="What note is Sirra translating?",a="The note was penned by Abercrombie, the hermit who lives secluded in a shack near the western edge of Duskwood. You carried out a string of errands for him before this note ended up in Sirra's hands for translation.",al={"what is the note","abercrombie note","what did abercrombie write"},sp=1},{q="Why does the air feel heavy when she finishes?",a="The sudden oppressive chill is an omen of impending doom: whatever the note says, it is grim news for Darkshire, and its full meaning becomes clear once the translation reaches Lord Ello Ebonlocke.",al={"why does air grow heavy","black curtain over land","duskwood dark air"},sp=2},{q="Who should receive the translated letter next?",a="Once Sirra finishes the translation, she instructs you to carry the chilling words directly across the room to Mayor Ello Ebonlocke so the Night Watch can prepare for what is to come.",al={"where do i take the translation","who gets the note next","next step after sirra"}},{q="Is Abercrombie actually an enemy of Darkshire?",a="Yes. While Abercrombie presents himself as a harmless, reclusive old man needing assistance to survive, he is in fact a vengeful necromancer who tricked traveling adventurers into gathering the components needed to construct his monstrous creation.",al={"is abercrombie evil","hermit enemy","abercrombie lore"},sp=2},{q="Why do you have to wait for her?",a="Translating ancient ciphers takes time and focus. The brief delay gives Sirra a moment to parse the hermit's handwriting and coded phrasing before producing the readable transcript for the mayor.",al={"why wait for sirra","how long do i wait","sirra waiting"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire's fragile safety hangs by a thread.",["class:Mage"]="Mages studying arcane scripts and runes will recognize the dark, lingering resonance of a cursed message as its contents are laid bare."},kw={"abercrombie","darkshire","duskwood","ello ebonlocke","sirra von'indi","translation"},rel={"npc:sirra-von-indi","quest:251","quest:252","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Sirra Von'Indi",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=401},src={"Wait for Sirra to Finish"}}
E["quest:453"] = {t="quest",n="Finding the Shadowy Figure",z="duskwood",s="Finding the Shadowy Figure is an Alliance quest that tasks adventurers with tracking down an elusive stranger connected to the tragedy at Sven Yorgen's farm. Guided by clues from Tavernkeep Smitts in Darkshire, travelers scour the haunted woods to the west in search of the fleeing fugitive.",h="Finding the Shadowy Figure is an Alliance quest that tasks adventurers with tracking down an elusive stranger...",sec={{t="On the Trail of a Ghost",b="Following Sven Yorgen's plea to identify the mysterious figure who fled his devastated homestead, the search led straight to the Scarlet Raven Tavern. Tavernkeep Smitts offered a handful of critical observations: the fugitive was a complete stranger to Darkshire, exceptionally nervous and jittery, and had hastily abandoned the town's faint perimeter lamps to vanish into the wilderness to the west.",sp=0},{t="Unmasking Jitters",b="Tracing the stranger westward into the gloom eventually leads to Jitters himself, shivering in fear among the perils of Duskwood. Confronted with the diary recovered from the ruined farm, Jitters collapses in nervous exhaustion, confessing that he authored the tattered journal. Far from being a calculated villain, he reveals himself as a terrified witness who fled the horrors unleashed upon the region, hinting that the diary only captures a fragment of the full nightmare.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the shadowy figure?",a="The shadowy figure is Jitters, a skittish wanderer who inadvertently documented the dark occurrences surrounding Sven Yorgen's farm before fleeing west into the woods.",al={"shadowy figure identity","who is jitters","who is the stranger"},sp=1},{q="Where does Tavernkeep Smitts say the figure went?",a="Smitts notes that the man was an outsider who appeared visibly terrified and fled westward out of Darkshire, braving the dangerous wilderness.",al={"where did he go","where is jitters","which way west"}},{q="Why was Jitters running from Sven's farm?",a="Jitters witnessed unspeakable horrors strike the farmstead and fled for his life, terrified that whatever destroyed Sven's family would come for him next.",al={"why did jitters run","what happened at sven farm","why is jitters scared"},sp=1},{q="What is the book found at Sven's farm?",a="It is a journal written by Jitters detailing the ominous events prior to the massacre at the farmstead. When confronted with it, Jitters admits it only tells half the story.",al={"book from sven's farm","jitters journal","what is the diary"},sp=1},{q="Where can Jitters be found?",a="Jitters hides out in the western wilds of Duskwood, sheltering near the Raven Hill encampment away from Darkshire and the prowling beasts of the forest.",al={"jitters location","where is jitters in duskwood","jitters coordinates"},sp=1},{q="What happens after finding Jitters?",a="Once Jitters confesses to writing the journal, he prepares a complete account of what actually happened, directing you back to Sven Yorgen with the truth.",al={"what next","after finding jitters","where do i go next"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Unraveling Jitters's flight is vital to understanding the growing darkness that threatens the southern frontier of the kingdom.",["class:Rogue"]="Tracking a panicked suspect through dense, shadow-draped woods requires keen observation and tracking skills to separate rumor from true tracks."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","finding the shadowy figure","raven hill","scarlet raven tavern","sven yorgen","tavernkeep smitts"},rel={"quest:266","quest:268","quest:262","npc:jitters","npc:tavernkeep-smitts","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Tavernkeep Smitts",["end"]="Jitters",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=453},src={"Finding the Shadowy Figure"}}
E["quest:5"] = {t="quest",n="Jitters' Growling Gut",z="duskwood",s="Stranded and terrified in the ruins of Raven Hill, the paranoid vagrant Jitters is desperate for real sustenance after subsisting on weeds and insects. He begs passing adventurers to travel east to Darkshire and convince Chef Grual to prepare a hot batch of his famous Dusky Crab Cakes.",h="Stranded and terrified in the ruins of Raven Hill, the paranoid vagrant Jitters is desperate for real...",sec={{t="Starving in Raven Hill",b="Raven Hill has become a den of ravenous undead and lurking beasts, leaving the eccentric hermit Jitters trapped in hiding for weeks. Prowling through dilapidated shanties under perpetual gloom, he has survived solely on dirt-dwelling grubs and wild weeds. Starved of civilized comfort, his nerves and stomach are pushed to their absolute limits.",sp=0},{t="A Plea for Crab Cakes",b="Desperate for any reminder of safety, Jitters dreams of the seasoned seafood patties crafted at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. He sends travelers across the haunted road to seek out Chef Grual, hoping Grual will agree to whip up a batch of Dusky Crab Cakes to quiet his violently growling gut.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jitters?",a="Jitters is a frightened, paranoid man hiding out in the ruined township of Raven Hill in western Duskwood. He is terrified of the undead infestation and constantly lives in fear of starvation and slaughter.",al={"jitters","who is jitters","where is jitters"}},{q="Where can I find Chef Grual?",a="Chef Grual works in the kitchen of the Scarlet Raven Tavern, located in the town of Darkshire along the eastern side of Duskwood.",al={"chef grual location","find grual","scarlet raven chef"}},{q="Why is Jitters eating grubs?",a="Cut off from civilization by hordes of roaming undead and predatory worgen, Jitters has spent weeks pinned down in the ruined town of Raven Hill with no access to provisions other than whatever insects and foliage he can scavenge.",al={"jitters eating bugs","why eats grubs","raven hill food"}},{q="What dish does Jitters want?",a="Jitters craves Dusky Crab Cakes, a regional specialty prepared by Chef Grual at the Scarlet Raven Tavern using coastal ingredients.",al={"jitters food","crab cakes quest","what does jitters want to eat"}},{q="What happens after speaking with Chef Grual?",a="Chef Grual is willing to cook the meal for Jitters, but he lacks fresh ingredients, tasking the adventurer with gathering gooey spider legs to prepare the Dusky Crab Cakes.",al={"after jitters growling gut","next quest jitters gut","chef grual task"},sp=1},{q="Can Horde players complete this quest?",a="No. Both Jitters and the town of Darkshire align with the Alliance, making this errand exclusive to Alliance adventurers.",al={"is jitters alliance only","horde jitters growling gut"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Chef Grual's renowned Dusky Crab Cakes showcase how frontier culinary masters make do with local, exotic ingredients when regular shipments fail to reach Duskwood.",["faction:Alliance"]="Lending aid to Jitters connects travelers with the fragile, struggling settlements and survivors clinging to life in the shadowed corners of Duskwood."},kw={"chef grual","crab cakes","darkshire","growling gut","jitters","raven hill","scarlet raven tavern"},rel={"npc:jitters","npc:chef-grual","quest:93","quest:240","subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","npc:grub"},m={start="Jitters",["end"]="Chef Grual",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=5},src={"Jitters' Growling Gut"}}
E["quest:55"] = {t="quest",n="Morbent Fel",z="duskwood",s="This quest is the final reckoning with Morbent Fel, the necromancer haunting the heights above Raven Hill Cemetery. Armed with the enchanted relic Morbent's Bane, heroes are sent by the grieving Sven Yorgen to shatter the sorcerer's wards and end his reign of terror over western Duskwood.",h="This quest is the final reckoning with Morbent Fel, the necromancer haunting the heights above Raven Hill...",sec={{t="The Perch Above the Dead",b="Morbent Fel makes his lair in an abandoned house perched atop a rocky ridge just east of Sven's camp, overlooking the sprawl of Raven Hill Cemetery. From this grim vantage, the necromancer has directed waves of undead to terrorize the surrounding forest and defile the graves of Duskwood. Protected by formidable dark magic and attended by loyal undead thralls, he has remained untouchable to ordinary steel.",sp=0},{t="Sven's Vengeance",b="Sven Yorgen was driven mad with grief when dark forces butchered his family and drove him into hiding. While Sven knows that the enigmatic Dark Riders of Karazhan are the true culprits behind the massacre at his farm, Morbent Fel's vile sorcery has perpetuated the region's nightmare. Smiting the necromancer offers Sven the only tangible shred of justice left to him in this blighted land.",sp=1},{t="Morbent's Bane",b="Direct assault against Morbent Fel is suicide without supernatural aid; his defensive sorceries deflect conventional attacks. To bypass these wards, Sven entrusts adventurers with Morbent's Bane, an enchanted artifact designed specifically to unravel the necromancer's magical shielding. Once invoked, the barrier collapses, leaving Fel vulnerable to a mortal strike.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Morbent Fel?",a="Morbent Fel is a powerful necromancer who oversees the undead infesting the Raven Hill region. He lurks in a house atop a hill overlooking Raven Hill Cemetery, using dark sorcery to shield himself while tormenting the living of Duskwood.",al={"morbent fel lore","who is morbent fel","morbent fel background"}},{q="Why is Morbent's Bane necessary to kill him?",a="Morbent Fel surrounds himself with potent wards that render him almost completely invulnerable to mundane damage. Morbent's Bane is an enchanted relic specifically forged to dispel these protective enchantments, exposing him to harm.",al={"morbents bane","why use morbents bane","how to beat morbent fel"}},{q="What is Sven Yorgen's connection to Morbent Fel?",a="Sven lost his family and farm to the dark entities stalking Duskwood. While mysterious Dark Riders were responsible for the slaughter, Morbent Fel's necromantic grip on the surrounding countryside represents the festering evil plaguing western Duskwood, making him a prime target for Sven's vengeance.",al={"why does sven want morbent dead","sven yorgen morbent fel","sven revenge"}},{q="Where can Morbent Fel be found?",a="He resides on the upper floor of a decrepit, ruined house located on a hill directly east of Sven Yorgen's camp, looming over the western side of Raven Hill Cemetery.",al={"morbent fel location","where is morbent fel","morbent house"}},{q="Did Morbent Fel kill Sven's family?",a="No. Sven's family was slaughtered by the mysterious Dark Riders seeking the Scythe of Elune. However, Morbent Fel's necromancy plagued the surrounding region and desecrated the graves of Duskwood, making his destruction essential to reclaiming peace.",al={"did morbent kill sven family","who slaughtered sven family"},sp=1},{q="What happens after Morbent Fel is slain?",a="Returning Morbent's Bane to Sven brings the grieving hermit a small measure of solace. Though the elusive Dark Riders remain at large, the elimination of Fel breaks the necromantic grip over Raven Hill and secures the adventurer's reputation across Duskwood.",al={"after morbent fel","quest conclusion","does sven get peace"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Slaying Morbent Fel removes one of the gravest threats looming over the people of Duskwood, securing the road and honoring the suffering of western settlements like Raven Hill.",["class:Paladin"]="Striking down a foul necromancer and purifying Raven Hill of his unnatural wards is a quintessential calling for knights of the Holy Light.",["class:Priest"]="The desecration of Raven Hill Cemetery cries out for spiritual cleansing, making the dispelling of Fel's sorcerous wards a holy duty."},kw={"duskwood","morbent fel","morbent's bane","necromancer","raven hill","raven hill cemetery","sven yorgen"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","zone:duskwood","quest:163","topic:dark-riders"},m={start="Sven Yorgen",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=55},src={"Morbent Fel (quest)"}}
E["quest:56"] = {t="quest",n="The Night Watch",z="duskwood",s="Tasked by Commander Althea Ebonlocke in Darkshire, this mission enlists adventurers to thin the ranks of undead rising in the nearby Tranquil Gardens Cemetery. Abandoned by Stormwind's official garrison, Darkshire's local militia relies on traveling mercenaries to stem the encroaching horrors.",h="Tasked by Commander Althea Ebonlocke in Darkshire, this mission enlists adventurers to thin the ranks of...",sec={{t="Abandoned by the Crown",b="Duskwood once stood under the shield of Stormwind, but as royal resources stretched thin and political discord gripped the capital, the crown withdrew its commissioned soldiers. Darkshire was left largely defenseless against the encroaching shadows. In response, Commander Althea Ebonlocke formed the Night Watch, a homegrown militia composed of local citizens standing between the cursed forest and the town's remaining residents.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Tranquil Gardens",b="South of Darkshire lies the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery, a once-peaceful resting place now crawling with restless skeletons and reanimated spellcasters. With the Night Watch spread perilously thin across Duskwood's borders, Commander Ebonlocke directs incoming adventurers to strike down Skeletal Warriors and Skeletal Mages before the cemetery's dead spill onto the roads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does the Night Watch need outside help?",a="Stormwind recalled its official garrison from Duskwood, leaving the town of Darkshire to fend for itself. The Night Watch is merely a localized militia without the manpower or supplies to fight off the surging undead across the entire territory without auxiliary aid.",al={"why need help","why darkshire weak","why no guards"}},{q="Who is Commander Althea Ebonlocke?",a="Althea Ebonlocke is a relative of Darkshire's mayor, Lord Ello Ebonlocke, and the resolute commander of the Night Watch. She took up the duty of organizing the town's defenses and rallying any able bodies willing to stand against Duskwood's dark menaces.",al={"who is althea","commander ebonlocke","althea ebonlocke lore"}},{q="Where is the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery?",a="Tranquil Gardens Cemetery lies just south of Darkshire. It serves as an active burial site that has fallen victim to the dark magic permeating Duskwood, causing the dead to rise and harass travelers near the town's perimeter.",al={"tranquil gardens location","where is cemetery","where to find skeletons"}},{q="What creatures are rising in the Tranquil Gardens?",a="The cemetery is overrun primarily by animated Skeletal Warriors and Skeletal Mages. Unlike ordinary corpses, these remains retain residual martial skill and arcane power, making them a lethal threat to common townfolk.",al={"what undead are there","skeletons in duskwood"}},{q="Is Stormwind sending any reinforcements?",a="No. Stormwind's regency and military leadership have chosen to consolidate their forces closer to Elwynn Forest and Redridge, leaving the remote frontier of Duskwood entirely to its own devices.",al={"stormwind help duskwood","will stormwind send troops"}},{q="Does this assignment end the threat at the cemetery?",a="No, culling the skeletons at Tranquil Gardens is only the opening effort. The Night Watch faces mounting threats deeper in the woods, requiring further expeditions to manage the territory's worsening corruption.",al={"is this the only quest","night watch chain"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance loyalists, this duty exposes the bitter truth of Stormwind's neglect, showing frontier citizens forced to bleed for their own survival without royal aid.",["class:Paladin"]="Tranquil Gardens represents an affront to the Light, where the desecrated graves of fallen citizens demand consecrated steel and righteous judgment.",["class:Priest"]="Laying these tormented, restless skeletons to rest is an act of spiritual mercy in a land suffocating under sinister curses."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","darkshire","duskwood","night watch","skeletal mage","skeletal warrior","stormwind","tranquil gardens"},rel={"topic:night-watch","npc:althea-ebonlocke","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Commander Althea Ebonlocke",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=56},src={"The Night Watch (Classic)"}}
E["quest:57"] = {t="quest",n="The Night Watch",z="duskwood",s="Tasked directly by Commander Althea Ebonlocke, adventurers are sent into Duskwood's haunted barrows to cull the rising tide of restless dead. This ongoing campaign targets the skeletal horrors clawing their way out of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery and Raven Hill. Driving back the skeletal scourge is essential to keeping the fragile haven of Darkshire from falling completely to the darkness.",h="Tasked directly by Commander Althea Ebonlocke, adventurers are sent into Duskwood's haunted barrows to cull...",sec={{t="The Dead Do Not Rest",b="Duskwood's tragic descent from the verdant region once called Grand Hamlet into a fog-drenched twilight has left its graveyards unnaturally restless. Commander Althea Ebonlocke, leading Darkshire's volunteer militia known as The Night Watch, faces an endless siege. Without aid from Stormwind, her forces are stretched dangerously thin. Reports of animated skeletal fiends and horrors rising from the dirt threaten to overrun the eastern settlements, forcing the militia to recruit any able-bodied travelers willing to enter the deadlands.",sp=0},{t="Haunted Soil",b="The campaign takes recruits to two focal points of necromantic unrest: the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery just south of town, and the vast, overgrown expanses of Raven Hill Graveyard to the far west. Skeletons pull themselves from forgotten tombs and shallow roadside graves, animated by dark magic lingering in the shadowed forest. Cutting down these fiends buys vital breathing room for Darkshire's beleaguered citizens, though it remains a ceaseless battle against an entrenched evil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Night Watch relying on travelers rather than Stormwind guards?",a="Stormwind has largely abandoned Duskwood to its own devices, leaving the defense of the region to Commander Althea Ebonlocke and her local volunteer militia. Facing internal political strife and a missing king, the capital provides no garrison reinforcements, forcing the Night Watch to hire passing adventurers.",al={"why no stormwind help","where is stormwind army","why darkshire alone"}},{q="Where are the skeletons coming from?",a="The skeletal fiends and horrors are clawing out of the consecrated grounds of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery and the sprawling Raven Hill Graveyard. Dark magical forces pervading the woods have disturbed centuries of burials, raising ancient remains as mindless, violent sentries.",al={"skeletons duskwood origin","why are there skeletons","undead source duskwood"}},{q="Who leads the Night Watch?",a="Commander Althea Ebonlocke commands the Night Watch. She is a relative of Darkshire's mayor, Lord Ello Ebonlocke, and she personally directs the defense of the town and coordinates operations against Duskwood's undead and monstrous threats.",al={"night watch leader","who is althea ebonlocke","commander ebonlocke"}},{q="What is the difference between Tranquil Gardens and Raven Hill?",a="Tranquil Gardens Cemetery lies immediately south of Darkshire and represents an immediate, localized threat to the town. Raven Hill Graveyard, situated across the forest to the far west, is a massive burial ground that serves as the heart of Duskwood's undead infestation.",al={"tranquil gardens vs raven hill","which graveyard is better","graveyard locations duskwood"}},{q="What happens after culling these skeletons?",a="Clearing skeletal horrors and fiends is only one phase of Althea's campaign. The Night Watch continuously monitors rising threats across the forest, escalating from ghouls and skeletons to more dangerous undead and the sinister necromancers directing them deeper within Duskwood.",al={"what next night watch","night watch questline","after night watch 2"}},{q="Why is Darkshire in constant danger?",a="Once a peaceful province of the Kingdom of Stormwind known as Grand Hamlet, Duskwood was consumed by a magical twilight and plagued by shadowy curses. The woods are now overrun with feral worgen, ravenous spiders, and restless undead, leaving Darkshire as the last bastion of living humanity in the zone.",al={"why duskwood dangerous","darkshire danger","what cursed duskwood"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire represents the fragile southeastern border of the Alliance in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. Aiding the Night Watch ensures the town remains a viable foothold rather than falling completely to ruin.",["class:Paladin"]="For the Silver Hand and knights of the Light, confronting the defiled dead in Tranquil Gardens is a sacred duty to cleanse corrupted resting places.",["class:Priest"]="Priests walking the tainted soil of Raven Hill face the raw perversion of burial traditions, using their faith to bring quiet rest to tormented souls.",["race:Human"]="Many of the skeletons rising from Duskwood's earth are the ancestors of living Stormwind and Darkshire citizens, making the battle deeply personal for human defenders."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","darkshire","duskwood","night watch","raven hill","skeletal fiend","skeletal horror","tranquil gardens"},rel={"quest:56","npc:althea-ebonlocke","topic:night-watch","zone:duskwood","subzone:darkshire","subzone:tranquil-gardens-cemetery","quest:163"},m={start="Commander Althea Ebonlocke",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=57},src={"The Night Watch (2)"}}
E["quest:58"] = {t="quest",n="The Night Watch",z="duskwood",s="This final mission from Commander Althea Ebonlocke directs Alliance adventurers into the crypts of eastern Raven Hill Cemetery. With the Night Watch spread thin defending Darkshire, outsiders must enter the tombs to exterminate the teeming plague spreaders. It marks the culmination of the town guard's direct military campaign to contain the undead overrun.",h="This final mission from Commander Althea Ebonlocke directs Alliance adventurers into the crypts of eastern...",sec={{t="A Desperate Frontier",b="Darkshire stands almost entirely isolated, abandoned by the Stormwind military and reliant entirely on its own civilian militia, the Night Watch. Commander Althea Ebonlocke has exhausted her limited manpower simply guarding the crossroads, town perimeter, and supply lines. As the restless dead multiply throughout Duskwood, the commander has no choice but to deputize wandering champions to carry the fight directly into the shadowed recesses of Raven Hill.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Mausoleum",b="The eastern mausoleum in Raven Hill Cemetery represents one of the most hazardous concentrations of undeath in the region. Unlike the open barrows, this stone crypt teems with plague spreaders—ghouls bearing corrupting afflictions capable of sickening the living. Clearing out twenty of these abominations buys precious breathing room for the weary Night Watch, ensuring Darkshire does not face a coordinated undead surge from the west.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Night Watch sending adventurers instead of their own men?",a="The Night Watch is stretched thin across all of Duskwood. With Stormwind providing no official troops, Commander Althea Ebonlocke barely has enough guards to hold Darkshire's perimeter and monitor the roads, leaving no spare militia to clear deep, fortified crypts like Raven Hill.",al={"why help darkshire","why the night watch needs help","night watch low numbers"}},{q="Where is the eastern mausoleum located?",a="It is situated in the eastern portion of Raven Hill Cemetery, located in northwestern Duskwood. The entrance leads underground into stone crypts where plague spreaders gather.",al={"where are plague spreaders","eastern mausoleum location","where is the mausoleum"}},{q="What makes the plague spreaders dangerous?",a="Plague spreaders are ravenous ghouls carrying virulent decay. Left unchecked, their foul corruption threatens to spread beyond the cemetery and taint the surviving residents of Darkshire.",al={"why kill plague spreaders","what are plague spreaders"}},{q="Who is Commander Althea Ebonlocke?",a="Althea Ebonlocke is the commander and leader of the Night Watch, as well as a relative of Darkshire's mayor, Lord Ello Ebonlocke. She organizes the defense of Duskwood from inside Darkshire.",al={"who is althea","commander ebonlocke","who leads the night watch"}},{q="Does completing this chain end the undead threat in Duskwood?",a="No. While thinning out the mausoleum eases immediate pressure on Darkshire, Raven Hill remains thoroughly infested, and darker powers throughout Duskwood continue to stir the dead.",al={"is raven hill saved","is darkshire safe now"}},{q="How does this fit into the Night Watch questline?",a="This is the third and final chapter in Commander Ebonlocke's direct 'The Night Watch' martial series, moving from the open roads to the graveyard outskirts, and finally deep into the mausoleum.",al={"what chain is this","is this the last night watch quest"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="With the royal crown in Stormwind ignoring Duskwood's pleas, Alliance champions must personally step up to save loyal citizens from being overrun by the undead.",["class:Paladin"]="Raven Hill's plague-ridden vaults represent an unholy mockery of sacred burial rites, making the purge of its crypts a vital duty for servants of the Holy Light.",["class:Priest"]="The vile contagion spread by the ghouls in the eastern mausoleum challenges the Light's sanctity, demanding spiritual and physical cleansing."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","darkshire","duskwood","ghouls","mausoleum","night watch","plague spreaders","raven hill","undead"},rel={"topic:night-watch","npc:althea-ebonlocke","quest:56","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","quest:163","topic:light"},m={start="Commander Althea Ebonlocke",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=58},src={"The Night Watch (3)"}}
E["quest:66"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="The Legend of Stalvan begins in Darkshire with a foreboding vision from the town diviner, Madame Eva. Disturbed by an omen portending death for her granddaughter Alyssa, Eva draws upon her cards and trance visions to divine a single lingering name: Stalvan. To untangle this thread of dread, she sends travelers to consult town records in the Darkshire Town Hall.",h="The Legend of Stalvan begins in Darkshire with a foreboding vision from the town diviner, Madame Eva.",sec={{t="A Vision of Death",b="In the perpetual gloom of Duskwood, Madame Eva serves as Darkshire's resident seer, interpreting portents and reading cards for troubled locals. After being jolted awake by a terrible disturbance, Eva consulted her divination deck, only to draw the Death card in connection to her young granddaughter, Alyssa. Falling into a deep, shadowy trance to pierce the gloom, she pulled forth only a single clue: the name Stalvan. Terrified of what this omen means for her family and the town, she turns to capable adventurers to follow the thread before tragedy strikes.",sp=0},{t="Inquiries at Town Hall",b="Eva knows that uncovering the truth of Stalvan requires looking into Darkshire's written history. She directs adventurers across the square to the Darkshire Town Hall to speak with Clerk Daltry, the municipal keeper of ledgers and public archives. Daltry oversees the township's dusty documents, making him the only person capable of determining whether Stalvan was a former resident, a traveler passing through, or something far more sinister buried in Duskwood's past.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Madame Eva?",a="Madame Eva is a fortune teller and diviner who lives in Darkshire. She uses cards and trance rituals to glimpse portents of the future and senses magical disturbances shifting across Duskwood.",al={"madame eva","who is eva","darkshire fortune teller"}},{q="Why does Madame Eva need help?",a="Madame Eva experienced a terrifying vision indicating that her granddaughter Alyssa is in mortal danger. Her cards drew the Death card, and her trance yielded only the name 'Stalvan', prompting her to seek outside aid to investigate the threat.",al={"why start stalvan","eva vision","why help eva"}},{q="Who is Clerk Daltry?",a="Clerk Daltry is the civic record keeper stationed inside the Darkshire Town Hall. He manages the town's ledgers, registries, and historical documents, making him the best person to ask about unfamiliar names.",al={"clerk daltry","daltry","who is town clerk"}},{q="What is Darkshire Town Hall?",a="The Darkshire Town Hall is the administrative center of the town, housing the local government officials, historical records, and the Night Watch's command staff.",al={"darkshire town hall","town hall duskwood"}},{q="Who is Alyssa?",a="Alyssa is Madame Eva's young granddaughter living in Darkshire. Eva's reading revealed that Alyssa is targeted by a deadly omen connected to someone named Stalvan.",al={"alyssa","madame eva granddaughter"}},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Speaking to Clerk Daltry reveals town records and past inquiries, beginning an extensive investigation across Duskwood and neighboring regions to uncover Stalvan's history and fate.",al={"stalvan next step","what does daltry say"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As Duskwood struggles without regular army support from Stormwind, Alliance adventurers frequently step in to assist town elders and protect vulnerable families like Madame Eva's.",["class:Priest"]="Priests walking the dark roads of Darkshire often take heed of spiritual warnings, making Madame Eva's chilling death omens an urgent matter of pastoral duty."},kw={"alyssa","clerk daltry","darkshire","death card","duskwood","madame eva","stalvan","town hall"},rel={"npc:madame-eva","npc:clerk-daltry","subzone:darkshire-town-hall","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Madame Eva",["end"]="Clerk Daltry",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=66},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (Classic)"}}
E["quest:67"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This errand begins the paper trail into the fate of Stalvan Mistmantle, sent by Clerk Daltry from the town hall of Darkshire. His oldest records point across kingdom borders to the abandoned Moonbrook Schoolhouse in Westfall, setting off a classic investigation into an ordinary man's unraveling.",h="This errand begins the paper trail into the fate of Stalvan Mistmantle, sent by Clerk Daltry from the town...",sec={{t="The Town Clerk's Request",b="After the initial inquiries in Darkshire, Clerk Daltry pulls the town registry to locate Stalvan Mistmantle. To his surprise, the ledger hasn't been updated in years and lists Stalvan's last known residence far to the west, at the schoolhouse in Moonbrook. Unaware of the sinister nature of the investigation, Daltry treats it as routine bureaucratic upkeep, asking travelers to look into the address and gather whatever records might bring Darkshire's dusty archives up to date.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Moonbrook",b="Following the trail means venturing beyond the gloom of Duskwood into the lawless dust of Westfall. Moonbrook, once a thriving agricultural settlement, now crawls with Defias Brotherhood outlaws. Near the center of the derelict town stands its abandoned schoolhouse, standing quiet amid the bandit occupation. Inside, an old footlocker holds the first tangible clues to Stalvan's past life as an educator, as well as a lingering, restless sorrow bound to the chest.",sp=0},{t="A Tragic Haunting",b="Disturbing the old footlocker reveals more than just forgotten pages; it summons a Forlorn Spirit that attacks anyone unearthing Stalvan's past. The apparition's mournful magic curses intruders and hints at an unresolved tragedy tied to the schoolmaster's departure from Westfall, marking the transition of a simple historical inquiry into an active haunting.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Clerk Daltry?",a="Clerk Daltry is the town records keeper situated in the Darkshire Town Hall in Duskwood. He assists by searching the local registry for mention of Stalvan Mistmantle, only to find ancient, outdated entries.",al={"daltry","darkshire clerk","who starts legend of stalvan 2"}},{q="Where is the Moonbrook Schoolhouse?",a="The schoolhouse is located in Moonbrook in southwestern Westfall. It resembles the Darkshire town hall in architecture and stands in the middle of town, surrounded by hostile Defias bandits.",al={"moonbrook schoolhouse location","where is the schoolhouse","where is stalvan footlocker"}},{q="What is inside the Old Footlocker?",a="The footlocker holds old records and personal belongings from Stalvan Mistmantle's tenure as an instructor in Moonbrook, providing the next lead in the search for his whereabouts.",al={"stalvan footlocker","what is in the footlocker"}},{q="Why does a ghost attack when opening the footlocker?",a="Opening the footlocker summons a Forlorn Spirit that attacks with polymorph and curses. The restless apparition is bound to the dark tragedy surrounding Stalvan's past and his departure from Moonbrook.",al={"forlorn spirit","why does a ghost spawn","curse of stalvan ghost"},sp=1},{q="Why did Stalvan leave Westfall?",a="Stalvan served as a schoolmaster in Moonbrook before moving on to seek private tutoring employment elsewhere in the kingdom, leaving his old schoolhouse belongings locked away in the abandoned town.",al={"why did stalvan leave moonbrook","stalvan moonbrook history"}},{q="Is Moonbrook safe to enter?",a="No. Moonbrook has fallen entirely under the control of the Defias Brotherhood, meaning anyone seeking the schoolhouse must fight through armed thieves and outlaws.",al={"is moonbrook dangerous","mobs in moonbrook"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This leg of the investigation highlights how deeply the kingdom's rural towns have fractured, forcing heroes to trek through Defias-occupied Westfall just to resolve a Darkshire town registry query.",["class:Mage"]="The Forlorn Spirit that guards the footlocker uses polymorphism and debilitating curses, offering an eerie encounter with sorrow-bound magic in an otherwise mundane classroom setting."},kw={"daltry","duskwood","footlocker","forlorn spirit","mistmantle","moonbrook","schoolhouse","stalvan","westfall"},rel={"npc:clerk-daltry","subzone:moonbrook-schoolhouse","subzone:moonbrook","zone:westfall","zone:duskwood","quest:938"},m={start="Clerk Daltry",["end"]="Old Footlocker",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=67},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (2)"}}
E["quest:68"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This investigation unearths a forgotten chapter in the dark tale of Stalvan Mistmantle. A dusty, unsent letter pulled from a neglected footlocker in Moonbrook provides tangible proof of where he stayed before his vanished trail turned cold, leading back to Darkshire's records.",h="This investigation unearths a forgotten chapter in the dark tale of Stalvan Mistmantle.",sec={{t="A Forgotten Trace in Moonbrook",b="While tracking down the history of Stalvan Mistmantle, an old footlocker tucked away in Moonbrook yields a vital piece of the puzzle: a dusty, unsent letter. Moonbrook, once a thriving agricultural settlement, fell into ruin and now teems with outlaws and restless specters. Stalvan's presence here was brief enough to escape common memory, but this neglected missive definitively places him in the hamlet.",sp=0},{t="A Haunting at the Footlocker",b="Digging into Stalvan's belongings does not go unnoticed. Disturbing the chest stirs a Forlorn Spirit from the shadows, eager to guard the secrets left behind. The specter lashes out with bewitching magic and the debilitating Curse of Stalvan, suggesting that whatever fate befell the man, sorrow and dark enchantment cling heavily to his remaining possessions.",sp=1},{t="Updating the Town Registry",b="Delivering the letter back across the border to Darkshire gives Clerk Daltry the missing documentation he needs. While Daltry finds it peculiar that the letter was never mailed, the evidence is indisputable. With the Moonbrook connection verified, the bureaucratic paper trail can finally guide the investigation toward where Stalvan fled next.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the old footlocker in Moonbrook?",a="Inside the footlocker is a Dusty Unsent Letter written during Stalvan Mistmantle's stay in Moonbrook. It serves as tangible evidence confirming his residence in the town before he disappeared.",al={"what did i find","footlocker contents","stalvan letter"}},{q="Why does a spirit attack when the chest is opened?",a="A Forlorn Spirit lingers near Stalvan's forgotten possessions, rising to assault anyone who disturbs the trunk. It wields unsettling magic, including fears, polymorph spells, and the lingering Curse of Stalvan.",al={"forlorn spirit","why am i attacked","footlocker ghost"}},{q="Why take the letter to Clerk Daltry?",a="Clerk Daltry oversees the town records and registry in Darkshire's town hall. He requires concrete documentation to confirm Stalvan's past whereabouts before he can assist in tracking him further.",al={"who is clerk daltry","why daltry","darkshire town hall"}},{q="Why is it significant that the letter was never sent?",a="The fact that the letter remained tucked away and abandoned in an abandoned footlocker hints at an abrupt departure or growing paranoia, reinforcing the eerie secrecy surrounding Stalvan's movements.",al={"unsent letter mystery","why wasn't it mailed"}},{q="What does the Curse of Stalvan do?",a="Inflicted by the Forlorn Spirit that guards the footlocker, the Curse of Stalvan is a debilitating hex that dampens all primary attributes of its victim for ten minutes.",al={"curse of stalvan debuff","spirit curse"}},{q="Where does the trail lead after giving the letter to Daltry?",a="Once Clerk Daltry updates the municipal registry with this proof from Moonbrook, he is able to direct your inquiries toward Stalvan's subsequent known destination.",al={"what next","where after daltry","next clue"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Unraveling the mystery of Stalvan Mistmantle aids the beleaguered town of Darkshire in cataloging the shadowy figures that have crossed through the region's borders.",["class:Priest"]="The manifestation of a Forlorn Spirit bound to a simple chest of keepsakes speaks to an agonizing emotional burden that refused to rest after death.",["class:Mage"]="The hostile shade guarding the footlocker wields deceptive arcane tools like polymorph alongside a crippling curse, hinting at the unnatural forces woven into Stalvan's wake."},kw={"clerk daltry","curse of stalvan","darkshire","duskwood","dusty unsent letter","footlocker","forlorn spirit","mistmantle","moonbrook","stalvan"},rel={"npc:clerk-daltry","subzone:moonbrook","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Old Footlocker",["end"]="Clerk Daltry",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=68},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (3)"}}
E["quest:69"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This errand marks a pivotal turn in the search for the elusive Stalvan Mistmantle, leading investigators out of the gloom of Duskwood and back toward the heart of the kingdom. A hasty, scratched-out entry discovered in Darkshire's town registry points across the river to Goldshire. Following the paper trail to the bustling Lion's Pride Inn is the next step in uncovering where the mysterious tutor went.",h="This errand marks a pivotal turn in the search for the elusive Stalvan Mistmantle, leading investigators out...",sec={{t="A Clue in the Ledger",b="While reviewing Darkshire's records, Clerk Daltry catches an oversight in the town registry. Tucked beneath an earlier entry for Stalvan Mistmantle lies a second destination, hastily written and partially scratched out as if someone had second thoughts or meant to obscure their movements. The note indicates that Stalvan intended to travel northwest toward Elwynn Forest, specifically to the Lion's Pride Inn.",sp=0},{t="Crossing into Elwynn",b="Departing the shadowed groves of Duskwood for the sunny roads of Goldshire offers a stark contrast, but the shadow of Stalvan's past reaches even here. The Lion's Pride Inn serves as the bustling crossroads of Elwynn Forest, welcoming travelers, merchants, and soldiers alike. Innkeeper Farley presides over the busy taproom, making him the ideal person to ask about an educated wanderer seeking lodging.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does the trail lead to Goldshire?",a="Clerk Daltry discovered a second, partially scratched-out address in the Darkshire registry beneath Stalvan's initial listing. It clearly indicated he was bound for the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",al={"why goldshire","why go to goldshire","stalvan in goldshire"}},{q="Who is Clerk Daltry?",a="Clerk Daltry is the record keeper stationed in the town hall of Darkshire. He maintains the local registries and helps dig up historical documents regarding past residents.",al={"daltry","who is daltry"}},{q="Who do I speak to at the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="You need to speak directly with Innkeeper Farley, who manages the Lion's Pride Inn and keeps track of travelers and patrons passing through Goldshire.",al={"who to talk to","lion's pride contact","innkeeper goldshire"}},{q="Why was the entry scratched out in the registry?",a="The ledger entry was only partially erased, suggesting a rushed or deliberate attempt to conceal Stalvan's route toward Elwynn Forest when he departed Duskwood.",al={"scratched out note","why scratched out"}},{q="Does this quest involve any combat?",a="No. This step of the investigation is purely a matter of travel and inquiry, taking you safely from Darkshire's Town Hall to the taproom in Goldshire.",al={"is there fighting","do i fight anything"}},{q="What is the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn is the central hub of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. It is a well-known resting point for travelers journeying between Stormwind City, Westfall, and Duskwood.",al={"lions pride inn","goldshire inn"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="Retracing Stalvan's steps takes you through the heartland of the Kingdom of Stormwind, linking the haunted frontiers of Duskwood back to the familiar comforts of Elwynn Forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="Unraveling local histories and cold trails across the southern Alliance territories requires navigating between frontier outposts like Darkshire and core hamlets like Goldshire."},kw={"clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","elwynn forest","goldshire","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","stalvan"},rel={"npc:clerk-daltry","npc:innkeeper-farley","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire","zone:duskwood","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Clerk Daltry",["end"]="Innkeeper Farley",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=69},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (4)"}}
E["quest:70"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This leg of the investigation directs searchers to an abandoned letter left behind at Goldshire's inn years ago. Following the trail of Stalvan Mistmantle leads out of Elwynn Forest and into Stormwind's Canal District.",h="This leg of the investigation directs searchers to an abandoned letter left behind at Goldshire's inn years...",sec={{t="A Midnight Terror",b="When Innkeeper Farley of the Lion's Pride Inn is asked about Stalvan Mistmantle, he recalls a stormy night years ago. A traveling courier had sought shelter from the pouring rain, only to rush downstairs around midnight in sheer panic. Dressed in only his sleepwear, the courier bolted straight out into the dark storm and was never seen again.",sp=0},{t="The Leftover Parcel",b="In his panicked flight, the courier abandoned his satchel and personal chest in the upstairs room. Among the forgotten cargo lay an unsent letter bearing the name Stalvan, addressed to someone residing in the Canal District of Stormwind City. The chest remained untouched at the foot of the bed until Farley permitted it to be opened.",sp=0},{t="A Chilly Welcome",b="Carrying the long-overdue letter into Stormwind leads to Caretaker Folsom, who watches over property along the canals near the Park. Rather than gratitude for completing a neglected delivery, the mention of Stalvan's name and the sight of his handwriting provokes immediate disgust and hostility, suggesting deep-seated scandals tied to the sender.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the undelivered letter kept?",a="The letter sits in a storage chest on the upper floor of the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. Climb the stairs, turn right, and enter the bedroom with the bed; the chest rests at the foot of the bed frame.",al={"find letter","stalvan chest location","where is the chest"}},{q="Why was the letter never delivered originally?",a="The courier took shelter from a downpour at the Lion's Pride Inn years ago. Near midnight, something terrified him so severely that he fled into the storm wearing only his nightclothes, leaving his chest and deliveries behind.",al={"why abandoned letter","what scared the courier","why did messenger run"}},{q="Where do I find Caretaker Folsom in Stormwind?",a="Caretaker Folsom stands along the Canals in Stormwind City, close to the edge of the Park district.",al={"folsom location","where is caretaker folsom","canal district turn in"}},{q="Why is Caretaker Folsom angry about receiving the letter?",a="Folsom immediately recognizes Stalvan's handwriting and name, reacting with indignation. Stalvan Mistmantle left behind bitter memories and outrage among the people connected to his past in Stormwind.",al={"why is folsom mad","folsom reaction","you have some nerve"}},{q="How does this connect to the trouble in Duskwood?",a="The town council in Darkshire is investigating a lingering evil tied to the name Stalvan Mistmantle. Uncovering who Stalvan was in life requires retracing his earlier travels and associations through Elwynn Forest and Stormwind.",al={"why duskwood quest in goldshire","how does this relate to duskwood"}},{q="What happens after giving the letter to Caretaker Folsom?",a="Caretaker Folsom's sharp response opens up the Stormwind chapter of the investigation, pushing you to uncover Stalvan's former employment and the grim events that unfolded with the noble family he served.",al={"next step","what follows this quest"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Unraveling the mystery of Stalvan requires traveling through the heartlands of the Alliance, retracing an old trail from the sleepy hamlet of Goldshire to the capital's grand canals.",["race:Human"]="This investigation exposes the darker undercurrents of the Kingdom of Stormwind, showing that the evils haunting Duskwood have roots stretching right back to the capital's doorstep."},kw={"canals","caretaker folsom","goldshire","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","mistmantle","stalvan","stormwind","undelivered letter"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-farley","npc:caretaker-folsom","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:park","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Innkeeper Farley",["end"]="Caretaker Folsom",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=70},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (5)"}}
E["quest:72"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This leg of the investigation directs searchers to the Canals of Stormwind City, where Caretaker Folsom watches over the remaining possessions of the ruined Flintridge family. Looking for answers regarding the mysterious Stalvan Mistmantle, adventurers must dig through crated estate goods while confronting restless spirits tied to a past massacre.",h="This leg of the investigation directs searchers to the Canals of Stormwind City, where Caretaker Folsom...",sec={{t="Echoes of a Massacre",b="Tracking Stalvan's movements leads out of the shadowed groves of Duskwood and into the heart of Stormwind. Beside the city canals, Caretaker Folsom looks after what little remains of the Flintridge household. According to Folsom, his father served the estate before him and had the grisly task of mopping up blood in the wake of a horrific household slaughter—a tragedy with Stalvan at its center.",sp=0},{t="The Auction of a Ruined House",b="With the Flintridge trust funds entirely drained and royal tax vultures circling, the family's surviving heirlooms and packed belongings are slated for auction. Whatever keepsakes and papers survived the bloodshed sit piled into shipping crates along the canal embankment. Uncovering Stalvan's trail requires prying open these sealed boxes before the estate's remaining worldly goods are scattered to collectors across the kingdom.",sp=0},{t="A Restless Shade",b="Disturbing the crates of the deceased does not go unnoticed. The trauma of the murders still clings to these salvaged possessions, manifesting as a vengeful Forlorn Spirit that attacks anyone probing the family effects. This weeping apparition, believed to be the phantom of young Tilloa Flintridge, remains fiercely tethered to the physical relics of her abruptly stolen life.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Caretaker Folsom?",a="Caretaker Folsom is stationed along the Canals in Stormwind City, standing near a stack of discarded shipping crates and house goods beside the waterway.",al={"caretaker folsom location","where is folsom","where is caretaker folsom in stormwind"}},{q="What happened to the Flintridge family?",a="The Flintridges were a wealthy household torn apart by a sudden and vicious massacre. As caretaker lore reveals, the bloodbath was so extensive that Folsom's father had to mop the estate clean, leaving Stalvan Mistmantle implicated as the perpetrator.",al={"flintridge massacre","what was the massacre","who killed the flintridge family"}},{q="Why are the family's possessions packed in crates along the canal?",a="The Flintridge family trust completely dried up following the tragedy. Facing pressure from kingdom tax collectors, the estate's surviving belongings were crated and staged by the canals to be liquidated at auction.",al={"why auction flintridge items","why are crates in the canals","flintridge trust"}},{q="Why does a spirit attack when the crate is opened?",a="The violent trauma of the massacre left the victims' souls bound to their former belongings. The Forlorn Spirit that manifests to defend the crates is widely believed to be the shade of Tilloa Flintridge, one of the murdered children.",al={"forlorn spirit stormwind","who is the forlorn spirit","why ghost in stormwind canals"}},{q="How does this connect back to Duskwood?",a="The investigation began in Darkshire as a missing-person inquiry into Stalvan Mistmantle. Tracing his history led back to his time as a tutor for the Flintridge family in Elwynn and Stormwind before the fatal bloodbath forced him into the shadows.",al={"stalvan duskwood connection","why are we in stormwind for a duskwood quest","legend of stalvan city connection"}},{q="What do you find inside the sealed crate?",a="Rifling through the packed furniture and personal items yields documentary evidence and journal remnants that further unravel Stalvan's unhinged mindset and his obsession with the household.",al={"what is in the crate","sealed crate clue","flintridge crate contents"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The quiet tragedy of the Flintridge family unfolds right within the kingdom's capital, exposing how even Stormwind's most sheltered noble lines can be violently undone.",["class:Priest"]="Confronting the weeping Forlorn Spirit in the city canals reveals the lingering torment of innocent souls murdered before their time, demanding peace from the Light."},kw={"canals","caretaker folsom","duskwood","flintridge","forlorn spirit","legend of stalvan","massacre","sealed crate","stormwind","tilloa"},rel={"npc:caretaker-folsom","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Caretaker Folsom",["end"]="Sealed Crate",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=72},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (6)"}}
E["quest:74"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This step in the investigation leads deep into an old crate of Flintridge heirlooms left beside the canals of Stormwind City. Sifting through the dusty relics uncovers a torn journal page, offering a vital handwritten clue to the past life of Stalvan Mistmantle that leads to Marshal Haggard in Elwynn Forest.",h="This step in the investigation leads deep into an old crate of Flintridge heirlooms left beside the canals of...",sec={{t="Unearthing the Past",b="While digging through a sealed crate filled with musty heirlooms, old hunting trophies, and family portraits, investigators uncover a lone torn journal page hidden beneath a ceramic vase. Written in Stalvan Mistmantle's own hand, this remnant provides an intimate glimpse into the mind of a reclusive scholar before tragedy struck.",sp=0},{t="A Marshal's Fading Sight",b="Marshal Haggard, now aged and plagued by failing eyesight, struggles to read the script on the battered parchment. Even so, the distinctive handwriting strikes an uneasy chord in his memory, recalling documents and incidents from years past before the darkness took his sight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the sealed crate located?",a="The sealed crate sits by the Canals of Stormwind City, directly behind Caretaker Folsom among the Flintridge family's packed-up belongings. The page you find there is then taken to Marshal Haggard in southeastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"crate location","where is crate","haggard crate"}},{q="What is inside the sealed crate?",a="The crate contains dusty heirlooms, a family portrait, old books, hunting trophies, and a ceramic vase, beneath which lies a torn page from Stalvan's journal.",al={"crate contents","what is in the crate","torn page crate"}},{q="Who is Marshal Haggard?",a="Marshal Haggard is an elderly, retired officer of Stormwind living alone in southern Elwynn Forest. Despite his failing eyesight and frailty, his memories of old records and travelers make him a crucial witness to past events.",al={"who is haggard","marshal haggard lore","old marshal elwynn"}},{q="Why is this journal page important?",a="The torn journal page is direct evidence written by Stalvan Mistmantle himself. Its distinctive penmanship and lingering thoughts help tie disparate accounts across Duskwood and Elwynn back to his personal downfall.",al={"why torn page matters","journal page clue","stalvan journal"}},{q="What happens when the crate is opened?",a="Disturbing the remnants of Stalvan's past stirs the restless dead, causing a vengeful Forlorn Spirit to manifest and strike at those trying to unravel the tragedy.",al={"forlorn spirit spawn","ghost after crate","why did a ghost attack me"}},{q="Where does the investigation lead next?",a="After presenting the torn page to Marshal Haggard, his recollection of the handwriting guides the investigation onward to find more surviving fragments of Stalvan's history.",al={"next step","after torn page","where do I go next"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating old cold cases in the heart of Elwynn reveals how deeply personal horrors can slip past the eyes of Stormwind's marshals.",["race:Human"]="Marshal Haggard represents the aging veteran generation of Stormwind, holding vital memories of the kingdom before the First and Second Wars tore families apart."},kw={"duskwood","elwynn forest","forlorn spirit","marshal haggard","mistmantle","sealed crate","stalvan","torn journal page"},rel={"quest:1666","zone:elwynn","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Sealed Crate",["end"]="Marshal Haggard",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=74},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (7)"}}
E["quest:75"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This investigation into Stalvan Mistmantle leads out of Duskwood to an isolated home in southeastern Elwynn Forest. Marshal Haggard, an aging veteran whose eyesight has deteriorated, directs you to an upstairs chest containing an old bundle of papers left behind when he moved in.",h="This investigation into Stalvan Mistmantle leads out of Duskwood to an isolated home in southeastern Elwynn...",sec={{t="A Veteran's Attic",b="Marshal Haggard lives far from town on the southeastern fringes of Elwynn Forest, near the borders of Duskwood and Redridge. When he moved into his secluded home, he found a chest tucked away upstairs packed with old parchments. With his failing eyesight clouding over, he abandoned any effort to read them, leaving the documents undisturbed until an investigator comes asking about Stalvan.",sp=0},{t="Lingering Shadows",b="The papers left in the upstairs chest are not ordinary household debris. Disturbance of Stalvan's belongings routinely agitates restless magic, drawing forth a Forlorn Spirit bound to Mistmantle's past. The journal page hidden inside provides a direct record of Stalvan's private writings, offering concrete proof that the reclusive scholar left his mark in Elwynn before vanishing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal Haggard?",a="Marshal Haggard is an elderly, near-blind veteran living quietly in a secluded cabin in southeastern Elwynn Forest. He holds onto long-forgotten papers discovered inside his house that belonged to Stalvan Mistmantle.",al={"marshal haggard","haggard elwynn","who is haggard"}},{q="Why did the trail lead back to Elwynn Forest?",a="Clues gathered in Darkshire and Moonbrook trace Stalvan's wanderings across southern Stormwind territory. Haggard's homestead held old possessions Stalvan discarded or left behind before his descent into madness.",al={"why elwynn forest","stalvan elwynn","why go to haggard"}},{q="What is inside the chest upstairs?",a="The chest contains a faded journal page written by Stalvan Mistmantle, preserved among a bundle of parchments that Haggard never managed to inspect properly.",al={"upstairs chest","faded journal page","what is in the chest"}},{q="Why does a spirit attack when the chest is opened?",a="A Forlorn Spirit haunts the relics of Stalvan's former life, manifesting violently when an outsider disturbs his personal writings and memories.",al={"forlorn spirit","why ghost attacks","ghost in haggard house"}},{q="How does this advance the Stalvan investigation?",a="The faded page provides firsthand evidence in Stalvan's own hand, helping assemble the tragic chronology of his employment, unrequited obsession, and eventual murder spree.",al={"stalvan mystery","what does the page reveal","stalvan questline step"},sp=1},{q="Why couldn't Marshal Haggard read the papers himself?",a="Haggard's eyesight has grown hazed and weak with age, preventing him from deciphering small or weathered handwriting on the faded documents.",al={"haggard blind","why haggard needs help"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Unraveling Stalvan's legacy exposes dark chapters tucked quietly inside Elwynn's otherwise peaceful pastoral borders.",["race:Human"]="Stalvan's path winds through ordinary human settlements, serving as a cautionary tale of isolation and malice hidden in plain sight."},kw={"duskwood","elwynn forest","faded journal page","forlorn spirit","marshal haggard","stalvan"},rel={"zone:elwynn","zone:duskwood","quest:1666"},m={start="Marshal Haggard",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=75},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (8)"}}
E["quest:78"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This errand marks a turning point in uncovering the history of Stalvan Mistmantle, sending investigators from Elwynn Forest back into the shadowed town of Darkshire. Guided by Marshal Haggard's memory of his service days, you bring a recovered journal page to Tavernkeep Smitts at the Scarlet Raven Tavern to identify the chilling handwriting.",h="This errand marks a turning point in uncovering the history of Stalvan Mistmantle, sending investigators from...",sec={{t="A Lead from the Marshal",b="After recovering a weathered, torn journal page from Marshal Haggard's chest in Elwynn Forest, the retired commander cannot read the faded script due to his failing eyesight. Recognizing that the trail leads back across the river, Haggard recalls his past commanding the Stormwind Guard and remembers spending evenings at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. He directs you to Tavernkeep Smitts, a barkeep whose long tenure has made him an unofficial custodian of local history and rumors.",sp=0},{t="Return to the Scarlet Raven",b="Crossing back through the gloomy woods of Duskwood, you present the faded manuscript to Smitts behind his counter. Smitts immediately softens upon hearing the name of his old acquaintance Haggard, though he laments the veteran's fading health. Upon laying eyes on the parchment, the barkeep's easygoing demeanor instantly shatters into alarm: he recognizes the distinctive script without a shadow of doubt, pulling the investigation closer to the horrifying truth of Stalvan's madness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Marshal Haggard send me back to Darkshire?",a="Marshal Haggard is aging and nearly blind, preventing him from examining the recovered journal page himself. He recalls that Tavernkeep Smitts of the Scarlet Raven Tavern was an expert on local lore and history when Haggard served with the Stormwind Guard, making Smitts the ideal person to identify the script.",al={"why go to darkshire","haggard to darkshire","why smitts"}},{q="Where is Tavernkeep Smitts located?",a="Tavernkeep Smitts tends the bar inside the Scarlet Raven Tavern, situated on the eastern side of Darkshire in Duskwood.",al={"where is smitts","smitts location","scarlet raven tavern location"}},{q="What item do you carry to Tavernkeep Smitts?",a="You bring a Faded Journal Page, an excerpt from Stalvan Mistmantle's lost journal that was previously found secured inside Marshal Haggard's footlocker.",al={"what item","faded journal page","stalvan journal page"}},{q="Does Tavernkeep Smitts recognize the handwriting?",a="Yes. The moment Smitts inspects the faded page, he swears by the Light in shock, instantly recognizing the distinctive handwriting of Stalvan Mistmantle.",al={"does smitts know the writing","smitts reaction to journal"}},{q="How does Smitts know Marshal Haggard?",a="Smitts hosted Haggard years ago when Haggard led patrols of the Stormwind Guard into Duskwood and frequented the Scarlet Raven Tavern for drinks.",al={"smitts haggard relationship","how smitts knows haggard"}},{q="What comes next in the search for Stalvan?",a="Recognizing the handwriting, Smitts provides the next vital clue pointing deeper into Duskwood, guiding you toward unraveling Stalvan's tragic history and fate.",al={"what is next","next step stalvan","stalvan chain continue"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The quest highlights the deep bonds among former defenders of the realm, connecting retired Stormwind guardsmen to community keepers across the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="This step reveals the grim memories lurking within human settlements, showing how past tragedies in Grand Hamlet and Darkshire refuse to stay buried."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","elwynn","journal","marshal haggard","mistmantle","scarlet raven tavern","stalvan","tavernkeep smitts"},rel={"quest:1666","npc:tavernkeep-smitts","subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Haggard",["end"]="Tavernkeep Smitts",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=78},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (9)"}}
E["quest:79"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This quest marks the moment where scattered rumors about Stalvan Mistmantle solidify into undeniable proof of a brutal crime. Tavernkeep Smitts hands over long-hidden muddy journal pages, directing the investigator straight to Night Watch Commander Althea Ebonlocke.",h="This quest marks the moment where scattered rumors about Stalvan Mistmantle solidify into undeniable proof of...",sec={{t="A Breakthrough in Darkshire",b="For years, the grim fate of a visiting noble family remained an unresolved tragedy in Duskwood. Tavernkeep Smitts and Marshal Haggard, then a leader of the Stormwind Guard, originally investigated the massacre site and discovered a handful of torn, muddy journal pages. Without handwriting samples or corroborating papers, the notes sat cold, unable to officially implicate the recluse rumored to dwell in the wilderness. The evidence gathered across Elwynn, Westfall, and Duskwood finally connects the handwriting to Stalvan Mistmantle, turning town gossip into an open-and-shut case of murder.",sp=0},{t="Taking It to the Watch",b="Darkshire lives under constant siege from the undead, feral beasts, and worse horrors stalking the forest gloom. Commander Althea Ebonlocke has little patience for tall tales or ungrounded suspicions when the survival of her town hangs by a thread. Delivering these muddy pages bridges the gap between cold history and immediate military justice. Presented with concrete proof of a massacre on Duskwood soil, the Night Watch is finally forced to recognize Stalvan Mistmantle not just as an eccentric hermit or ghost story, but as a dangerous fugitive demanding retribution.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What evidence did Tavernkeep Smitts have all along?",a="Years ago, Smitts joined Haggard to investigate the slaughter of visiting nobles. They recovered torn, muddy journal pages from the scene, but lacked matching handwriting samples to prove Stalvan Mistmantle was the author until now.",al={"smitts journal pages","muddy journal pages","what did smitts find"}},{q="Why didn't Smitts report this to Commander Ebonlocke earlier?",a="Without proof linking the handwriting on the muddy pages to the reclusive tutor, Smitts and Haggard only held circumstantial scraps. Presenting unsubstantiated rumors to Commander Ebonlocke would have been dismissed as an unhelpful waste of the Night Watch's strained time.",al={"why wait so long","why keep the pages secret","why didn't smitts tell the guard"}},{q="Who is Commander Althea Ebonlocke?",a="Commander Althea Ebonlocke is the leader of the Night Watch, the beleaguered town militia responsible for guarding Darkshire and patrolling Duskwood's roads against the Scourge and woodland predators.",al={"who is ebonlocke","althea ebonlocke role","commander of darkshire"}},{q="What massacre took place in Duskwood?",a="A visiting noble family was butchered in Duskwood several years prior. While rumors pointed to their former tutor, Stalvan Mistmantle, local investigators initially lacked the definitive evidence needed to charge him.",al={"what massacre","slaughter of nobles","who was murdered"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the overall investigation?",a="This step represents the transition from private investigation to formal justice. After scouring registries, school records, and family crates across three territories, you hand the assembled evidence over to the local authorities to sanction action against Stalvan.",al={"stalvan quest chain step","how far in is this","is this the end of the quest"}},{q="Why is the Night Watch so reluctant to investigate old crimes?",a="Darkshire faces immediate, daily extinction from wandering abominations, worgen packs, and spiders. Commander Ebonlocke must focus every available watchman on survival, meaning cold cases require undeniable proof before she will spare personnel.",al={"why is ebonlocke busy","darkshire defense priority","night watch priorities"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The investigation demonstrates how the southern territories must lean on wandering Alliance heroes to enforce justice when Stormwind's official support is entirely absent.",["class:Paladin"]="Bringing long-buried murders to the light fulfills the calling of a paladin, demanding accountability for innocent lives violently taken in the shadows of Duskwood.",["class:Rogue"]="Piecing together handwriting samples across taverns and dusty trunks reflects the patient detective work often necessary to track elusive quarry."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","ebonlocke","investigation","mistmantle","muddy journal","night watch","smitts","stalvan"},rel={"subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","npc:althea-ebonlocke","npc:tavernkeep-smitts","topic:light"},m={start="Tavernkeep Smitts",["end"]="Commander Althea Ebonlocke",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=79},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (10)"}}
E["quest:80"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This crucial step in the investigation of Stalvan Mistmantle brings the gathered evidence before Darkshire's authorities. With a bloodstained journal page in hand, Commander Althea Ebonlocke directs the investigator to Clerk Daltry to authenticate the handwriting once and for all.",h="This crucial step in the investigation of Stalvan Mistmantle brings the gathered evidence before Darkshire's...",sec={{t="Closing the Net",b="Following the trail of journal pages recovered across Duskwood and the surrounding human territories, the Night Watch finally holds what appears to be damning evidence against the elusive tutor, Stalvan Mistmantle. Commander Althea Ebonlocke has harbored suspicions about the man for some time, but bringing formal judgment requires absolute certainty. A single bloodstained page is not enough to pass sentence until it can be proven beyond doubt that the macabre scribblings originated from Stalvan's own hand.",sp=0},{t="The Clerk's Eye",b="To bridge the gap between suspicion and certainty, the Night Watch relies on Darkshire's town archivist, Clerk Daltry. Having overseen the town registry for years, Daltry has examined countless ledgers and signatures, making him an authority on handwriting identification. Comparing the newly discovered journal page directly against Stalvan's historical signatures in the town records provides the final, incontrovertible match needed to confirm his dark descent and guilt.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Commander Ebonlocke need Clerk Daltry's confirmation?",a="Commander Althea Ebonlocke wants to ensure Stalvan's guilt is established beyond a shadow of a doubt before taking final action. Clerk Daltry maintains Darkshire's town registry and has extensive experience examining signatures, making him uniquely qualified to verify whether the bloodstained page matches Stalvan's handwriting in the town records.",al={"why daltry","why check handwriting","clerk daltry purpose"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the Legend of Stalvan storyline?",a="This is the eleventh chapter of the lengthy investigation. It takes place immediately after recovering the bloodstained journal page and serves as the final evidentiary verification before the Night Watch takes decisive steps against Stalvan.",al={"what part is this","how far in chain","stalvan quest chain order"}},{q="Where is Clerk Daltry located in Darkshire?",a="Clerk Daltry can be found inside Darkshire's town hall, managing the local records and property registries for the community.",al={"daltry location","where is clerk daltry","find daltry"}},{q="What evidence did the investigator bring to Darkshire?",a="The investigator carries a bloodstained journal page recovered during the ongoing search into Stalvan's whereabouts. The writing describes his grim thoughts and experiences, but requires handwriting verification against official records.",al={"what is the evidence","what page is this","bloodstained page lore"}},{q="Does Clerk Daltry confirm the handwriting is Stalvan's?",a="Yes. Upon reviewing the bloodstained page alongside the town registry entries, Clerk Daltry confirms that the handwriting perfectly matches the signatures Stalvan left behind in Darkshire.",al={"does the handwriting match","is it stalvan","did stalvan write it"},sp=1},{q="Why is the Night Watch so cautious about accusing Stalvan?",a="Even in the troubled, isolated forest of Duskwood, the Night Watch strives to maintain lawful order. Accusing a former scholar of horrific crimes requires concrete, verifiable proof rather than mere rumor or conjecture.",al={"why proof needed","why not just kill stalvan","ebonlocke suspicion"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The investigation highlights how frontier towns like Darkshire strive to maintain law, order, and civil records despite being besieged by undead and shadowed beasts.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the southern kingdoms, this quest touches on the interconnected tragedies linking Stormwind nobility, Duskwood settlers, and the scattered manors of Elwynn."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","bloodstained journal page","clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","legend of stalvan","night watch","stalvan mistmantle"},rel={"npc:althea-ebonlocke","npc:clerk-daltry","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Commander Althea Ebonlocke",["end"]="Clerk Daltry",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=80},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (11)"}}
E["quest:90"] = {t="quest",n="Seasoned Wolf Kabobs",z="duskwood",s="Seasoned Wolf Kabobs is an Alliance culinary quest offered by Chef Grual at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. Grual seeks to prepare his signature house dish, tasking adventurers with hunting wild wolves in Duskwood and fetching rare seasoning herbs from a flower shop in Stormwind City. It highlights the everyday survival challenges and resourcefulness required to keep a besieged hamlet fed.",h="Seasoned Wolf Kabobs is an Alliance culinary quest offered by Chef Grual at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in...",sec={{t="A Dish for Darkshire",b="Darkshire is an isolated settlement surrounded by the creeping horrors of Duskwood, where trade caravans rarely venture and normal agriculture has completely collapsed. Despite the ever-present gloom and lurking undead, the town's citizens still require sustenance. Chef Grual, presiding over the kitchens of the Scarlet Raven Tavern, makes practical use of the forest's dangerous fauna by transforming wild wolf meat into hearty skewers. Because local timber and soil cannot sustain delicate crops, Grual relies on specialized spices brought in from the capital to make the gamey forest meat palatable.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Stormwind",b="To complete Grual's recipe, travelers must secure lean flanks from the ferocious wolves stalking Duskwood and travel north to Stormwind. The required seasoning herbs are sold by herbalist and florist Felicia Gump, whose canal-side shop, Fragrant Flowers, borders the city's Trade District and Old Town. This errand underscores Darkshire's delicate connection to the broader kingdom: while royal military aid has dwindled, small-scale civic ties and supply lines between the city merchants and outer hamlets still barely endure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Chef Grual?",a="Chef Grual is the town cook stationed at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. He keeps the patrons, locals, and Night Watch members fed, crafting hearty meals out of whatever game can be hunted in the surrounding woods.",al={"chef grual","grual darkshire","who gives seasoned wolf kabobs"}},{q="Where do you get the Stormwind Seasoning Herbs?",a="The seasoning herbs are procured from Felicia Gump, who runs the Fragrant Flowers shop in Stormwind City. Her storefront is situated along the canal path between the Trade District and Old Town.",al={"stormwind herbs location","felicia gump location","where are seasoning herbs"}},{q="Where are the wolves for the wolf flanks found?",a="Wild wolves roam throughout the dark forests of Duskwood, particularly stalking the groves and pathways just outside Darkshire. Any of the local wolves yield the lean meat Chef Grual requires.",al={"lean wolf flank location","wolf flanks duskwood","where to hunt wolves"}},{q="Why does Darkshire need wolf meat for food?",a="Duskwood's farmland is ruined and cut off by monsters, making traditional livestock and crop cultivation virtually impossible. The locals survive by hunting the dangerous wildlife prowling outside their borders, including the ubiquitous wolves.",al={"why eat wolves","darkshire food supply","why wolf kabobs"}},{q="Why can't Grual get herbs locally in Duskwood?",a="The pervasive curse blighting Duskwood has corrupted much of the native plant life, leaving little in the way of edible or fragrant cooking herbs. Grual must rely on cultivated varieties imported from Stormwind to season his dishes.",al={"why buy herbs in stormwind","duskwood herbs"}},{q="Does this quest tie into a larger storyline?",a="It is a standalone local flavor quest rather than part of a grand narrative. However, it vividly illustrates the rustic, self-reliant lifestyle of Darkshire's folk and their ongoing, tenuous supply link back to Stormwind.",al={"wolf kabobs lore significance","is seasoned wolf kabobs important"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Chef Grual's recipe teaches adventurers how wilderness hunters make use of tough predator meat by masking wild gaminess with refined city spices.",["faction:Alliance"]="The delivery run between Darkshire and Stormwind demonstrates how isolated settlements in the kingdom rely on the capital's markets even when military garrisons are withheld.",["class:Hunter"]="Tracking down Duskwood's ravenous wolf packs requires classic tracking and culling skills to protect the hamlet while keeping the tavern larder stocked."},kw={"chef grual","darkshire","duskwood","felicia gump","fragrant flowers","lean wolf flank","scarlet raven tavern","stormwind","wolf kabobs"},rel={"npc:chef-grual","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","subzone:trade-district","subzone:old-town","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Chef Grual",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=90},src={"Seasoned Wolf Kabobs (Classic)"}}
E["quest:93"] = {t="quest",n="Dusky Crab Cakes",z="duskwood",s="Chef Grual of Darkshire's Scarlet Raven Tavern has a secret behind his famous Dusky Crab Cakes: they contain no crab at all. Tasked with aiding the famished and nervous Jitters, adventurers are sent to harvest spider legs from the deadly arachnids roaming northern Duskwood to prepare the town's beloved snack.",h="Chef Grual of Darkshire's Scarlet Raven Tavern has a secret behind his famous Dusky Crab Cakes: they contain...",sec={{t="A Questionable Delicacy",b="Duskwood has long suffered from isolation, dark magic, and severed supply routes, forcing the locals of Darkshire to adapt their cuisine. Chef Grual, the resident cook at the Scarlet Raven Tavern, solved his meat shortages by inventing the Dusky Crab Cake. Despite the name suggesting seafood from distant shores, Grual readily admits that the dish's distinctively tangy flavor comes entirely from the gooey legs of local giant spiders.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Venom Webs",b="To fulfill the order, Grual directs hunters north toward the foothills and riverbanks where Venom Web Spiders spin their snares. In a gloomy forest crawling with undead and feral beasts, harvesting fresh spider meat is hazardous work, yet it remains one of the few readily available protein sources in the blighted woods. Grual fries the seasoned arachnid limbs on a hot skillet until they skitter to a crisp.",sp=0},{t="Comfort for a Cursed Soul",b="The culinary errand is born out of concern for Jitters, an agitated vagrant sheltering in the abandoned village of Raven Hill in western Duskwood. Consumed by guilt and trembling terror after inadvertently unleashing horrors upon the region, Jitters can think of little else besides his starving stomach. A hot batch of Grual's savory spider cakes serves as a rare, albeit bizarre, comfort in his wretched exile.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Are Dusky Crab Cakes actually made of crab?",a="No. Chef Grual openly confesses to adventurers that Dusky Crab Cakes are made entirely from gooey spider legs. Darkshire has no access to the sea or fresh crab, so Grual relies on local giant spiders to mimic the texture and deliver a sharp, tangy snack.",al={"is it real crab","crab cakes secret","what are crab cakes made of"}},{q="Where does Chef Grual get the spider legs?",a="Grual relies on adventurers to harvest gooey legs from Venom Web Spiders. These aggressive arachnids nest predominantly in northern Duskwood, between the forest foothills and the river.",al={"where to find spider legs","spider locations duskwood","venom web spiders location"}},{q="Who are these crab cakes being made for?",a="While Grual serves them to patrons in Darkshire, this particular batch is ordered for Jitters. Jitters is a frightened hermit starving out in the ghost town of Raven Hill in western Duskwood, desperate for something to fill his growling stomach.",al={"who wants the crab cakes","who eats the crab cakes","why make crab cakes"}},{q="Will Chef Grual teach me how to make Dusky Crab Cakes?",a="Chef Grual keeps his precise recipe for Dusky Crab Cakes a strictly guarded secret, refusing to share his trademark spice blend. However, he does reward helpful adventurers with an alternative recipe from his culinary repertoire.",al={"can i learn crab cakes recipe","crab cake recipe cooking"}},{q="Why does Darkshire rely on spiders for food?",a="Duskwood's roads are besieged by undead, Nightbane worgen, and hostile creatures, severely disrupting trade caravans and farming. As fresh livestock and imported goods are scarce, Darkshire's inhabitants make creative use of whatever wildlife they can catch.",al={"why eat spiders in darkshire","duskwood food shortages"}},{q="Does Jitters know the cakes are made of spiders?",a="Jitters specifically craves Grual's famous crab cakes and cares little about the ingredients. Paralyzed by dread and starvation out in the woods, he is eager for any familiar meal from Darkshire, regardless of its creepy origin.",al={"does jitters know about the spiders","jitters reaction to spider meat"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Chef Grual demonstrates the grit required of frontier cooks, showing that even terrifying wilderness predators like giant venomous spiders can be turned into a town's prized regional delicacy.",["faction:Alliance"]="The dish illustrates the precarious state of the Alliance's southern frontier, where towns like Darkshire are pushed to subsisting on giant vermin due to neglected infrastructure and severed supply lines."},kw={"chef grual","darkshire","duskwood","dusky crab cakes","jitters","scarlet raven tavern","spider legs","venom web spider"},rel={"quest:5","quest:240","npc:chef-grual","npc:jitters","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Chef Grual",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=93},src={"Dusky Crab Cakes (Classic)"}}
E["quest:95"] = {t="quest",n="Sven's Revenge",z="duskwood",s="Driven by grief and vengeance, the hermit Sven Yorgen asks travelers to return to his ruined farmstead in eastern Duskwood. While he spent years pursuing the shadowy horsemen who slaughtered his family, a suspicious figure once buried something near his barn that may hold answers.",h="Driven by grief and vengeance, the hermit Sven Yorgen asks travelers to return to his ruined farmstead in...",sec={{t="Tragedy at the Farmstead",b="Sven Yorgen was once a simple farmer working the fields in southeastern Duskwood. His life shattered when hooded Dark Riders riding down from Deadwind Pass attacked his homestead, massacring his family while he was away. Returning to the slaughter, Sven caught sight of an unknown figure skulking near the barn, frantically burying something in the earth. Sven chose vengeance, setting off immediately to hunt down the killers, leaving whatever had been concealed behind.",sp=0},{t="Unearthing Secrets",b="Now camped in the western hills and consumed by wrath, Sven needs someone to return to the Yorgen Farmstead. Behind an old tree stump sitting between the farmhouse and the ruined barn lies a mound of loose dirt hastily piled together. Recovering whatever is buried there is the first step toward understanding why the shadowy riders targeted a quiet Duskwood farmer in the first place.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sven Yorgen?",a="Sven Yorgen was an ordinary farmer who lived in southeastern Duskwood near the border of Deadwind Pass. After returning home to find his family murdered by sinister riders, he abandoned his farm and became a recluse obsessed with seeking vengeance against those responsible.",al={"who is sven","sven lore","sven backstory"}},{q="What happened to Sven's farm?",a="Sven's farmstead was raided by the mysterious Dark Riders coming out of Deadwind Pass. They slaughtered his entire family, leaving the property in ruins before Sven could return to defend them.",al={"yorgen farmstead tragedy","what happened to sven farm","why is sven farm destroyed"}},{q="Who buried something behind the barn?",a="Sven saw a shadowy figure lurking near his barn burying an object just after the massacre took place. Sven fled into the wilds chasing the Dark Riders before he could catch the stranger or unearth what was hidden.",al={"who buried the item","shadowy figure sven farm","who dug the mound"}},{q="Where is the mound of loose dirt located?",a="The mound of loose dirt is found at the Yorgen Farmstead in southeastern Duskwood, buried directly behind an old tree stump between the barn and the ruined farmhouse.",al={"where is the dirt mound","dirt mound location","where is the stump"}},{q="Who are the Dark Riders?",a="The Dark Riders are ominous, hooded horsemen that ride out of Deadwind Pass. Little is known about their origins, but their violent incursions into Duskwood leave only death and ruin in their wake.",al={"what are the dark riders","dark riders lore","riders of deadwind pass"}},{q="Why didn't Sven dig up the buried item himself?",a="When Sven returned home and saw the figure burying the item, he was consumed by grief and immediately pursued the retreating Dark Riders. By the time he established his hidden camp, the farm was overrun and too painful for him to revisit directly.",al={"why didn't sven check the dirt","why did sven leave"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The slaughter of the Yorgen family is yet another sign of Duskwood's isolation, showing how far the reaches of dark forces extend without regular Stormwind army patrols.",["class:Paladin"]="The violent slaughter of innocents by sinister forces out of Deadwind Pass calls for righteous retribution and justice for the dead."},kw={"dark riders","deadwind pass","duskwood","mound of loose dirt","stump","sven yorgen","sven's revenge","yorgen farmstead"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","subzone:yorgen-farmstead","topic:dark-riders","quest:164","quest:230","zone:duskwood","zone:deadwind"},m={start="Sven Yorgen",["end"]="Mound of loose dirt",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=95},src={"Sven's Revenge"}}
E["quest:97"] = {t="quest",n="The Legend of Stalvan",z="duskwood",s="This leg of the investigation finally confirms the sinister truth connecting the elusive tutor to Darkshire's records. Clerk Daltry successfully matches the handwriting found on the recovered documents to Stalvan Mistmantle, prompting an immediate report to Commander Althea Ebonlocke. It marks the moment the Night Watch's suspicions harden into undeniable fact.",h="This leg of the investigation finally confirms the sinister truth connecting the elusive tutor to Darkshire's...",sec={{t="A Match in the Records",b="After combing through distant manors, inns, and municipal archives across the human kingdoms, the fragmented trail returns to Darkshire's town hall. Clerk Daltry examines the recovered writing samples and compares them against local registries. The result is unequivocal: the penmanship belongs to Stalvan Mistmantle. Any remaining doubt over whether the tutor had truly passed through Duskwood dissolves, providing the Night Watch with the hard evidence needed to treat the matter as an urgent local threat.",sp=0},{t="The Night Watch's Suspicions",b="Commander Althea Ebonlocke had harbored grim instincts regarding Stalvan from the start of the inquiry. Duskwood already buckles under the weight of feral worgen, skeletal undead, and lurking necromancers; an unaccounted-for murderer hiding within the shadows of the woods is a danger she cannot ignore. Receiving confirmation from Daltry validates her darkest fears and sets the Night Watch on course to locate and neutralize the recluse once and for all.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What did Clerk Daltry discover?",a="Clerk Daltry compared the collected writings from your travels against official records and confirmed that the handwriting was an exact match for Stalvan Mistmantle. This proved that the suspect was indeed the same tutor who once resided in town.",al={"what did daltry find","daltry handwriting match","stalvan handwriting proof"}},{q="Why does Commander Althea Ebonlocke care so much about Stalvan?",a="Commander Althea Ebonlocke leads the Night Watch, Darkshire's beleaguered militia. In a land already beset by terrors, she cannot allow a violent, shadowy figure with a dark past to remain loose and unaccounted for within Duskwood's borders.",al={"why does althea care","ebonlocke investigation","night watch stalvan"}},{q="Where does this step take place?",a="This entire step takes place within the town of Darkshire. Clerk Daltry is stationed inside the town hall, while Commander Althea Ebonlocke can be found patrolling nearby along the town's central roads.",al={"where is this quest","quest location","darkshire stalvan turn in"}},{q="What happens after reporting the handwriting match?",a="Once Commander Ebonlocke receives the confirmation from Clerk Daltry, the investigation turns toward actively hunting down Stalvan's current whereabouts in the haunted wilds of Duskwood.",al={"what next stalvan","after daltry match","next step stalvan chain"}},{q="Who was Stalvan Mistmantle originally?",a="Stalvan Mistmantle was a schoolteacher and private tutor originally from Duskwood. After seeking employment abroad, his life took a dark and tragic turn, eventually drawing him back to his native woods as a dangerous recluse.",al={"who is stalvan","stalvan background","stalvan mistmantle story"}},{q="Why was handwriting analysis necessary?",a="Because the events and accusations surrounding Stalvan occurred across different regions—including Moonbrook and Goldshire—official records were disjointed. Darkshire's civic registry held verified local samples that could definitively tie the foreign clues to the specific man.",al={"why match handwriting","why did daltry check writing","proving stalvan identity"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance investigators, unraveling Stalvan's trail demonstrates the vital cooperation required between Darkshire's battered leadership and wandering adventurers to keep the realm's southern territories secure.",["race:Human"]="Human players see the tragic decay of their own society reflected here, where respected tutors and rural towns alike slip quietly from civilization into madness and isolation."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","handwriting","mistmantle","night watch","stalvan"},rel={"npc:clerk-daltry","npc:althea-ebonlocke","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood"},m={start="Clerk Daltry",["end"]="Commander Althea Ebonlocke",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=97},src={"The Legend of Stalvan (12)"}}
E["subzone:addle-s-stead"] = {t="subzone",n="Addle's Stead",z="duskwood",s="Addle's Stead is an abandoned farmstead in southwestern Duskwood, lying quiet under the forest's gloom south of Raven Hill. While its original homesteaders fled long ago, the farm has become a hidden staging ground for the Defias Brotherhood.",h="Addle's Stead is an abandoned farmstead in southwestern Duskwood, lying quiet under the forest's gloom south...",sec={{t="A Outpost in the Dark",b="Like many of the forgotten homesteads scattered across Duskwood, Addle's Stead fell into disrepair when darkness and ruin enveloped the region. Rather than remaining empty, the farm has been repurposed by the Defias Brotherhood. Agents prowl the perimeter, lurk within the decrepit farmhouse, and stash supplies in the barn, using the shadowy cover of southwestern Duskwood to escape the notice of both the Night Watch and Stormwind authorities.",sp=0},{t="Tangled in the King's Disappearance",b="The presence of the Defias here goes beyond simple banditry. Addle's Stead functions as an operational safehouse holding sensitive records for the Brotherhood. Crucial documents and dockets linking regional conspirators to the disappearance of King Varian Wrynn can be traced back to this very plot of land, turning an unassuming derelict farm into a vital thread in unraveling treason within the Alliance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Addle's Stead located?",a="Addle's Stead is in southwestern Duskwood, situated just south of the Raven Hill township and directly west of the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound.",al={"addle's stead location","where is addles stead","find addles stead"}},{q="Who controls Addle's Stead right now?",a="The farmstead is heavily occupied by the Defias Brotherhood, including night runners, night blades, and enchanters who use the old house and barn as a remote hideout.",al={"who is at addles stead","mobs at addles stead","addles stead enemies"}},{q="Why is the farm abandoned?",a="Like much of Duskwood, the farm was abandoned by its original inhabitants when the forest fell under a pervasive curse of darkness, beasts, and undead, driving common folk away.",al={"what happened to the farm","who was addle","why is addles stead ruined"}},{q="What brings Alliance adventurers to Addle's Stead?",a="Adventurers investigating the disappearance of King Varian Wrynn are guided toward Addle's Stead to retrieve an important Defias docket linking rogue agents to the royal abduction.",al={"why go to addles stead","addles stead quest","missing king duskwood"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance investigators tracking the missing King Varian Wrynn, this dilapidated farmhouse holds vital conspiratorial dockets left by the Defias Brotherhood.",["class:Rogue"]="The covert outpost shows how deeply the Defias syndicates slip unnoticed across territorial borders, embedding their operatives behind the veil of Duskwood's gloom."},kw={"addle's stead","addles stead","defias","defias brotherhood","duskwood","raven hill"},rel={"zone:duskwood","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:varian-wrynn","quest:163","subzone:vul-gol-ogre-mound","topic:alliance"},src={"Addle's Stead"}}
E["subzone:beggar-s-haunt"] = {t="subzone",n="Beggar's Haunt",z="duskwood",s="Beggar's Haunt is an abandoned Stormwind scout tower perched on a hillside in northeastern Duskwood, near the mountain road to Deadwind Pass. While originally built to keep watch over the kingdom's eastern borders, it has become an outpost for Forsaken infiltrators deep within Alliance territory.",h="Beggar's Haunt is an abandoned Stormwind scout tower perched on a hillside in northeastern Duskwood, near the...",sec={{t="A Watchtower in the Shadows",b="Perched above the foggy hills east of Manor Mistmantle, Beggar's Haunt was once an active observation post manned by the Stormwind Guard to secure the eastern approaches to the realm. As Grand Hamlet collapsed into the gloom of modern Duskwood and kingdom patrols withdrew to Darkshire, the stone tower was abandoned to the elements. Today, its commanding vantage point serves a far more sinister purpose: agents of the Forsaken, including members of the Royal Apothecary Society and Deathstalkers, use the ruined stronghold to conduct research and monitor the region under the Alliance's nose.",sp=0},{t="Knight's Hollow and the Forgotten Dead",b="Behind the tower, a steep, twisting path descends to a secluded pool and waterfall known as Knight's Hollow. Here lies an unmarked grave flanked by two ominous hooded stone statues resembling the guardians flanking the Dark Portal. Nearby resting plots, including the burial site of an Unknown Soldier, speak to forgotten clashes fought along this frontier long before the Forsaken moved into the watchtower.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there Forsaken at Beggar's Haunt?",a="Agents from the Undercity, including Apothecary Faustin of the Royal Apothecary Society and Deathstalker Zraedus, have claimed the abandoned watchtower. From here, they can monitor Alliance movements and quietly carry out experiments far to the south.",al={"who is at beggars haunt","why is horde here","undead at beggars haunt"}},{q="Was this tower originally built by the Forsaken?",a="No. The tower was constructed as a scout outpost by the kingdom of Stormwind. When local defenses faltered and the region deteriorated into Duskwood, the Stormwind Guard abandoned it, leaving it empty until Forsaken scouts seized it.",al={"who built beggars haunt","beggars haunt history","is this an alliance tower"}},{q="What is the strange grave behind the tower?",a="Down the path behind the haunt lies Knight's Hollow, a secluded waterfall pool featuring an unmarked grave framed by hooded guardian statues identical in style to the monuments flanking the Dark Portal.",al={"knights hollow statues","grave behind tower","dark portal statues duskwood"}},{q="Is Beggar's Haunt hostile to Alliance travelers?",a="Yes. The Forsaken stationed at the tower are seasoned agents who will strike down any Alliance adventurers that wander too close to their hillside redoubt.",al={"will they attack me","beggars haunt guards","is beggars haunt safe"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The presence of Forsaken agents stationed inside an old Stormwind scout tower just off the main road is an alarming sign of Horde infiltration right on Darkshire's doorstep.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken operatives, this secluded outpost offers a rare and dangerous foothold deep within the human lands of the south."},kw={"apothecary faustin","beggar's haunt","deathstalker zraedus","duskwood","knight's hollow","scout tower","stormwind guard"},rel={"zone:duskwood","topic:forsaken","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:stormwind-guard","subzone:manor-mistmantle","zone:deadwind","subzone:darkshire","subzone:dark-portal"},src={"Beggar's Haunt"}}
E["subzone:brightwood-grove"] = {t="subzone",n="Brightwood Grove",z="duskwood",s="Brightwood Grove is a shadowed expanse of woodland located just west of Darkshire in Duskwood. Once part of the region's serene agrarian landscape, it is now infested with savage Nightbane worgen who make camp among ruined homesteads and attack any travelers wandering too close.",h="Brightwood Grove is a shadowed expanse of woodland located just west of Darkshire in Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Grove in Shadow",b="Situated within sight of Darkshire's perimeter, Brightwood Grove represents the creeping peril threatening the town's borders. The homesteads and fences that once demarcated peaceful farmland now lie collapsed and rotting. In their place, crude camps have been erected by the Nightbane worgen, who prowl the overgrown clearings. The proximity of these wolf-beasts poses an ongoing threat to the town, forcing the Night Watch and passing adventurers to continually cull their numbers before the settlement is overrun.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Brightwood Grove?",a="Brightwood Grove is located in eastern Duskwood, lying just west of the town of Darkshire along the main paths.",al={"brightwood grove location","where is brightwood grove","brightwood duskwood"}},{q="What creatures inhabit Brightwood Grove?",a="The grove is heavily infested by savage Nightbane worgen. These cursed wolf-men have established crude camps throughout the ruined buildings and attack anyone who approaches.",al={"monsters in brightwood grove","brightwood enemies","what lives in brightwood"}},{q="Why is the grove dangerous to Darkshire?",a="Because Brightwood Grove sits immediately west of Darkshire, the aggressive worgen packs lurking in the brush are an immediate hazard to town patrols, supply lines, and any travelers arriving along the road.",al={"why is brightwood grove dangerous","darkshire brightwood threat"}},{q="Are there any friendly settlements in the grove?",a="No. The few stone buildings and farmsteads on the outskirts of the grove lie entirely in ruins, abandoned to the elements and occupied by roving worgen.",al={"is anyone friendly in brightwood","brightwood town"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Brightwood Grove sits right outside the gates of Darkshire, making the elimination of its worgen packs vital to keeping the beleaguered town from being cut off from the west.",["class:Hunter"]="The dark thickets of the grove provide harsh terrain for tracking the vicious Nightbane, testing any hunter's awareness against ambushes lurking behind the tree line."},kw={"brightwood grove","darkshire","duskwood","night watch","nightbane","wolf men","worgen"},rel={"zone:duskwood","subzone:darkshire","topic:worgen","topic:alliance"},src={"Brightwood Grove"}}
E["subzone:darkened-bank"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkened Bank",z="duskwood",s="The Darkened Bank is the northern shoreline of Duskwood, bordering the river that separates the shadowed woods from Elwynn Forest. Stretching from the far west all the way east toward the Redridge Mountains, it marks the boundary between the relative safety of the north and the dark terrors of the forest.",h="The Darkened Bank is the northern shoreline of Duskwood, bordering the river that separates the shadowed...",sec={{t="A Precarious Boundary",b="Running along the southern bank of the river opposite Elwynn Forest, the Darkened Bank forms the northern edge of Duskwood. It extends from the western riverbends east toward the stone span leading to the Redridge Mountains. While visually gloomy under the pervasive canopy of Duskwood's curse, this shoreline is often the first foothold for travelers venturing south from Elwynn. Near its far western tip sits a makeshift campsite where displaced refugees, including Sven Yorgen and Lars, have taken shelter just barely outside the grasp of the deep woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Darkened Bank located?",a="The Darkened Bank stretches across the entire northern shore of Duskwood along the river, directly across the water from Elwynn Forest. It extends from the far western edges of the zone east to the bridge crossing into the Redridge Mountains.",al={"darkened bank location","where is darkened bank","darkened bank duskwood"}},{q="Who lives along the Darkened Bank?",a="A modest refuge camp sits at the far western edge of the bank, occupied by Sven Yorgen and Lars. Driven from their former lives deeper in the territory, they use this northern riverbank as a fragile haven while looking for aid against the threats of Duskwood.",al={"camp on darkened bank","who is at darkened bank","darkened bank npcs"}},{q="How do travelers usually reach this area?",a="Travelers can easily reach the western stretch of the Darkened Bank by swimming south across the river from the southwestern reaches of Elwynn Forest, or by following the northern riverbank west from the Redridge bridge.",al={"how to get to darkened bank","getting to darkened bank"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers heading out of Elwynn Forest, the Darkened Bank serves as an initial staging ground before venturing deeper into the haunted heart of Duskwood."},kw={"darkened bank","duskwood","elwynn forest","lars","river","shoreline","sven yorgen"},rel={"zone:duskwood","zone:elwynn","zone:redridge","npc:sven-yorgen","npc:lars"},src={"Darkened Bank"}}
E["subzone:darkshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkshire",z="duskwood",s="Darkshire, formerly known as Grand Hamlet, is a battered settlement in eastern Duskwood. Cloaked in an enduring, unnatural gloom and neglected by Stormwind, the town survives only through the vigilance of the Night Watch and the stubborn endurance of its people.",h="Darkshire, formerly known as Grand Hamlet, is a battered settlement in eastern Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Town Abandoned",b="Once a peaceful woodland settlement called Grand Hamlet, the village was razed by the Old Horde during the First War and later rebuilt. Its fortune turned truly bitter following the fall of Medivh at Karazhan, whose lingering death throes cursed Brightwood into the shadowy wilderness now called Duskwood. Despite being a nominal holding of the Kingdom of Stormwind, the town hall receives virtually no aid from the crown. Political paralysis in Stormwind City has left the garrison unstaffed and the borders unpatrolled, forcing Mayor Ello Ebonlocke and the local council to administer their own harsh, insular justice in the shadows.",sp=0},{t="The Line in the Dark",b="Surrounded by walking dead from the western graveyards and feral worgen hunting through the woods, Darkshire clings to life along its palisades. The town's primary shield is the Night Watch, a voluntary civilian militia commanded by Althea Ebonlocke. Operating out of the town square and patrolling the pitch-black thoroughfares, these weary sentries keep the town's roads open and turn back the terrors prowling the tree line. Travelers arriving at the Scarlet Raven Tavern find the locals suspicious, frightened, and desperate for any mercenary capable of holding a blade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was the town renamed from Grand Hamlet?",a="The settlement was originally named Grand Hamlet when the region was still the sunny forest of Brightwood. After the Guardian Medivh died at nearby Karazhan, dark magic crept across the woods, blocking the sunlight and raising the dead. As Brightwood decayed into Duskwood, the bleak reality of their cursed surroundings prompted the residents to rename the village Darkshire.",al={"why is it called darkshire","grand hamlet name change","darkshire history"}},{q="Why isn't Stormwind helping defend Darkshire?",a="Stormwind is paralyzed by domestic political gridlock following the disappearance of King Varian Wrynn. Under the guidance of royal court advisors like Lady Katrana Prestor, the crown has focused its remaining resources narrowly around Elwynn and Redridge, leaving outlying settlements like Darkshire to fend entirely for themselves without soldiers or supplies.",al={"where is the stormwind army","why no guards in duskwood","why did stormwind abandon darkshire"}},{q="Who leads Darkshire?",a="Civic authority rests with Lord Ello Ebonlocke and the Council of Darkshire, operating out of the town hall alongside town clerk Daltry. Martial defense is led by Ello's daughter, Commander Althea Ebonlocke, who commands the volunteer militia known as the Night Watch.",al={"who is in charge of darkshire","darkshire leadership","mayor of darkshire"}},{q="What is the Night Watch?",a="The Night Watch is a local civilian militia formed out of necessity by Althea Ebonlocke. Because the Stormwind Army will not deploy troops to Duskwood, local townsfolk took up arms to patrol the gloomy roads, secure the borders, and push back ghoul incursions and rogue beasts.",al={"what is the nightwatch","darkshire guards","who protects darkshire"}},{q="Who was Morgan Ladimore?",a="Morgan Ladimore was a returning veteran of the Third War who arrived in Darkshire only to discover his homestead ruined and his family gone. After a local priest suggested looking among the tombstones at Raven Hill Cemetery, grief and tragedy drove Ladimore to his death, leaving a dark legacy that still haunts the region.",al={"morla dime lore","ladimore darkshire","who is the ladimore guy"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire is a stark reminder of the kingdom's fracturing frontier. Alliance heroes will find grateful townsfolk, but also palpable bitterness toward the unresponsive nobility back in Stormwind City.",["class:Paladin"]="With the dead rising in every surrounding cemetery and the Light all but forgotten by frightened locals, holy warriors find no shortage of unholy blights to purge around the village perimeter."},kw={"brightwood","darkshire","duskwood","ebonlocke","grand hamlet","night watch","scarlet raven"},rel={"zone:duskwood","npc:althea-ebonlocke","npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","topic:night-watch","subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern","zone:stormwind","quest:56","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery"},src={"Darkshire"}}
E["subzone:darkshire-town-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkshire Town Hall",z="duskwood",s="Darkshire Town Hall stands on the western edge of the town square as the seat of local governance in Duskwood. From inside these dimly lit halls, Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke and his council attempt to administer a settlement besieged by creeping darkness and undead monstrosities.",h="Darkshire Town Hall stands on the western edge of the town square as the seat of local governance in Duskwood.",sec={{t="The Seat of Darkshire",b="Located directly west of the main town square, the Town Hall is where Darkshire's civic leadership gathers to govern an increasingly isolated territory. Within its weathered walls sits Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke, struggling to preserve civil order and protect the populace while Stormwind offers little in the way of military aid. Alongside the mayor, municipal officials like Clerk Daltry work to track local records and the travelers braving Duskwood's dangerous roads, though keeping ledgers current is a grim and challenging task in such perilous times.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who leads the town from this building?",a="Lord Ello Ebonlocke serves as the Mayor of Darkshire and presides over the town council from inside the Town Hall. He directs local defenses and appeals to visiting adventurers for help, as the town receives virtually no reinforcements from the kingdom's capital.",al={"who is the mayor","who runs darkshire","who is in the town hall"}},{q="What records are kept inside the Town Hall?",a="Clerk Daltry maintains town registries documenting the residents and the travelers passing through Darkshire. Due to the chaos and frequent dangers plaguing Duskwood, many of his logs and records have fallen somewhat out of date.",al={"clerk daltry records","what does daltry do","town registry"}},{q="Why is the Town Hall so important to Duskwood's survival?",a="With Duskwood cut off from direct military support from Stormwind, the Town Hall functions as the operational hub for the Night Watch and local authorities. It is where the council coordinates civilian defense and dispatches aid across the shadowy region.",al={"why does the town hall matter","darkshire council role"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, the Town Hall represents the fragile authority of the kingdom's southern frontiers, showing how thin Stormwind's protection stretches in isolated settlements."},kw={"clerk daltry","council","darkshire","duskwood","ello ebonlocke","town hall"},rel={"subzone:darkshire","npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","npc:clerk-daltry","quest:1041","zone:duskwood"},src={"Darkshire Town Hall"}}
E["subzone:dawning-wood-catacombs"] = {t="subzone",n="Dawning Wood Catacombs",z="duskwood",s="Carved deep beneath Raven Hill Cemetery, the Dawning Wood Catacombs are a dark labyrinth teeming with the fiercest undead in Duskwood. Those who brave the subterranean tunnels face entrenched swarms of skeletal guardians and flesh-eating ghouls.",h="Carved deep beneath Raven Hill Cemetery, the Dawning Wood Catacombs are a dark labyrinth teeming with the...",sec={{t="Beneath Raven Hill",b="Long before the twilight curse settled over the forest, the Dawning Wood Catacombs served as a grand resting place for the honored dead of Grand Hamlets and the surrounding homesteads. Now buried beneath the ruined Raven Hill Cemetery, these dark stone corridors hold the most lethal undead in the region. The catacombs feature two distinct subterranean wings: the western passages are held by ranks of animated skeletons guarding ancestral tombs, while the eastern passages descend into a foul warren overrun by ravenous, disease-bearing ghouls. Lone travelers rarely survive deep within their depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Dawning Wood Catacombs located?",a="The catacombs lie directly beneath Raven Hill Cemetery, on the far western edge of Duskwood. Entrances descend from the surface among the sprawling grave markers and ruined crypts.",al={"catacombs location","where is dawning wood catacombs","how to get to catacombs"}},{q="What lurks inside the catacombs?",a="The catacombs harbor the most concentrated and ferocious undead in Duskwood. The western wing is defended by heavily armed skeletal warriors, while the eastern tunnels are infested with savage, plague-ridden ghouls.",al={"catacombs enemies","what is in dawning wood catacombs","catacomb monsters"}},{q="Why were the catacombs built in the first place?",a="Back when the region was still the verdant Brightwood, the catacombs were excavated as a grand burial vault for local families and luminaries. The dark curse that later engulfed the woods reanimated those entombed within.",al={"catacombs history","why build catacombs","original purpose of catacombs"}},{q="Is it safe to explore the catacombs alone?",a="Venturing into the catacombs alone is perilous. The claustrophobic tunnels offer little room to retreat, and the undead pack tightly together in aggressive swarms capable of overwhelming isolated travelers.",al={"can i solo catacombs","catacombs danger","is catacombs hard"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The catacombs are a grim testament to the fallen of the kingdom, demanding that the holy wrath of the Light cleanse the desecrated tombs.",["class:Priest"]="Beneath the stone vaults of Raven Hill, restless spirits and decaying corpses cry out for final rest, making the catacombs a somber trial of faith."},kw={"crypts","dawning wood catacombs","duskwood","ghouls","raven hill cemetery","skeletons","undead"},rel={"subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","zone:duskwood","quest:163","topic:light","topic:alliance"},src={"Dawning Wood Catacombs"}}
E["subzone:forlorn-rowe"] = {t="subzone",n="Forlorn Rowe",z="duskwood",s="The Forlorn Rowe is an ominous, shadowy hill perched on the northern boundary of the Raven Hill Cemetery in Duskwood. It is infamous as the dark abode of Morbent Fel, a necromancer whose malevolent magic animates the restless dead throughout the forest.",h="The Forlorn Rowe is an ominous, shadowy hill perched on the northern boundary of the Raven Hill Cemetery in...",sec={{t="A Seat of Necromancy",b="Rising along the northern edge of the Raven Hill Cemetery, the Forlorn Rowe is perpetually cloaked in gloom. Atop this rise sits the home of Morbent Fel, the lich-like necromancer responsible for much of the walking dead haunting the surrounding wilderness. Bound by foul arcane enchantments, the master of the hill directs his skeletal servants from this vantage, rendering the entire northwestern corner of Duskwood perilous for travelers.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Hill",b="Morbent Fel's grasp on the Forlorn Rowe cannot be broken by ordinary steel alone. His dark enchantments protect his physical form from mortal weapons until he is weakened by specialized relics of holy power. Bringing down the necromancer and breaking his hold over the woods requires adventurers to secure consecrated armaments, striking at the heart of the curse smothering the cemetery grounds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Forlorn Rowe located?",a="The Forlorn Rowe is situated in northwestern Duskwood, resting directly on the northern ridge overlooking the sprawling Raven Hill Cemetery.",al={"forlorn rowe location","where is forlorn rowe","find forlorn rowe"}},{q="Who lives at the Forlorn Rowe?",a="It is the lair of Morbent Fel, a powerful and malevolent necromancer who uses dark arcane rites to raise and command the legions of undead wandering Duskwood.",al={"who is at forlorn rowe","forlorn rowe boss","house on the hill duskwood"}},{q="Why is Morbent Fel so hard to fight here?",a="Morbent Fel shields himself with foul sorcery, rendering mundane attacks almost useless until he is stripped of his dark protections by a consecrated relic crafted to dispel his magic.",al={"morbent fel shield","morbent fel immune","how to kill morbent fel"},sp=1},{q="Is the Forlorn Rowe part of the cemetery?",a="Yes, it stands as an elevated bluff along the northern boundary of the Raven Hill Cemetery, directly overlooking the graves and crypts below.",al={"is forlorn rowe raven hill","raven hill connection"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The dark rites woven at the Forlorn Rowe represent an affront to the Holy Light, requiring consecrated relics and righteous wrath to pierce the necromancer's wards.",["faction:Alliance"]="Rooting out Morbent Fel from the Forlorn Rowe is critical for restoring a semblance of safety to Duskwood's western border."},kw={"cemetery","duskwood","forlorn rowe","morbent fel","necromancer","raven hill","undead"},rel={"quest:55","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","zone:duskwood","quest:163","topic:light","topic:alliance"},src={"Forlorn Rowe"}}
E["subzone:hushed-bank"] = {t="subzone",n="Hushed Bank",z="duskwood",s="The Hushed Bank is the shadowy western shoreline of Duskwood, bordering the river that divides the forest from Westfall. Stretching from the junction near the Three Corners south toward Stranglethorn Vale, it is a quiet yet hazardous woodland stalked by prowling beasts and shadowed by dark mysteries.",h="The Hushed Bank is the shadowy western shoreline of Duskwood, bordering the river that divides the forest...",sec={{t="A Frontier Along the River",b="Running along the river boundary between Duskwood and Westfall, the Hushed Bank marks the transition from open plains and sunlit farms to pervasive, unnatural twilight. The wooden covered bridge crosses the river here, offering passage to travelers heading west out of the grim wood. Thick underbrush and creeping fog dominate the riverbanks, where large spiders and hungry forest wolves stalk unwary wayfarers who stray from the beaten path.",sp=0},{t="Outcasts and Hermits",b="Near the northern reaches of the bank, solitary souls have carved out meager existences away from the suspicious eyes of Darkshire. Sven Yorgen and his companion Lars keep camp in these dense woods, watching the treeline and harboring bitter grievances tied to the dark tragedies that plagued the region. Their isolated refuge remains one of the few signs of living humanoid presence on this lonely shore.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Hushed Bank located?",a="The Hushed Bank forms the western edge of Duskwood along the river that separates the forest from Westfall. It extends from the fork near Three Corners in the north down toward the southern borders leading toward Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"hushed bank location","where is hushed bank","hushed bank map"}},{q="What connects the Hushed Bank to Westfall?",a="A wooden covered bridge spans the river at the Hushed Bank, allowing foot and cart traffic to cross safely between the sunny plains of Westfall and the cursed gloom of Duskwood.",al={"bridge to westfall","westfall bridge duskwood","how to cross river to westfall"}},{q="Who lives along the Hushed Bank?",a="Sven Yorgen and his associate Lars have established an encampment in the northern corner of the bank. Both live as isolated recluses, having fled the horrors that claimed Sven's nearby farm.",al={"camp on hushed bank","who is at hushed bank","npcs hushed bank"}},{q="What threats are found along this shoreline?",a="The Hushed Bank is home to vicious woodland beasts, including overgrown webwood spiders and predatory dusking wolves that prey upon anything moving through the brush.",al={"hushed bank mobs","dangers of hushed bank","hushed bank monsters"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The wolves and spiders haunting the dense foliage along the riverbank offer classic wilderness beasts for trackers charting the darker reaches of the forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="The covered bridge along the bank serves as a critical strategic passage connecting the farmlands of Westfall to the besieged outpost of Duskwood."},kw={"covered bridge","duskwood","hushed bank","lars","riverbank","sven yorgen","westfall"},rel={"zone:duskwood","zone:westfall","npc:sven-yorgen","npc:lars","subzone:three-corners","zone:elwynn","zone:stranglethorn"},src={"Hushed Bank"}}
E["subzone:manor-mistmantle"] = {t="subzone",n="Manor Mistmantle",z="duskwood",s="Manor Mistmantle is a decaying estate nestled in the shadowed hills of northeastern Duskwood, north of Darkshire. Once a proper family homestead, it has fallen into ruin and horror, crawling with undead ghouls bound to its infamous master.",h="Manor Mistmantle is a decaying estate nestled in the shadowed hills of northeastern Duskwood, north of...",sec={{t="A Blighted Homestead",b="Located west of Beggar's Haunt, Manor Mistmantle stands as a grim monument to murder and madness. The grounds are choked with decay and prowled by vicious ghouls who defend the ruined structure. Amidst the rot and withered vegetation, the only sign of living beauty on the entire property is a solitary, sorrowful blossom growing in the untended garden: the flower known as the Tear of Tilloa.",sp=0},{t="The Master of the Estate",b="The manor belongs to Stalvan Mistmantle, a former schoolteacher and private tutor whose horrific crimes in Moonbrook and Goldshire became the stuff of dark legend across the kingdom. Now an agent of the undead, Stalvan lurks in the upper floor of his family home, surrounded by remnants of his slaughtered victims and guarded by shambling horrors. Travelers and investigators from Darkshire frequently find that the trail of Duskwood's most notorious phantom ends at this blood-soaked manor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Manor Mistmantle located?",a="Manor Mistmantle lies in the northeastern reaches of Duskwood, situated directly north of Darkshire and just west of Beggar's Haunt.",al={"manor mistmantle location","where is mistmantle manor","how to find manor mistmantle"}},{q="Who lives in Manor Mistmantle?",a="The estate belongs to Stalvan Mistmantle, a former tutor who went mad, butchered his employers, and now exists as a vengeful undead creature surrounded by ghouls.",al={"who is in mistmantle manor","manor mistmantle boss","stalvan house"},sp=1},{q="What is the Tear of Tilloa?",a="The Tear of Tilloa is a solitary, delicate flower blooming in the garden of Manor Mistmantle, standing out as the only surviving sign of natural life amidst the decayed grounds.",al={"tear of tilloa flower","mistmantle garden flower","tilloa flower"}},{q="Why are there undead guarding the grounds?",a="The ghouls roaming the manor grounds are minions bound to Stalvan Mistmantle, serving to protect their master and slaughter anyone who dares trespass on his blighted estate.",al={"why are ghouls at mistmantle","mistmantle undead","manor mistmantle enemies"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance investigators tracking the grim fate of the Moonbrook and Goldshire victims, Manor Mistmantle is the tragic final destination of the Legend of Stalvan."},kw={"beggar's haunt","darkshire","duskwood","ghouls","manor mistmantle","stalvan","stalvan mistmantle","tear of tilloa"},rel={"zone:duskwood","subzone:darkshire","subzone:beggar-s-haunt","quest:938"},src={"Manor Mistmantle"}}
E["subzone:raven-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Raven Hill",z="duskwood",s="Raven Hill is a desolate, ruined village in western Duskwood sitting in the long shadow of the vast Raven Hill Cemetery. Once a lively human settlement, it lies abandoned by all but a handful of frightened squatters and invisible spirits.",h="Raven Hill is a desolate, ruined village in western Duskwood sitting in the long shadow of the vast Raven...",sec={{t="A Town Lost to Darkness",b="Situated along the western thoroughfare of Duskwood just north of Addle's Stead, Raven Hill is a tragic shell of its former self. When dark magic and undead horrors swept through the Grand Hamlet region, the living evacuated eastward toward Darkshire or fled the territory entirely. Today, ruined timber homes rot beneath perpetual gloom, avoided by travelers who fear both the restless dead wandering down from the neighboring cemetery and the invisible Unseen lurking between the crumbling walls.",sp=0},{t="The Few Who Remain",b="Despite its bleak reputation, Raven Hill is not entirely uninhabited. A nervous wreck of an adventurer named Jitters hides among the abandoned structures, terrified of the horrors his own past curiosity helped unleash. Higher up in one of the dilapidated attics, an entrepreneurial goblin named Bliztik ekes out a solitary living selling supplies to wary passersby. They share the ruins with invisible spirits known as the Unseen, living on borrowed time at the edge of the sprawling burial grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Raven Hill abandoned?",a="Raven Hill was abandoned when the shadow fell over Duskwood, bringing forth undead horrors, dark magic, and predatory beasts. The town's proximity to the massive Raven Hill Cemetery made it especially indefensible, forcing surviving residents to flee eastward toward the fortified settlement of Darkshire.",al={"what happened to raven hill","why is raven hill ruined","who lived in raven hill"}},{q="Who actually lives in the village now?",a="Only a few daring or desperate souls dwell here. The terrified human Jitters hides among the ruined foundations, plagued by guilt and fear, while a goblin vendor named Bliztik operates out of an upper floor, trading with anyone brave enough to search the abandoned buildings.",al={"who is in raven hill","raven hill npcs","living people raven hill"}},{q="What are the Unseen haunting Raven Hill?",a="The Unseen are invisible, hostile spirits that wander through Raven Hill and the nearby cemetery. While invisible to ordinary sight, their presence poses a sudden and deadly threat to any unwary traveler exploring the desolate township.",al={"unseen raven hill","invisible monsters raven hill","ghosts in raven hill"}},{q="Where does the road through Raven Hill lead?",a="The road running past Raven Hill connects westward toward the river bridge into Westfall, southward toward Addle's Stead and the border of Stranglethorn Vale, and eastward through the heart of Duskwood to Darkshire.",al={"raven hill road","where does road go","travel raven hill"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers crossing the bridge from Westfall, Raven Hill serves as an ominous welcome to the nightmare overtaking western Duskwood.",["race:Human"]="The decaying cottages stand as a grim reminder of how much territory the kingdom of Stormwind has lost to creeping darkness and neglect."},kw={"abandoned town","bliztik","cemetery","duskwood","jitters","raven hill","unseen"},rel={"subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","npc:jitters","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","subzone:addle-s-stead","zone:westfall","topic:goblin","quest:163"},src={"Raven Hill"}}
E["subzone:raven-hill-cemetery"] = {t="subzone",n="Raven Hill Cemetery",z="duskwood",s="Raven Hill Cemetery is a vast, cursed graveyard stretching across the western reaches of Duskwood. Once a peaceful burial ground for local hamlets, the cemetery has been overrun by hordes of walking dead, scavenger spiders, and ruthless grave robbers.",h="Raven Hill Cemetery is a vast, cursed graveyard stretching across the western reaches of Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Garden of the Restless Dead",b="Before the darkness engulfed the Dawning Wood, Raven Hill Cemetery served as the primary resting place for the surrounding settlements. As dark sorceries fell upon the region, the dead failed to remain in their plots. Skeletons, ghouls, and shambling horrors clawed their way out of the soil, swelling the graveyard's grim boundaries. Today, it stands as one of the most perilous blights in Duskwood. The cemetery is prowled not only by rotting abominations and giant spiders, but also by desperate grave robbers eager to plunder ancestral crypts unhindered by local authorities.",sp=0},{t="Restless Spirits and Dark Powers",b="The cemetery's tragedy is personified by Mor'Ladim, the mindless skeletal horror of the fallen knight Morgan Ladimore, who endlessly patrols the headstones after taking his own life amidst madness and sorrow. Further north on the rises of Forlorn Rowe, the dark necromancer Morbent Fel harnesses the foul energy of the graves to raise and bind legions of undead. Farther toward the northeast edge sits the secluded shack of Abercrombie the hermit, watching the graveyard from the edge of the mist.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are so many undead rising in Raven Hill Cemetery?",a="The cemetery fell under dark corruption when Duskwood was blighted, allowing necromantic powers to seep into the earth. The foul mage Morbent Fel, lurking in Forlorn Rowe on the graveyard's edge, actively twists these energies to raise and control corpses from their graves.",al={"why are there zombies","why is raven hill haunted","who raised the dead in raven hill"}},{q="Who is Mor'Ladim?",a="Mor'Ladim is the skeletal revenant of Morgan Ladimore, a knight who returned from the Third War only to find his family dead. Driven into madness by grief, he took his own life after a violent outburst in the graveyard. He now stalks the headstones, blindly slaughtering anyone he encounters.",al={"morladim","skeleton wandering the graveyard","morgan ladimore"},sp=1},{q="Where is Morbent Fel located in the cemetery?",a="Morbent Fel resides atop the hill known as Forlorn Rowe, situated in the northwestern corner of Raven Hill Cemetery. He inhabits a decrepit house overlooking the tombstones, directing the undead around him.",al={"morbent fel location","where is morbent fel","forlorn rowe"}},{q="Who is the hermit living on the edge of the cemetery?",a="The hermit is Abercrombie, an eccentric and frail old man living in a ramshackle hut near the northeastern borders of the cemetery. He frequently petitions passing travelers to gather strange components and ingredients for his morbid personal projects.",al={"hermit at raven hill","abercrombie","shack in raven hill"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The relentless corruption and despoiled graves of Raven Hill Cemetery call for holy consecration.",["class:Priest"]="The cemetery harbors powerful conduits of shadow and residual sorrow, serving as a bleak lesson in the tragedy of spirits denied passage to the Light."},kw={"abercrombie","duskwood","forlorn rowe","grave robbers","mor'ladim","morbent fel","raven hill cemetery","skeletons"},rel={"zone:duskwood","topic:mor-ladim","subzone:forlorn-rowe","quest:55","npc:abercrombie","subzone:darkshire","quest:163","topic:light"},src={"Raven Hill Cemetery"}}
E["subzone:roland-s-doom"] = {t="subzone",n="Roland's Doom",z="duskwood",s="Roland's Doom is an abandoned, shadow-drenched mine tucked into the southeastern hills of Duskwood, just east of the Rotting Orchard. Once an ordinary delve, it has become infamous as a dangerous den overrun by savage worgen.",h="Roland's Doom is an abandoned, shadow-drenched mine tucked into the southeastern hills of Duskwood, just east...",sec={{t="A Den of Shadows and Savagery",b="Cut into the ridges east of the Rotting Orchard, Roland's Doom long ago ceased to be a functioning mine. Instead, it serves as a violent staging ground for the Nightbane worgen pack, led by beasts such as Gutspill and Nefaru. The dark tunnels echo with guttural snarls and the reek of damp earth and blood, making it one of the most perilous corners in all of Duskwood for unwary travelers.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Velinde Starsong",b="The true tragedy of Roland's Doom lies buried deep within its tunnels. It was here that the night elven priestess Velinde Starsong met her end while carrying the Scythe of Elune, an ancient artifact of immense and volatile power. Later, the terrified wanderer Jitters stumbled upon the scythe inside the delve, accidentally unleashing an escalation of savage worgen and drawing the deadly Dark Riders to Duskwood. Disturbed dirt within the mine can still stir the lingering spirit of Velinde to speak of her final moments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Roland's Doom?",a="Roland's Doom is a ruined, abandoned mine located in southeastern Duskwood, east of the Rotting Orchard. It is currently overrun by vicious Nightbane worgen.",al={"where is rolands doom","what is this mine"}},{q="Why are there worgen inside the mine?",a="The mine became infested with worgen following the loss of the Scythe of Elune. Currently, powerful beasts of the Nightbane pack, including Nefaru and Gutspill, make their lair within its damp shafts.",al={"why worgen here","who lives in rolands doom"},sp=1},{q="Who was Velinde Starsong and why is she connected to this place?",a="Velinde Starsong was a night elven priestess of Elune who wielded the Scythe of Elune to fight the demons of Felwood. Her journey brought her across the sea to Duskwood, where she was killed inside this very mine, leaving the Scythe behind.",al={"velinde starsong rolands doom","who died here"},sp=1},{q="How does Jitters fit into the story of Roland's Doom?",a="Jitters entered Roland's Doom and discovered the buried Scythe of Elune. His meddling unintentionally released more worgen into Duskwood and drew the sinister Dark Riders to the region, plunging the forest into greater peril.",al={"jitters mine","jitters scythe"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The tragic demise of Priestess Velinde Starsong within this mine makes Roland's Doom a site of somber reflection and sorrow for night elves investigating the fate of their kin and the elusive Scythe of Elune.",["profession:Mining"]="Though once a working quarry, any prospector foolish enough to swing a pick here will quickly find that the only veins running in Roland's Doom belong to bloodthirsty worgen."},kw={"gutspill","jitters","nefaru","nightbane","roland's doom","rolands doom","rotting orchard","scythe of elune","velinde starsong"},rel={"quest:1043","quest:1044","quest:1037","topic:worgen","npc:jitters","subzone:rotting-orchard","zone:duskwood","topic:dark-riders"},src={"Roland's Doom"}}
E["subzone:rotting-orchard"] = {t="subzone",n="Rotting Orchard",z="duskwood",s="The Rotting Orchard is a blighted, abandoned fruit grove situated in southern Duskwood. Once a source of harvest for the nearby settlement of Darkshire, it has fallen into ruin and is now overrun by ravenous lupine predators known as the Nightbane pack.",h="The Rotting Orchard is a blighted, abandoned fruit grove situated in southern Duskwood.",sec={{t="Den of the Nightbane",b="Located east of the ruined Yorgen Farmstead and west of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery, the Rotting Orchard stands as a grim testament to Duskwood's decline. The trees hang heavy with withered, spoiled fruit, while dilapidated barns and outbuildings have been converted into rough encampments by the Nightbane worgen. Nightbane Stalkers prowl the twisted brush, while dark casters known as Shadow Weavers weave their sinister magic amid the decaying timber. The pack answers to their fierce leader, Marus, who prowls the surrounding woods keeping watch over their stolen domain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures occupy the Rotting Orchard?",a="The orchard is completely infested by the Nightbane pack, a faction of ravenous worgen. These include cunning prowlers called Nightbane Stalkers, dark spellcasters known as Nightbane Shadow Weavers, and their roaming leader, Marus.",al={"rotting orchard mobs","who lives in rotting orchard","what is at rotting orchard"}},{q="Where is the Rotting Orchard located in Duskwood?",a="The Rotting Orchard lies in southern Duskwood, southwest of the town of Darkshire. It is nestled right between the ruined Yorgen Farmstead to its west and the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery to its east.",al={"rotting orchard location","where is rotting orchard","how to find rotting orchard"}},{q="Who leads the worgen in this orchard?",a="The packleader of the worgen here is named Marus. He prowls the territory between the decaying orchard grounds and his nearby den, aggressively defending the pack's domain.",al={"rotting orchard boss","packleader marus","who leads nightbane"}},{q="Was this place always overrun by monsters?",a="No. Like many surrounding homesteads in Duskwood, it was once a productive farm and fruit grove supporting the local human populace before dark curses and supernatural horrors overtook the region and drove the farmers away.",al={"orchard history","why is orchard rotting"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The encroachment of the Nightbane worgen at the Rotting Orchard poses a direct predatory threat to the fragile security of Darkshire just up the road.",["class:Hunter"]="The twisted trees and ruined outbuildings provide prime stalking ground, but the predatory senses and spellcraft of the Nightbane pack make it an ambush waiting to happen."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","marus","nightbane","rotting orchard","shadow weavers","worgen"},rel={"zone:duskwood","topic:worgen","subzone:darkshire","subzone:yorgen-farmstead","subzone:tranquil-gardens-cemetery","topic:emerald-dream"},src={"Rotting Orchard"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Raven Tavern",z="duskwood",s="The Scarlet Raven Tavern is the social center and primary inn of Darkshire, offering hearthside shelter in the gloom of Duskwood. Presided over by Tavernkeep Smitts, it serves as a gathering spot for beleaguered locals, passing adventurers, and terrified travelers trying to escape the horrors lurking beyond the town's perimeter.",h="The Scarlet Raven Tavern is the social center and primary inn of Darkshire, offering hearthside shelter in...",sec={{t="A Dim Refuge",b="Standing near the heart of Darkshire, the Scarlet Raven Tavern keeps its hearth ablaze while eternal dusk chokes the surrounding forest. Years ago, it was a bustling stop where Marshal Haggard and the Stormwind Guard would share pints after patrols. Today, business has withered alongside the town's security. Tavernkeep Smitts tends bar for a somber, anxious clientele huddled against the cold and fear. Even so, the tavern remains an indispensable crossroads for rumors, serving as the starting point for travelers seeking answers to the dark phenomena consuming the region.",sp=0},{t="Secrets and Stolen Pints",b="Beyond serving as a shelter, the tavern holds pieces of several unfolding mysteries. The reclusive wanderer Jitters rented a room here for days, frantically scribbling in his journal by night before fleeing town ahead of the terrifying Dark Riders. Decades-old town gossip and preserved guest records kept beneath its roof also link back to long-forgotten figures like Stalvan Mistmantle, making Smitts' taproom the first place inquisitive investigators search when tracing the histories of Duskwood's restless dead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who runs the Scarlet Raven Tavern?",a="Tavernkeep Smitts owns and operates the tavern. He handles lodging, sells local fare, and laments the creeping corruption that has driven away customers and plunged Darkshire into gloom.",al={"innkeeper of darkshire","who owns the scarlet raven","tavernkeep smitts"}},{q="Why is the tavern's atmosphere so gloomy?",a="The curse hanging over Duskwood has choked the trade routes and terrified the locals. With undead, feral worgen, and shadowy riders prowling the woods outside, the patron crowd consists of terrified townsfolk and desperate mercenaries rather than carefree travelers.",al={"why is scarlet raven depressing","darkshire inn atmosphere"}},{q="Did Jitters stay at the Scarlet Raven?",a="Yes. Jitters took a room at the inn for several nights, drinking and frantically writing his journal. He fled in terror into the forest when the sinister Dark Riders arrived searching for him.",al={"jitters room","jitters tavern","did jitters live here"}},{q="What connection does this tavern have to the Legend of Stalvan?",a="Old patrons and past town records preserved in and around the tavern hold clues regarding Stalvan Mistmantle, who once frequented the settlement before falling into tragedy and infamy.",al={"stalvan inn connection","stalvan mistmantle darkshire inn"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers traversing the southern border, the Scarlet Raven provides one of the few safe hearths and rest stops between Elwynn Forest and Deadwind Pass.",["profession:Cooking"]="The inn's menu features regional delicacies like Dusky Crab Cakes, a local staple that desperate wanderers like Jitters crave even while hiding in the graveyard."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","dusky crab cakes","haggard","jitters","scarlet raven","smitts","tavernkeep smitts"},rel={"subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","npc:tavernkeep-smitts","npc:jitters","quest:266","quest:93","quest:66","topic:dark-riders"},src={"Scarlet Raven Tavern"}}
E["subzone:tranquil-gardens-cemetery"] = {t="subzone",n="Tranquil Gardens Cemetery",z="duskwood",s="Tranquil Gardens Cemetery sits just southeast of Darkshire in Duskwood. Despite its peaceful name, the grounds have become overrun with shambling skeletons and ghouls, turning the former burial site into an immediate hazard for the nearby town.",h="Tranquil Gardens Cemetery sits just southeast of Darkshire in Duskwood.",sec={{t="Restless Grounds",b="Once a quiet resting place for the departed of Grand Hamlet, Tranquil Gardens Cemetery is now anything but serene. As dark curses settled over Duskwood, the dead buried here began clawing their way out of their plots. While the skeletal warriors, skeletal mages, and wandering undead haunting these gravestones are relatively weak compared to the horrors lurking deeper in the woods, their close proximity to Darkshire poses a relentless threat to the townsfolk.",sp=0},{t="On the Town's Threshold",b="Because the cemetery lies so close to Darkshire's edge, it serves as the frontline for the local militia. The Night Watch frequently sends fresh recruits and arriving adventurers here to cull the rising dead before they breach the settlement. Among the tumbled headstones and the ruined chapel, more dangerous threats such as the Insane Ghoul lurk, while Night Watch patrols like Watcher Eva keep vigil nearby.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Tranquil Gardens if it is full of undead?",a="The cemetery was established back when Duskwood was known as Grand Hamlet, a peaceful region of Stormwind. It was meant to be a quiet, dignified resting place for local families. The moniker turned into a grim irony once the curse fell over the region and the dead began rising from their graves.",al={"why tranquil","tranquil gardens name origin","why is it called tranquil"}},{q="What threats wander around the cemetery?",a="The grounds are infested with relatively weak undead, including shambling skeletons, skeletal warriors, and skeletal mages. A particularly vicious Insane Ghoul can also be found haunting the ruined chapel or roaming the headstones.",al={"enemies in tranquil gardens","what mobs are here","cemetery mobs"}},{q="Why does the Night Watch send recruits here?",a="Because the cemetery sits immediately southeast of Darkshire, any unchecked rise in undead numbers threatens to spill directly into the town. The Night Watch uses the site to blood new defenders against the weaker undead before sending them deeper into the dangerous forest.",al={"night watch cemetery quest","why cull tranquil gardens","who protects the cemetery"}},{q="Who lives just north of the cemetery?",a="Just north of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery sits an isolated cottage inhabited by the spirit known as Blind Mary, who lingers near the blighted graveyard.",al={"house near tranquil gardens","ghost north of cemetery","blind mary house"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The desecration of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery is an affront to the Holy Light, making it an urgent proving ground for paladins seeking to grant peace to Duskwood's restless dead.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions arriving in Darkshire, defending this nearby graveyard is critical to keeping the town's perimeter secure from an undead breach."},kw={"cemetery","darkshire","duskwood","gardens","insane ghoul","skeletons","tranquil","watcher eva"},rel={"subzone:darkshire","topic:night-watch","quest:56","npc:blind-mary","zone:duskwood","topic:light"},src={"Tranquil Gardens Cemetery"}}
E["subzone:twilight-grove"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Grove",z="duskwood",s="Tucked away in the center of Duskwood, the Twilight Grove is a stunning enclave of lush Kalimdor flora contrasting the grim, blighted forest around it. Beneath its towering great tree and ancient night elf architecture sits a moonwell and a massive emerald gateway connected directly to the Emerald Dream.",h="Tucked away in the center of Duskwood, the Twilight Grove is a stunning enclave of lush Kalimdor flora...",sec={{t="A Verdant Sanctuary",b="Hidden behind steep crater ridges in the heart of Duskwood, the Twilight Grove looks utterly alien to the Eastern Kingdoms. Ancient night elf gazebos, vibrant green meadows, and a serene moonwell frame an unnamed great tree that towers over the gloomy canopy. Millennia ago, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm and his circle planted an enchanted bough of Nordrassil here to purge toxic corruption rising from the deep earth. The tree took root as a conduit of nature, filtering the raw vigor of the Emerald Dream into the waking world and allowing this crater to thrive even beneath the eternal gloom of Duskwood.",sp=0},{t="The Emerald Gateway",b="At the base of the great tree looms a massive stone portal, one of four known gateways across Azeroth linking the physical realm directly to the Emerald Dream. While traditionally watched over by Ysera's green dragonflight, dark whispers claim that malevolent forces have begun twisting the tranquil realm beyond. The gateway stands largely silent for now, but its emerald swirl serves as a grim reminder that cosmic corruption can spill forth into Duskwood from paths far deeper than the Scourge or the local worgen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there night elf architecture in Duskwood?",a="Thousands of years ago, druids led by Fandral Staghelm traveled from Kalimdor across the world to contain subterranean blights. They planted an enchanted branch from the World Tree Nordrassil in this crater and tended to it with traditional kaldorei structures and a sacred moonwell.",al={"elf ruins duskwood","why night elf buildings here","moonwell in duskwood"}},{q="What is the giant glowing green portal?",a="It is a Great Tree portal leading directly into the Emerald Dream, the primordial blueprint of Azeroth overseen by the green dragonflight. Three similar portals exist in Ashenvale, Feralas, and the Hinterlands.",al={"green portal duskwood","emerald dream portal duskwood","stone archway in grove"}},{q="Who watches over the grove today?",a="Historically, lieutenants of Ysera's green dragonflight guarded this sanctuary. While often empty to travelers passing through, growing disturbances within the Emerald Dream threaten to bring corrupted guardians through the portal into the mortal world.",al={"who guards twilight grove","green dragons twilight grove"}},{q="Why doesn't the Twilight Grove look dead like the rest of Duskwood?",a="The great tree acts as a conduit to the Emerald Dream, radiating pure, untamed life energy. This constant influx of natural vitality protects the inner basin from the supernatural curse and blight choking the surrounding woods.",al={"why is twilight grove green","why alive in duskwood"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids exploring the Eastern Kingdoms, the grove is a rare oasis of home, housing an active moonwell and a direct link to the ancestral dreamways.",["race:NightElf"]="Finding a secluded moonwell and traditional gazebos so far from Kalimdor is a poignant reminder of your people's ancient duty to heal the wounds of Azeroth."},kw={"duskwood","emerald dream","fandral staghelm","great tree","green dragonflight","moonwell","nordrassil","portal","twilight grove"},rel={"zone:duskwood","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:nordrassil","zone:ashenvale","zone:feralas","zone:hinterlands"},src={"Twilight Grove"}}
E["subzone:vul-gol-ogre-mound"] = {t="subzone",n="Vul'Gol Ogre Mound",z="duskwood",s="Vul'Gol Ogre Mound is a sunken basin in southern Duskwood overrun by the Splinter Fist ogres under the brute Zzarc'Vul. Once a cluster of human homesteads, its ruined farmhouses and subterranean cavern are now littered with the carcasses and scavenged plunder of the clan.",h="Vul'Gol Ogre Mound is a sunken basin in southern Duskwood overrun by the Splinter Fist ogres under the brute...",sec={{t="A Blighted Homestead",b="Tucked away in the shadows southwest of the fork heading toward Stranglethorn Vale, the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound serves as the seat of the Splinter Fist clan in Duskwood. The basin was once peaceful farmland, but its human inhabitants have long since fled or perished, leaving behind hollowed-out cabins now claimed by lumbering ogres and used as crude shelters. Inside the cavern beneath the rise, piles of slaughtered black bears attest to the clan's voracious appetite. Their chieftain, Zzarc'Vul, rules over the encampment, hoarding odd trinkets alongside mundane scavenged goods.",sp=0},{t="A Menace on the Southern Border",b="Because the beleaguered Night Watch must stretch its thin ranks to guard Darkshire against rabid worgen and the restless dead, Commander Althea Ebonlocke and her militia rely on outside mercenaries to cull the Splinter Fist numbers before they push north. However, the ogres have made enemies beyond the town guard. They raided the recluse Abercrombie, stealing a crate of his alchemical tools, and attracted the attention of inquisitive mages seeking the arcane lenses that chieftain Zzarc'Vul is rumored to possess.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound?",a="The mound is occupied by the Splinter Fist clan of ogres, led by the hulking chieftain Zzarc'Vul. They dwell among ruined human cottages and deep within an earthen cavern.",al={"who is at vul'gol","vul'gol enemies","ogres in duskwood"}},{q="Why hasn't the Night Watch cleared out the ogres?",a="The Night Watch lacks the manpower to march in force on the southern basin. With Darkshire threatened on all sides by undead, worgen, and the horrors of Addle's Stead, the militia hires travelling adventurers to cull the Splinter Fist instead of risking town guards.",al={"night watch ogres","why doesn't darkshire attack vul'gol"}},{q="Who lived here before the ogres?",a="Human homesteaders once farmed the fertile pocket in southern Duskwood, back when the region was still known as Brightwood. When the curse fell upon the land, the farms fell to ruin, and the invading ogres claimed the abandoned structures.",al={"ruined buildings vul'gol","vul'gol history"}},{q="Why did the hermit Abercrombie send me here?",a="The Splinter Fist ogres ambushed the hermit Abercrombie and made off with a crate containing his herbs and embalming tools. Unable to fight them himself, Abercrombie directs travelers into the mound to recover his stolen goods.",al={"abercrombie ogres","abercrombie crate"}},{q="Where is the mound located?",a="Vul'Gol lies in the far south of Duskwood, just southwest of the road junction that splits off and leads south toward the border of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"vul'gol location","how to get to vul'gol"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers traversing the southern path toward Stranglethorn Vale, keeping the Splinter Fist contained at Vul'Gol is vital to maintaining an open supply route through an already treacherous forest.",["race:Human"]="The smashed remnants of farmsteads in the basin are a bitter reminder of how much territory the kingdom of Stormwind has lost in Duskwood over the past generation."},kw={"abercrombie","duskwood","night watch","ogres","splinter fist","vul'gol","zzarc'vul"},rel={"zone:duskwood","topic:night-watch","npc:abercrombie","quest:134","npc:viktori-prism-antras","zone:stranglethorn","topic:alliance"},src={"Vul'Gol Ogre Mound"}}
E["subzone:yorgen-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Yorgen Farmstead",z="duskwood",s="The Yorgen Farmstead is a derelict farm nestled in southern Duskwood, fallen into ruin alongside the rest of the troubled region. Formerly owned by the farmer Sven Yorgen, the property has been seized and occupied by brigands of the Defias Brotherhood.",h="The Yorgen Farmstead is a derelict farm nestled in southern Duskwood, fallen into ruin alongside the rest of...",sec={{t="A Ruined Homestead",b="Situated amidst the gloomy woodlands of southern Duskwood, the Yorgen Farmstead was once a functioning homestead belonging to Sven Yorgen. Like many isolated holdings in the region, the farm could not withstand the encroaching perils of the territory. Sven was forced to abandon his lands, retreating north to a makeshift camp along the Darkened Bank. In his absence, the abandoned grounds were claimed by outlaws looking for a foothold far from the gaze of Stormwind's authorities.",sp=0},{t="Defias Infiltration",b="Rather than lying vacant, the farmstead has been repurposed as a staging ground by the Defias Brotherhood. Masked highwaymen and stealthy cutthroats lurk among the decaying fences and weathered outbuildings, using the dense tree cover to conceal their presence. Travelers approaching the farmstead must tread carefully, as Defias assassins patrol the perimeter and ambush anyone trespassing on their newly seized sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns the Yorgen Farmstead?",a="The farmstead was originally established and farmed by Sven Yorgen. After tragedy struck his home and driven away by rising dangers, Sven fled to a solitary camp located further north on the Darkened Bank.",al={"who lived here","who owns yorgen farm","sven yorgen farm"}},{q="Who occupies the farmstead now?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has seized the deserted property. Cutpurses, bandits, and stealthed assassins prowl the overgrown yards and barnyards, making the farmstead extremely dangerous to visit.",al={"who is at yorgen farmstead","what enemies are here","who lives here now"}},{q="Where did Sven Yorgen go?",a="Sven abandoned the farm and can now be found residing in a modest camp along the Darkened Bank, situated to the north along the river separating Duskwood and Elwynn Forest.",al={"where is sven","sven yorgen location","find sven yorgen"}},{q="Why is the Defias Brotherhood in Duskwood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has expanded its operations far beyond Westfall. Disorganized rural settlements and weakened regional defenses allow their agents to set up secret camps and strongholds out of reach of Stormwind's marshals.",al={"defias in duskwood","why are bandits here","defias brotherhood farm"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The hidden Defias assassins stalking the farmstead make the area treacherous, demonstrating how readily rogue operatives turn neglected wilderness holdings into camouflaged hideouts.",["faction:Alliance"]="The loss of Sven's farmstead to the Defias Brotherhood highlights how deeply the outlaw syndicates have penetrated Duskwood while the Night Watch struggles to maintain order in Darkshire."},kw={"darkened bank","defias","defias brotherhood","duskwood","farm","sven yorgen","yorgen farmstead"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","zone:duskwood","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:darkened-bank"},src={"Yorgen Farmstead"}}
E["topic:mor-ladim"] = {t="topic",n="Mor'Ladim",z="duskwood",s="Mor'Ladim is a dangerous, vengeful skeletal warrior wandering the grounds of Raven Hill Cemetery in Duskwood. Formerly the noble knight Morgan Ladimore, he succumbed to profound grief and madness upon discovering the loss of his family, rising in undeath to slaughter anyone crossing his path.",h="Mor'Ladim is a dangerous, vengeful skeletal warrior wandering the grounds of Raven Hill Cemetery in Duskwood.",sec={{t="A Knight of the Silver Hand",b="Before he became the terror of Raven Hill, Mor'Ladim lived as Morgan Ladimore, a devoted knight and defender of the helpless from Grand Hamlet—the town now known as Darkshire. Married at eighteen to his wife Lys, he raised three children in peace until war summoned him north. Morgan marched alongside Uther the Lightbringer to Lordaeron during the Third War, witnessing the downfall of the Knights of the Silver Hand, the spread of Kel'Thuzad's plague, and the tragic death of Uther himself.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Morgan Ladimore",b="Returning home after the war, Morgan found Duskwood twisted by darkness and his homestead ruined. Driven toward Raven Hill Cemetery, he searched among the headstones until he discovered the graves of Lys and two of their children. Overcome by grief and fury, Morgan lashed out, striking at the gravestones. When graveyard attendants attempted to calm him, the knight slaughtered them in a blind frenzy. Horrified by his heinous act once clarity returned, Morgan drove his own blade into his heart. Ashamed, the townsfolk buried his corpse in an unmarked, remote corner of the cemetery.",sp=1},{t="The Scourge of Raven Hill",b="Burial brought Morgan no peace. Bound by the heavy guilt of innocent blood and suffocating grief, his corrupted remains rose from the dirt as a hulking skeletal revenant. Calling him Mor'Ladim, travelers and members of the Night Watch quickly learned to dread his name. Armed with his ancestral blade Archeus, the mindless apparition patrols the mist-choked graves, cutting down both beasts and unwary adventurers who venture too close to his resting place.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Mor'Ladim in life?",a="Mor'Ladim was originally Morgan Ladimore, an honorable paladin and knight from Grand Hamlet who fought alongside Uther the Lightbringer during the Third War in Lordaeron.",al={"who is morladim","morladim backstory","morgan ladimore lore","who was morladim"},sp=1},{q="Why is Mor'Ladim hostile?",a="Morgan went mad with grief upon discovering the graves of his family. After slaughtering innocent cemetery attendants and taking his own life, his soul became trapped by guilt and anguish, reanimating his body as a murderous undead fiend.",al={"why does morladim attack","why is he angry","morladim madness"},sp=1},{q="Where does Mor'Ladim roam?",a="He patrols the sprawling paths and mausoleums of Raven Hill Cemetery in western Duskwood, frequently catching travelers unaware due to his sweeping patrol route.",al={"morladim path","where to find morladim","morladim location"}},{q="Did all of Morgan Ladimore's family die?",a="No. While his wife Lys and two of his children perished, a third child survived Duskwood's decline—a detail Morgan missed entirely in his blind despair at the graveyard.",al={"did morgan ladimore family survive","morgan ladimore daughter","who survived in ladimore family"},sp=1},{q="What is the weapon Mor'Ladim carries?",a="Mor'Ladim wields Archeus, a fine blade that served him faithfully as a knight throughout his lifetime before becoming an instrument of slaughter in undeath.",al={"morladim sword","archeus sword","what sword does morladim use"},sp=1},{q="Who wants Mor'Ladim destroyed?",a="Commander Althea Ebonlocke and the Night Watch of Darkshire actively seek his destruction to protect patrols and travelers from his relentless ambushes in western Duskwood.",al={"who wants morladim dead","night watch morladim","althea ebonlocke morladim"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Morgan Ladimore was once an honorable warrior of the Light who fought alongside Uther the Lightbringer. His fall illustrates the dreadful danger of allowing sorrow and wrath to eclipse sacred vows.",["faction:Alliance"]="The tragic ruin of Morgan Ladimore serves as a grim reminder of how deeply the Third War shattered southern kingdoms like Stormwind, leaving veteran soldiers to return to ruined families."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","archeus","duskwood","grand hamlet","lys ladimore","mor'ladim","morgan ladimore","raven hill"},rel={"subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","zone:duskwood","subzone:darkshire","npc:althea-ebonlocke","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:third-war","topic:lordaeron","topic:light"},src={"Mor'Ladim"}}
E["topic:night-watch"] = {t="topic",n="Night Watch",z="duskwood",s="The Night Watch is the beleaguered town militia responsible for defending Darkshire and the shadowy roads of Duskwood. Abandoned by the House of Nobles in Stormwind, these local volunteers stand alone against roaming undead, feral worgen, and lurking necromancy. Led by Commander Althea Ebonlocke, they rely heavily on visiting adventurers to keep darkness from overtaking their home.",h="The Night Watch is the beleaguered town militia responsible for defending Darkshire and the shadowy roads of...",sec={{t="Abandoned by the Crown",b="When foul magic overtook the once-vibrant Grand Hamlet and turned the forest into Duskwood, the kingdom of Stormwind turned its back. Following King Varian Wrynn's disappearance, the royal garrison was pulled back to the capital. Stripped of official royal troops and supplies, the townsfolk formed their own volunteer militia—the Night Watch—swearing to hold the borders of Darkshire against the creeping horrors of the woods.",sp=0},{t="A Frontline in the Mist",b="Operating out of their headquarters in Darkshire, the Watchers patrol along roads perpetually choked with unnatural mist. Their adversaries are relentless: ravenous skeletal fiends and ghouls spilling outward from Raven Hill and Tranquil Gardens cemeteries, alongside terrifying feral worgen prowling Roland's Doom and Brightwood Grove. Severely outmatched in numbers and resources, the militia has lost many of its finest defenders to ruthless threats like the wandering abomination Mor'Ladim.",sp=0},{t="The Vigil of Commander Ebonlocke",b="Commander Althea Ebonlocke, daughter of Darkshire's mayor, directs the defensive effort with grim pragmatism. Lacking veteran reinforcements, she enlists any capable traveler arriving at town to thin out skeletal legions, cull starving wolf packs, or investigate mysterious local murders. The Night Watch views itself as the final bulwark preserving human life in the region; if their lines break, Darkshire falls entirely into the shadow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Stormwind not send troops to help the Night Watch?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing, the Stormwind House of Nobles is gripped by political gridlock. Claiming military resources must remain concentrated around the capital and Elwynn Forest, the crown withdrew its garrisons, leaving Duskwood's citizenry entirely to their own devices.",al={"why no stormwind guards","where is stormwind army","why duskwood abandoned"}},{q="Who commands the Night Watch?",a="Commander Althea Ebonlocke leads the militia from the Night Watch office in Darkshire. She is the daughter of Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke and personally organizes road patrols, bounties, and defense strategies across Duskwood.",al={"who leads the night watch","night watch commander","who is in charge of darkshire watch"}},{q="What threats does the Night Watch fight most often?",a="Their most frequent foes are the risen undead pouring out of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery and Raven Hill, feral wolf packs, and the mysterious wolf-beasts known as worgen who stalk Brightwood Grove and Roland's Doom.",al={"duskwood enemies","what do watchers fight","night watch threats"}},{q="Who is Mor'Ladim, and why do the Watchers fear him?",a="Mor'Ladim is a wandering, exceptionally powerful undead terror haunting Raven Hill Cemetery. He cut down several of the Night Watch's strongest patrols, making him one of the deadliest and most feared entities in the zone.",al={"mor'ladim lore","morladim night watch","cemetery boss duskwood"}},{q="Are the Watchers professional soldiers or volunteers?",a="They are local volunteers, farmers, hunters, and townsfolk who took up weapons out of survival. Although trained by local veterans, they lack formal military backing, royal equipment, and regular military wages.",al={"are watchers guards","night watch background","is night watch an army"}},{q="Where is the Night Watch headquarters located?",a="Their headquarters is situated in the heart of Darkshire, where Commander Althea Ebonlocke and her officers plan patrols and receive scouting reports from sentries stationed along the trails.",al={"night watch building","where to find watchers","darkshire watch hall"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the kingdom, the plight of the Night Watch exposes the rot and negligence within Stormwind's noble court, which has left fellow citizens to die in the shadows.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes who visit Darkshire find a frontline community holding the border against nightmarish forces without any official aid from the high command.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins view the Night Watch's desperate vigil as a sacred duty, stepping in with holy magic to shield ordinary townsfolk from rampant necromancy.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors find kindred spirits in the rugged militia members who stand ground against ghouls, giant spiders, and worgen with basic steel and raw grit."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","darkshire","duskwood","militia","mor'ladim","night watch","raven hill","stormwind","worgen"},rel={"subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","npc:althea-ebonlocke","quest:56","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","topic:mor-ladim","topic:worgen","quest:145"},src={"Night Watch"}}
E["zone:duskwood"] = {t="zone",n="Duskwood",z="duskwood",s="Once a sunlit expanse of southern Elwynn known as Brightwood, Duskwood is now a cursed woodland trapped beneath an unnatural, perpetual gloom. Abandoned by the authorities in Stormwind, its besieged human inhabitants cling to survival in Darkshire under the watchful protection of the local Night Watch militia. Across its darkened groves and haunted barrows roam flesh-eating ghouls, gigantic venomous spiders, raiding ogres, and savage, mysterious worgen.",h="Once a sunlit expanse of southern Elwynn known as Brightwood, Duskwood is now a cursed woodland trapped...",sec={{t="From Brightwood to Shadow",b="Before the darkness descended, this province was known as Brightwood, a rich agricultural tract of the Kingdom of Stormwind boasting prosperous settlements like Grand Hamlet and Raven Hill. The region's tragedy began when Guardian Medivh fell at Karazhan during the First War, unleashing waves of corrupted fel magic that twisted the serene woodland into a gnarled, shadowy morass. Spiders mutated into terrifying predatory beasts, while fleeing wolves spilled north into Elwynn Forest. Over time, Grand Hamlet was rechristened Darkshire, its terrified townsfolk left largely to fend for themselves as the realm's royal garrison withdrew to defend the capital.",sp=0},{t="The Scythe and the Wolf-Men",b="The land's modern nightmare deepened with the arrival of a night elf priestess named Velinde Starsong, who carried an otherworldly artifact known as the Scythe of Elune. When she vanished within the disused mine called Roland's Doom, the relic was eventually unearthed by a prospecting laborer named Jitters. The careless handling of the weapon unleashed ravenous, bipedal wolf-beasts known as worgen into the woods. Clad in perpetual mist and bloodlust, these extradimensional predators tore through the western groves, compounding the miseries of a region already groaning under undead curses.",sp=1},{t="A Beleaguered Borderland",b="Today, Darkshire survives only through the vigilance of Commander Althea Ebonlocke and her volunteer militia, the Night Watch, while Lord Ello Ebonlocke attempts to govern the crumbling settlement. Beyond the town's lantern-lit perimeter lies utter peril: the massive Raven Hill Cemetery churns with restless dead raised by the necromancer Morbent Fel, the Vul'Gol ogres have migrated from Deadwind Pass to claim the south, and sinister Dark Riders stalk the crossroads in relentless search of the lost Scythe.",sp=0},{t="The Twilight Grove",b="Near the center of Duskwood lies a deep, ancient crater that defies the surrounding corruption: the Twilight Grove. Long before human kingdoms walked these lands, the archdruid Fandral Staghelm planted a bough from Nordrassil here to contain foul saronite growths. The branch blossomed into a Great Tree hosting a dormant portal into the Emerald Dream. Bathed in a soft, ethereal twilight, the grove remains an unearthly sanctuary in an otherwise dying land, watched over by sleeping druidic energies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Duskwood instead of Brightwood?",a="The land was once Brightwood, a vibrant southern province of Elwynn. When the Guardian Medivh was slain in nearby Karazhan during the First War, volatile fel energies washed over the forest, choking out the sunlight, twisting the flora, and giving rise to the name Duskwood.",al={"why duskwood dark","brightwood history","what happened to brightwood"}},{q="Where did the worgen come from?",a="The night elf Velinde Starsong brought the mystical Scythe of Elune into the region and perished near Roland's Doom. Years later, a frightened worker named Jitters disturbed the scythe in the mine, unwittingly opening tears that summoned the savage wolf-men into the forest.",al={"why are there worgen","worgen origin duskwood","scythe of elune worgen"},sp=1},{q="Why are there so many undead in Raven Hill?",a="Raven Hill Cemetery served as the resting place for countless souls lost to famine, beasts, and war. The vile necromancer Morbent Fel established his lair on Forlorn Rowe, using dark sorcery to animate the graves into ghouls, skeletons, and abominations.",al={"raven hill undead","why ghosts in duskwood","morbent fel undead"}},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind sent soldiers to help Darkshire?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and resources stretched thin, Stormwind's regency has pulled its military back to protect Elwynn and the throne. Darkshire is left entirely to its own devices, defended solely by the volunteer militia known as the Night Watch.",al={"why no stormwind guard","stormwind abandoned darkshire","where is the army"}},{q="Who are the Dark Riders stalking the woods?",a="The Dark Riders are mysterious hooded horsemen originating from Deadwind Pass near Karazhan. Drawn by the release of the Scythe of Elune, they swept into Duskwood, ruthlessly slaughtering Sven Yorgen's family while hunting for the artifact.",al={"black riders deadwind","riders at yorgen farm","who are dark riders"},sp=1},{q="What is the massive tree in the center crater?",a="The crater is the Twilight Grove, home to a Great Tree grown thousands of years ago from a branch of Nordrassil planted by Fandral Staghelm. It contains a portal to the Emerald Dream and maintains a calm, mystical twilight distinct from the cursed dark of the forest.",al={"twilight grove tree","green portal duskwood","crater tree"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Though technically an Alliance holding, Duskwood receives zero official troop support from Stormwind, relying purely on heroic adventurers and the Night Watch to stave off annihilation.",["class:Paladin"]="The desecrated barrows of Raven Hill and the sinister necromancy of Morbent Fel make Duskwood an urgent testing ground for holy crusaders wielding the Light.",["class:Druid"]="The Twilight Grove cradles an ancient Great Tree with deep ties to the Emerald Dream, making Duskwood a focal point for druids investigating the world's slumbering magic.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The haunted barrows and cursed soil yield rare flora like Grave Moss and Kingsblood, drawing gatherers willing to braving restless undead in the cemeteries."},kw={"althea ebonlocke","brightwood","darkshire","duskwood","ello ebonlocke","jitters","morbent fel","night watch","raven hill","scythe of elune","sven yorgen","twilight grove","worgen"},rel={"subzone:darkshire","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","subzone:twilight-grove","topic:night-watch","npc:althea-ebonlocke","npc:jitters","quest:1043","quest:55"},m={levels="18-30"},src={"Duskwood (Classic)","Duskwood"}}
